  },
  CollectionHall_126989_Title = {Text = "Xu"},
  CollectionHall_127110_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The great sword was long and heavy, capable of slicing a person in half with enough force.

The dagger was light and nimble, easy to hide, perfect for a surprise attack.

The curved sword was beautifully arched, the blade sharp, easily embedding itself into flesh and opening a deep gash.

The firearm was quick and domineering, the crossbow silent and swift, various metal parts glinting coldly under the light. Ten-year-old Ramona stood in front of the wall full of weapons, her face showing an unexpected maturity and seriousness for her age.

"Which one do you want?" The voice of her caretaker - no, the father who raised her - came from behind, "Once you choose, I will help you find a teacher."

Which one? The weight of the great sword was both an advantage and a disadvantage; the dagger couldn't handle longer weapons; the curved sword, although long, always inflicted a lot of unnecessary damage; firearms were too loud, and crossbows could easily run out of ammo.

After observing the training ground of Mythag for so many days, she knew she could spot the weaknesses of both combatants at a glance and nearly instinctively plan the attack routes. Those things that required abundant experience to know could be deduced in just a second for her. No, what she needed was something more precise, a weapon that could inflict the greatest damage with the least force.

The girl pondered for a moment, moved a stool from the side, stood on it, and reached for the rapier hanging high above.

Long, elegant, agile, and lightweight, it could accurately inflict harm - yes, that's it, it met all her requirements]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127110_Title = {
    Text = "Rewinding Time"
  },
  CollectionHall_127111_Desc = {
    Text = "\"What kind of fun happens when a world is heading towards its end?\"\n\nMouchette didn't know, but she was looking forward to it.\n\nThis anticipation was different from before; this time it wasn't just about having a bit of fun with some Ancient Monsters, it was research and investigation measured on the scale of an entire world. And at the core of this research and investigation was one person—\n the Keeper of Mythag.\n\n\"I will save this world...\"\n\n\"This world will definitely not meet a fate of collapse...\"\n\nThat person, who held ideals and bore the fate of a world, made such a promise. In response, Mouchette knew she should show a moved expression; it was the social etiquette established in human society.\n\nBut she didn't want to pretend anymore, or rather, after witnessing the Keeper confront @4, sacrificing themselves to save a world, she felt there was no need to pretend in front of someone who had experienced cosmic horror.\n\n\"Pretending\" was the game rule of human society—decent yet boring—while the universe... the universe was real and straightforward—\n either survive or perish.\n\nThus, her response to the Keeper was also genuine and straightforward.\n\n\"I don't care if this world will be saved or destroyed... Compared to that, I am more curious about you.\"\n\nI am curious whether you can fulfill your ideals or if you will crumble on the path of pursuing them.\n\nI am also curious whether this world will respond to your wishes or inevitably head towards destruction.\n\nNo matter which outcome, it will be a grand and rare form of fun.\n\nI will always look forward to that day...\n\nwith my eyes and my axe, waiting."
  },
  CollectionHall_127111_Title = {
    Text = "Doomsday Rampage"
  },
  CollectionHall_127112_Desc = {
    Text = [[
"What is memory?" 
"It is what you have forgotten." 

Lily has a forgetful mother. 
She forgets to call Lily for meals, forgets to give Lily her medicine, and even forgets Lily's name. 
"What should I do?" 
Lily sat on the hospital bed, pretending to be deep in thought, and sighed. 
Such a mother is truly worrying. 

Later, Lily wrote her name on a wooden board and hung it around her neck every day. 
That should help her remember, right? 
At first, her mother could still laugh and say she was overreacting, that it was just a complication from long-term fatigue. 

Gradually, she began to show confusion and impatience: 
"Lily... what is Lily?" 
Amber eyes gazed at Lily, carrying a hint of veiled caution. 
It turned out that when the meaning of words is forgotten, the harmony temporarily maintained through language will ultimately disappear. 

Lily hugged her mother. 
The heartbeats of mother and daughter were merely inches apart, yet she felt extremely lonely. 

After that day, Lily put away the wooden board, no longer indulged in her mother's affection, and stopped reminding her that she had gone hungry for many days. 
She was a sick patient on the brink of death, numbly waiting for the verdict of death. 
She was a distant spectator, watching herself being injected, anesthetized, and manipulated into any form her mother wished her to be. 
The happy words exchanged between mother and daughter, the soft embraces... 
Those joyful memories flashing like dreamy bubbles were carefully locked in Lily's heart. 
Only on some weary nights did she reluctantly take them out and gently savor them.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127112_Title = {
    Text = "Grace Through Pain"
  },
  CollectionHall_127113_Desc = {
    Text = "The towering spire collapsed with a thunderous roar, books written by scholars from different races across different times scattered all around. In an instant, black triangles of all sizes covered each book and every brick, quickly merging into one and spreading outwards.\nBlack slime flowed like lava along the orderly streets as people screamed and cried, attempting to escape this terrifying disaster. Many tried to use transportation to flee but crashed into buildings or other vehicles that had encountered accidents in the chaos; more people were caught off guard, running away from the slime only to be knocked over by others equally terrified and ultimately assimilated by the slime. Children cried loudly on the streets, while several young people hid in the remnants of buildings, deluding themselves that they could evade death this way.\n\"There was no warning, why, why!\"\n\"Why didn't anyone warn us!\"\n\"@1, it's dissolution! Help!\"\n\"Quick, initiate consciousness transfer! It's the only way—ah!\"\n\"@2, hurry, use the device!\" said a voice, \"We'll buy you time!\"\n\"No! I—\"\n\"We've already been @1, but you, you still have hope.\" answered a gentle voice, \"Survive, @2, survive. Then—\"\n\nWinkle awoke abruptly, her eyes snapping open to find herself surrounded by stacks of books and several coffee-stained mugs. On the nearby blackboard were notes and memos of varying sizes, along with an equation only partially completed. In the disheveled room, lights were placed in corners and at the center, as well as beside the large device she was at, illuminating the entire office brilliantly.\nShe remained silent for a moment, curling her body more into the positioning device, continuing the interrupted calculations."
  },
  CollectionHall_127113_Title = {
    Text = "Incalculable Factor"
  },
  CollectionHall_127114_Desc = {
    Text = "Pain, intense pain filled her every sense.\n\nThe metal diving suit was insignificant under the water pressure, its shell buckling inward, screws bursting. Something pressed against her abdomen, something pierced her arm. Cold seawater squeezed in through the damaged suit, and only the thickened metal helmet barely held its form, preserving a meager amount of oxygen for her.\n\nThrough the lone peephole of the helmet, she watched as the water outside turned from azure to ink blue, and from ink blue to pitch black. The vapor from her breath condensed on the glass, and the roar of the whirlpool gradually faded, becoming mere phantasms in her ears. She gradually lost sensation in her limbs, her breathing growing heavier.\n\nShe guessed she must have fainted, from cold, blood loss, and lack of oxygen; any would be enough to cloud her consciousness. Yet she was unsure because, no matter how much she blinked, all she saw was the same darkness.\n\nThis was a place where light could not reach, an uncharted domain in Aequor.\n\nA dull excitement finally stirred her blood—an unknown domain, the final adventure. Wouldn't she have fulfilled her dream? Even though she couldn't see anything now.\n\nA strange sensation came from her ankle. Instinctively looking down, she discovered that, in the darkness, something seemed to climb up her leg. Was it a peculiar deep-sea creature, colder than the sea itself? How... in such darkness, she seemed able to see its outline?\n\nBlack, writhing, like sludge...\nWhat is this? Where is she? Who... is she?"
  },
  CollectionHall_127114_Title = {
    Text = "Memory Spiral"
  },
  CollectionHall_127115_Desc = {
    Text = "(The following answers are excerpted from Dr. Clementine's diagnostic manual for reference only)\n\n\n1. Caecus.\n\n2. 16, 17...? Who knows.\nWhy should I care? I'm already dead.\n\n3. A rural fishing village, you wouldn't find its name on any map.\n\n4. I don't want to say.\n\n5. Freak. Ugly. Silly pig. Stupid @1... these are rather common.\n\n6. Shimmering golden catfish face, abbreviated as \"catfish face\".\n\n7. Rainy days.\n\n8. I don't know. When it rains, I walk back and forth on the beach...\nIt's been a few years. I just look in the distance, nothing else.\n\n9. I SAID I DON'T #¥% KNOW, @1 GET LOST!!\n-------\n\n14. Umm... maybe it's because, Uncle Ornn once told me he would come take me \"home\" in a big sailboat when it rained...\n\n15. Yes, he fulfilled his promise...\nI drifted at the bottom of the sea for several days, starving and thirsty, every part of my body in pain...\nThen I saw Uncle Ornn and his white sailboat.\nHis whole body... No, his whole skeleton, to be precise, was hanging on the mast of the sailboat—he also failed his transformation.\nThen, with my last strength, I drifted over and sat on the mast with him.\n\n16. We promised to go home together."
  },
  CollectionHall_127115_Title = {
    Text = "Fin of Sorrow"
  },
  CollectionHall_127116_Desc = {
    Text = "\"People are born with the tide and die with the ebb.\"\nThis is a legend that has been passed down in Nymphaea's hometown.\n\nThe villagers of Sevada do not fear death; to them, the sprouting and wilting of life are like the rise and fall of the tide, both part of nature.\nThey love the blue sky, the ocean, the flocks of seagulls, and the calla lilies blooming in the morning sun.\nThey despise steam, iron tracks, and all things too heavily marked by human intervention—interference with life is included in that disdain.\nTo cut one's life short is unacceptable in the eyes of the Sevadians.\n\nNymphaea is not a typical Sevadian.\nFor instance, she is always drawn to the atmosphere of shipwrecks.\nA dead shipwreck is home to countless lives: fish, water plants, various shellfish...\nHere, life and death intertwine in a mysterious and sacred manner.\nWith calmness, Nymphaea approaches the wreck, as if stepping into an immensely solemn cathedral.\n\nDuring the years when her father took her on trips to relax, Nymphaea saw a five-act play.\nThe content of that play has long faded from her memory; it seemed to tell the life of an ancient emperor.\nHe lived a chaotic life filled with military campaigns north and south, only to die from a shameful conspiracy.\nShe remembers one line:\n<Italic:Cowards die many times before their deaths; the valiant never taste of death but once.>\n\nYears later, when Nymphaea steps into the cold seawater, pained by her longing for life, that line floats through her mind:\n\"The valiant never taste of death but once...\"\nSo she wipes her tears, says goodbye to her parents one last time, and continues towards the shipwreck in her heart.\nShe will become her own warrior."
  },
  CollectionHall_127116_Title = {
    Text = "Gift of Decay"
  },
  CollectionHall_127117_Desc = {
    Text = "A.F.@1/06/05\nAlbinor brought back some rare Silvers from the D-Rift. Truly impressive.\nI made some improvements to the purification method.\nThis time, I introduced a sufficient amount of carbon dioxide and chlorine gas, followed by low-temperature evaporation and crystallization...\nThese mechanical steps aren't worth recording in detail.\n\nA.F.@1/06/06\nI dissected the internal organs and limbs of specimen 024.\nThis material was brought back by Albinor from the clinic and has generated 13 dissolution holes, with a maximum diameter of 8mm.\nCutting the parasitic organisms of the OS-106 D-Rift monster.\nAccording to the comparison of various test data, it shows the highest resonance compatibility with 024.\nThe only issue is... those tentacles are a bit too \"lively.\"\nI think I won't want to eat octopus for a long time.\nI hope the final result doesn't disappoint me.\n\n@1 Year 6 Month 6 Day\nThe grafting experiment succeeded, but the vital signs of the specimen disappeared.\nThis is a common occurrence; we just need to ensure that the grafting site hasn't spread infection.\nSent for a week of observation—what follows won't be my responsibility anymore.\nToday, I read two articles criticizing living Awakener experiments in the \"Internal Journal.\"\nNeedless to say, the signatures reveal they are my old friends from Mythag.\nIt's laughable—if these old fogeys would just move their hefty butts and visit the lab, they'd know my conclusions are unshakable.\nThe experiment with 024 will serve as an excellent counterattack.\n\nA.F.@1/06/22\nTwo weeks have passed, and the vital signs of 024 remain unstable—or rather, the personality within her is dividing and multiplying rapidly like cellular mitosis.\nThe experiment has failed in an astonishing manner.\nSend 024 to the wax museum; I don't need her following me daily, reminding me of my foolishness and rashness."
  },
  CollectionHall_127117_Title = {
    Text = "Aberrant Devour"
  },
  CollectionHall_127118_Desc = {
    Text = [[
It was a silver-white, clear, and spotless heart.

Made of pure silver, it beat steadily inside its mechanical frame.

It had once been stained by blood, smeared by mud.

But as death's shadow fell, it returned at last to its original form.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127118_Title = {
    Text = "Heart of Silver"
  },
  CollectionHall_127119_Desc = {
    Text = "Time flowed, and Lotan could no longer clearly recall her memories of the planet's birth.\nShe only remembered that she was a chosen being.\n\nThis was a story that took place before all concepts had arisen.\n\"Life\" had not yet taken root, and the \"Gods\" were still far beyond the heavens.\nWithin this chaotic nebula, Chaos collided with Chaos, and matter gradually took form amidst the impacts and turbulence.\nStars gathered dust, rocks rose into mountainous shapes, and atmospheres condensed into vast bodies of water.\nThen, this place was declared a \"planet.\"\n\nThe soul of Chaos, trapped within the cage of time, crashed against the newborn soil.\nUnable to control its savage nature, driven by the urge to destroy, It toppled countless mountains and filled countless rivers and lakes.\nThen—The \"Gods\" crossed the distant stars and descended upon the barren world.\n\nThe \"Gods\" brought the seeds of civilization, and also imprisoned the soul of Chaos within a \"structured\" body.\n\"Make a pact with me...\"\nFacing the roaring Spirit of Chaos, the white-robed \"God\" whispered.\n\"A great civilization will be born here.\"\n\"You will meet wise but inactive philosophers, and clash with uncertain blades... In the future, you will no longer be ruled by destruction and devastation.\"\n\"Until that day comes... Until we are reunited, protect this place for me.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_127119_Title = {
    Text = "Celestial Beast"
  },
  CollectionHall_127120_Desc = {
    Text = "When the Duke appointed him a knight, the boy had witnessed only seven cycles of the four seasons.\n\nThough the Duke's gesture was born of a whimsical tease, the court took the oath to heart. The veteran knights honed his skills in horseback archery, the attendants drilled him in the nuances of etiquette, and the Princess—above all others—placed her absolute trust in her young protector.\n\nWhile strolling across the wild highlands of Aequidan and into the deep gorge, the young knight led the Princess's horse by the reigns. She lay weakly across the saddle, a hidden darkness slowly devouring her body from within.\n\n\"Princess, we can't go any further,\" he whispered.\n\nTo cross the gorge and the river beyond was to abandon the very soil that nurtured them. Outside their borders, war raged; the enemy watched their fertile lands with a hungry, predatory gaze. Only the great chasm had preserved their peace, allowing this small fragment of the world to maintain the dignity of a \"nation.\"\n\nFrom the safety of the cliffs, they had watched the downfall of those across the water. The pleas of the innocent drowned in the river, destined only to become the tragic meter of the victors' poetry.\n\nBut no matter how great the nation, none can truly escape the currents of history.\n\nThe enemy eventually came. They severed the knight's tender hands, ensuring he could never again raise spear or shield. They crushed his fragile knees, forcing him to watch in helpless agony as the cavalry smashed through the palace doors. Even then, the knight struggled, biting at the legs of the enemy's warhorses, a desperate and futile effort to halt their atrocities.\n\nThen, for the first time, he saw the \"black plague\" the Princess had warned of.\n\nA flood of dark liquid burst from the palace doors. It surged over the cavalry's greaves, yet the invaders did not falter. The \"black plague\" rose, filling the knight's mouth and nose and choking his lungs, yet he fought the urge to succumb.\n\nThen, a familiar voice—gentle and known—echoed in the chambers of his mind. \"You've done enough... my most loyal knight.\"\n\nIn the end, only a vast, silent blankness remained."
  },
  CollectionHall_127120_Title = {
    Text = "Heart of a Knight"
  },
  CollectionHall_127121_Desc = {
    Text = "They are born from humanity's imagination of the unknown, yet they do not possess the hysteria and clawing behavior often imagined.\n\nThey are rational; they are calm.\n\nThey come for the future, they come for existence.\n\nThey are the most unusual, the most incredible miracles.\n\nAt first, their voice was like the chirping of insects. But after fully comprehending their thoughts, that voice fell silent.\n\nYet afterward, the masters of the voice attempted to influence every decision she made.\n\nIn her first year as an <Awakener>, she learned to coexist with the voices in her head.\n\nShe plunged into consciousness, becoming part of the gestalt, seizing the information and knowledge she needed, and finally disengaging safely to return to reality.\n\nShe did the same when the \"Black Plague\" came for this body.\n\nShe aimed to separate the body from knowledge, memory, and soul, making the brain an immortal entity.\n\nAfter the surgery, she nearly entered a vivid and wonderful sleep—but within mere seconds, her thoughts began to operate once more.\n\nShe knew clearly that she was approaching that absolute destruction surpassing form, power, and the chaos of symmetry."
  },
  CollectionHall_127121_Title = {
    Text = "Deathless Ascent"
  },
  CollectionHall_127122_Desc = {
    Text = [[
People always like to define boundaries and symbols based on their own standards.
How narrow-minded, ignorant, and pathetic it is to confine the world within human flesh.
She abandoned her physical form early on, yet still could not reach the true boundaries.
The river of knowledge is chaotic and endless, and the black void has once again caught up with her.
Silently, she confronted it. If tangible aspects cannot reveal the totality of the world, could the void behind it hold the true answer?
She staked her life in the most insane gamble.
She finally saw the end.
The gate of truth opened wide, and the face of the world was instantly overturned.
So it is, so it is.
She desperately wanted everyone to see the truth within the void and be freed from their futile struggles.
Once, she stood atop the waves, leading the world forward.
Now, she still wields the shepherd's whip, joyfully guiding it into the Abyss.
People, terrified, expelled her, calling her a madwoman.
How strange, she thought.
But in my eyes, you are no different.
]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127122_Title = {
    Text = "Manikin of Oblivion"
  },
  CollectionHall_127123_Desc = {
    Text = "Do not fear death. It is merely the body returning the soul to the night, like the tide receding into the quiet dark. True horror is not the end—it is dissolving into nothingness, becoming an unremembered whisper in the void.\n\nShe did not die peacefully.\n\nThe withered corpse had stiffened, blood and dissolution fluid fused into dark crimson glass. Yet her soul still quivered in the hollow of her throat, a wisp of consciousness clinging like smoke between her bones. A butterfly with shattered wings, beautiful and doomed.\n\nDoresain stepped into the room, leaving the dust undisturbed. He knelt beside her, his gaze tracing her clenched eyelids, her frozen fingers, the restless ghost-light trapped within.\n\n\"Am I still alive?\"\n\n\"Will this darkness swallow me?\"\n\nHe did not answer. Instead, he pried open her cracked fingers with the care of one unfolding a dying flower. There was no pity in him, no judgment—only the serene patience of a god who deals in endings. And in that moment, she found peace.\n\nA rose between their joined hands—sweet, fragile. He bent low, pressing a kiss to her knuckles. As his lips met her skin, the last shudder of death stretched thin, then melted into the air like a sigh after a storm. No fear. No doubt. Only surrender.\n\n\"I will remember you.\"\n\nHe stood, studying her tranquil form. Then—sharp teeth, yielding flesh. Celina's voice curled through his mind:\n\n\"I believe in you, brother.\"\n\nShe was fortunate. In Doresain's memory, she would sleep forever."
  },
  CollectionHall_127123_Title = {
    Text = "Kiss of Repose"
  },
  CollectionHall_127124_Desc = {
    Text = "The first time you saw a living golem was at the scholar lady's house.\n\"Even now, she still amazes me. To me, she is the universe itself.\"\nThe golem gives you a mechanical smile, muttering incomprehensibly.\nYou gaze into her gray eyes, feeling like you are in a surging gray ocean, the shimmering waves moving from one horizon to another.\n\nBefore leaving, the scholar lady hands you a worn booklet with notes on making golems.\nThat night, you spread it out to study the scribbled formulas and spells, but your mind is filled with the golem's elusive smile.\nYou never forget her.\n\nDays later, you find an excuse to visit again.\nYou step over piles of books, tools, and skeletons, pull aside heavy curtains and entwined cobwebs, finally squatting before the golem.\nThe scholar lady is huddled in a corner, looking haggard and drained of light in just a few days.\n\"You came... just like them.\"\nThe scholar lady coughs weakly.\n\"Yes... I came.\"\nYou pick up the golem's hand and kiss it repeatedly.\nIts cool fingertips brush against your neck, causing a slight pain. You close your eyes.\n\nWhen you wake up, you are bathed in warm white sunlight, your body fluctuating with gentle waves.\nYou feel unprecedented lightness, as if your soul has left your body.\nYou turn your head and see gray-black heads.\nThey wail, twist, like dark wildflowers scattered across the gray primeval ocean.\n\"No—\"\nYour throat chokes out black mucus, and you can no longer move.\nIt turns out you have become one of those heads.\n\n\"In June of Year 2, renowned alchemist Romalin Ludwig was found mysteriously dead in his study, his head missing. The mysterious alchemy manual also disappeared...\"\n\n(This content is recorded in Volume 2 of \"Alchemy Anecdotes\" from Mythag Library)"
  },
  CollectionHall_127124_Title = {
    Text = "Treasured Rarity"
  },
  CollectionHall_127125_Desc = {
    Text = "To this day, Castor cannot explain the true meaning of freedom.\n\nHe often feels like the more foolish one among the twins, clumsily following Pollux since his youth, listening to his brother's wild ideas one after another.\n\nIn the dull and numb life of training, he thought that having that touch of lightness was the happiest thing—until Juliette ordered the regular transformation ritual for Pollux.\n\nEndless pain was poured entirely onto his brother, while Castor could only stay helplessly by his side, watching the vibrant smile fade more and more from his brother's face, powerless to stop it.\n\n\"Do you know what freedom means?\" In the dead of night, Pollux silently asked Castor, holding the worn manuscript they had both flipped through countless times.\n\nCastor shook his head.\n\n\"Then, do you want to see the outside world, brother?\"\n\nCastor was stunned. He seemed to understand what Pollux wanted to pursue—those things he had never seen, existing only in the withered texts, beyond his imagination.\n\nHe was deeply shaken by such a rebellious and shocking idea. He remained silent, perhaps for a long time, or perhaps just a few breaths, then he nodded without fear.\n\nEven if it meant going up against the entire church. Even if it meant sacrificing his life.\n\nThus, a pair of birds flew out of the cage they had never left. But unfortunately, they never thought the price of freedom would be so unbearable.\n\nWhen the Hunter's gunfire sounded, the birds fell from the sky.\n\nCastor had just begun to taste the flavor of freedom, yet he helplessly watched his brother's wings, which were carrying them toward it, being brutally torn out.\n\nFaced with Juliette's terrifying anger, his pale and trembling brother showed him an unyielding smile from amidst the crowd.\n\n\"Hold on, for the sake of freedom.\"\n\nCastor kept replaying Pollux's silent lips in his mind, until, in the dim torment, he chewed those two faith-like words into a burning brand. When he finally met Pollux again, he was astonished to find that the person who had always led him forward had heartlessly abandoned them."
  },
  CollectionHall_127125_Title = {
    Text = "Unbearable Freedom"
  },
  CollectionHall_127126_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Amidst the wind and rain-swept night, the daughter of the deity sat alone beneath the porthole.

The icy moonlight shone upon the swaddling clothes, where the Divine Fetus, dripping with black viscous fluid, slept peacefully.

She began to sing a lullaby.

<Italic:"Hush now, hush, my seaborne dear.">

<Italic:"The Black Moon holds your cradle near...">

<Italic:"Swallow the stars in your dream's mere.">

The song was also a prayer, and deep-sea fish gathered at its call.

The entire vessel became a gigantic altar, much like the day she gave birth to the Divine Fetus.

She cut open her own chest, removed the dripping flesh and bone, repaying the kindness of her upbringing and the destiny of her race with her life.

Her sacrifice did not earn the freedom she craved; death was not eternal rest, but merely the beginning of tragedy.

Since then, her only peace came in the night.

<Italic:"Hush now, hush, my seaborne dear...">

When this lullaby concludes, the great Eternal Realm will pierce the surface and rise from the turbulent ocean.

Embracing this futile illusion, Murphy gently closed her eyes.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127126_Title = {
    Text = "Uteri Somnia"
  },
  CollectionHall_127127_Desc = {
    Text = [[
He always pushed himself hard and drove away all his companions with his harshness, thinking he would walk this path alone forever in pursuit of musical perfection.
The heights are cold, and he accepted this destined fate.
Until he heard that person's performance.
It had nothing to do with perfection. The music was too unrestrained, like the person himself, sometimes deviating from the score and even suddenly forgetting parts. Then, his hands would improvise with clever, lively melodies, earning surprise and praise.
He watched him, as if watching a musical sprite play among the notes.
This is what his father called talent, indeed. He was deeply attracted, like everyone else, but he couldn't change his steps.
He was too ordinary and foolish, only able to traverse this laboriously paved path.
Everyone followed that person, and he grew further and further apart.
He longed to be close to him, but besides playing, he knew nothing else.
How to converse with him? What kind of score would attract his attention?
He composed scores as if drafting opening words. Until he had no chance to speak again.
Deep regret consumed him, making all else meaningless.
Only that unfinished letter remained, meant for the departed soul.
He exhausted himself, ultimately collapsing before the score, dreaming without reaching the end of the path.
If I can never reach the end, what is my life's persistence for?
Distant flute music from the light pacified his questioning soul.
In a daze, he picked up the flute, realizing his true mission.
With his ceaseless playing, bring eternal peace.
]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127127_Title = {
    Text = "Eternal Requiem"
  },
  CollectionHall_127128_Desc = {
    Text = "Even without the memories of your life before this point, your underdeveloped muscles clearly indicate that you were never the type to love sports or violence.\n\nYou really can't understand why Mythag set such high and comprehensive combat standards for Investigators.\n\nShouldn't the focus of an Investigator lie in the word \"investigation\"—in a sharp mind, rigorous logic, and a bit of well-timed luck?\n\nEvery time Ramona dragged you out of your warm bed in the dormitory on time, and you stood on the empty drill ground facing wave after wave of attacks, you missed Professor Doll's sarcastic logic classes more than ever. Even piles of homework and the most hair-raising exams were far gentler than the pain of being beaten and falling repeatedly during combat training.\n\nOn the 19th attempt, you lost your balance under the relentless pressure of the rapier that blocked all your escape routes and fell flat on your back, feeling as if every bone in your body was about to shatter. Gasping for breath, you wiped the sweat from your forehead in frustration and absolutely refused to get up again.\n\nRamona showed no surprise at all. She executed a graceful flourish with her sword and sheathed it, her heels clicking crisply as she walked toward you.\n\nYou shut your eyes tightly, determined to brace yourself for all kinds of scolding and criticism. Surprisingly, no blows or insults came. After three seconds, you opened your eyes again and saw only a faint smile right in front of you. Ramona slightly bent down, her gloved hand extended toward you.\n\n\"You've actually tried really hard, I know. But what we face is always the unknown fear and danger. Even I have moments of unexpected oversight.\"\n\n\"Just to make me feel a little more at ease, let's try one more time, partner.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_127128_Title = {
    Text = "Special Training"
  },
  CollectionHall_127129_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Humans are creatures who love to sing, and so are the people of that now desolate planet.

Melodies rise freely from their throats, without any intention or purpose.

Scattered by the wind into stray notes, they fade away with passing emotions.

It is said that every wandering tribe in the desert has its own songs.

But the Desolate-born lost theirs.

Along with their song, they also lost their name.

No one knows what the planet was originally called.

It is a cursed world, scorched by drought, storms, famine...

Disasters came one after another, until the planet was utterly broken.

The rich and powerful, dressed in finery, boarded arks and left.
The planet became desolate, home only to the unblessed, the lowly.

All of them were abandoned.

Since then, the Desolate-born decided they needed no laughter, no poetry, and no songs.

They will remember the pain of abandonment, forever crawling through the white desert, until the day the planet ends.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127129_Title = {
    Text = "Song of the Bound"
  },
  CollectionHall_127130_Desc = {
    Text = "Most of the time, death always arrives silently, before a human's consciousness has a chance to react. The reaper would have already crept close, claiming that tender, fragile life.\n\nHowever, it is said that in a remote desert unknown to most, there exists an amber-tinted death god. She brings Amber-Tinted Death with her amber fire and amber gun, after issuing a formal proclamation.\n\nThe man stood on the sandy sea beneath the moonlit night, his hand gripping the firearm trembling ceaselessly. He stared intently at Kathigu-Ra's amber silhouette without blinking, not daring to relax for even a moment.\n\nCold sweat dripped from his forehead, falling heavily into the hearts of everyone behind him. He had brought many people along, but at this moment, very few of them were actually useful.\n\nHe couldn't understand—this was supposed to be a simple mission to loot an abandoned warehouse, so why had he encountered the legendary death god?\n\n\"You mean the death god? That's just an idle rumor from before,\" Kathigu-Ra said indifferently.\n\n\"I used to coat them in amber; perhaps you could still find some leftover paint clinging to the surface?\"\n\nShe generously displayed the twin guns in her hands to the person before her.\n\n\"The amber-colored flame at the muzzle is just a special substance I sprinkled on.\"\n\nHer finger plunged into the barrel, rotating once around before pulling out some unknown powder.\n\n\"The so-called death god is merely an image I once crafted for myself.\"\n\n\"It was powerful, mysterious, and omnipotent.\"\n\n\"It helped me intimidate those incompetent petty villains.\"\n\nShe spoke arrogantly, completely unconcerned about the increasingly fierce gaze from the man before her.\n\nShe spoke as if no one else was present, entirely unaware that danger was already approaching.\n\nWhen the bullets finally rained down upon her, shock and bewilderment flickered in her eyes—\n\nmerely to conceal that subtle hint of excitement and madness buried deep within her subconscious.\n\n...\n\nThe gunfire ceased, and everything unfolded exactly as she had anticipated.\n\nShe stood at the center of the battlefield, everything around her scorched and marked by fire.\n\nKathigu-Ra performed only two actions—raising the gun, and firing.\n\nWhen she lifted the spear, death danced behind all things, equally casting its omen upon all.\n\nWhen she pulled the trigger, flames engulfed everything, offering the world a sea of amber blossoms.\n\n\"They have accompanied me through many years, bearing silent witness to endless bloodshed and death.\"\n\n\"They were once forced to wear the disguise of lies, used to hide my own weakness and helplessness.\"\n\n\"Now, they are no longer just rumors.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_127130_Title = {
    Text = "Amber-Tinted Death"
  },
  CollectionHall_127131_Desc = {
    Text = "<Italic:\"Do you regret it now?\">\n\nThe ancient deity, reborn from a resplendent glazed goblet, inhaled her scent. It lingered like a ghost upon her shoulder as he pushed open the window to usher in a night breeze laced with a faint fragrance.\n\n\"A single furrow of my brow causes beacon fires to flare along the city walls. If I smile, tribute boats from every land sail up the rivers, laden with wonders: rare treasures, exotic beasts, honeyed brews, and delicacies. I am the most precious treasure of the entire dynasty—why should I regret?\"\n\nFlushed with wine, she giggled and nestled into plush cushions of silk and fur, drowsy and content.\n...\n<Italic:\"Do you regret it now?\">\n\nThe ancient deity, bound to a wisp of incense, conversed with her. Faint, illusory smoke drifted down from the pavilion, tracing the outline of a flower bud as its petals unfurled.\n\n\"They exhaust themselves in a fever of plots and rivalries, while I reap the rewards without lifting a finger. The higher they climb, the harder they fall—but I? I already have everything. If anyone is due for regret, it certainly isn't me.\"\n\nWith a cheeky grin, he refilled the jug and casually plucked a soft twig to tease the insects chirping in their cage.\n...\n<Italic:\"Do you regret it now?\">\n\nThe ancient deity, emerging from the well in the form of swirling mist, chuckled softly in her ear. Its tendrils brushed through her hair and shook loose a plump white magnolia from its branch.\n\n\"I have love, I have bonds, I have warm congee when I return home at sunset, and I also have fine wine for joyous gatherings. How could I regret? Truly, I do not.\"\n\nShe picked up the <Italic:huadian> to put it on her forehead. The warm, golden candlelight swayed along the hem of her skirt; her gaze clung earnestly to the window, waiting for the one who would return.\n...\n<Italic:\"Do you regret it now?\">\n\nThe hem of her skirt, once elegant, is now spattered with the foul mire before the Palace Gates. The guards who yesterday offered her fawning gifts now stand deaf to her wailing pleas; two cold halberds cross and fall, sealing away her last path to life. \n\nThe mist heaves a long, lingering sigh. Then, crimson blood blooms upon the snow, only to be utterly buried by the next winter squall.\n...\n<Italic:\"Do you regret it now?\"> \n\nPearls from the South Seas spill from sandalwood chests, shattering against the green-stone floor. The crisp, clattering music of their fall is more melodious than any music. \n\nThe scrolls he most cherished—those he hung before his desk to admire daily—tumble into the hall. The brushwork of a master's landscape is pierced and shredded by a blade's tip, much like the sovereign lands he ignored as they were poisoned by the fires of war. \n\nThe mist curls in mockery. Then, a fire ignites, and the carved beams and painted rafters are reduced to the dying embers of a fallen dynasty.\n\n<Italic:\"Do you regret it now?\"> \n\nThe man whose name she once tasted upon her tongue never returns. Along a distant river lie withered bones; upon a silken pillow a beauty waits in vain. \n\nDid he become a trusted minister to the Emperor, or a consort to the Princess? Did he linger amidst the \"flowers\" of the pleasure quarters, never to look back? Or was he devoured by famished refugees, serving as mere grain for a year of disaster? \n\nThe mist murmurs in ambiguous tones, yet it never grants her the answer she so desperately seeks.\n\nThe most precious treasure in the dynasty's heyday becomes the most cherished burial offering when the dynasty falls.\nThe most carefree favorite of a flourishing family becomes the most ideal scapegoat when the family declines.\n\nAnd as for the last story—it is one that is all too common in this world."
  },
  CollectionHall_127131_Title = {
    Text = "Vain Regrets"
  },
  CollectionHall_127132_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Gloomy clouds shrouded Londinium, blocking the moonlight. The midnight chimes have rung, and the towering chimneys continue to spew hot black smoke and steam. Snowflakes, touched by the dust in the wind, are stained with a dull gray before touching the ground; they flutter down onto the streetlamp, almost instantly melting from the heat of the light and dripping onto the girl passing by.
The girl wears a brown dress, with oversized sleeves carelessly rolled up, revealing her bony arms. She struggles to jog, occasionally pulling up her sleeves, trying hard to catch up with the woman ahead.
The woman glances sideways at the girl and clicks her tongue: "Hurry up, don't think that just because you walk slowly you don't have to go." 
"Okay, okay, Mom," the girl quickly runs up beside the woman, panting, "Sorry, Mom." 
"Don't call me Mom!" The woman grabs the girl's arm and drags her along faster, "You bloodsucking waste, if it weren't for you, I wouldn't have sunk to this wretched place." 
"Sorry..." 
"Shut up, useless thing." The woman's nails dig into the girl's arm, leaving a line of deep marks, "I tell you, from now on the Fang is your home, don't even think about coming out to find me; I don't want to see you even if it kills me, got it?" 
"I... I understand." The girl lowers her head, tears falling beneath her shoes, disappearing into the filthy slush along the Tablet road. In the distance, the factory sounds its closing whistle, a stray cat darts through the alley, the subtle noise is swallowed up by the footsteps of the two. They turn the corner, passing a yard with clothes hanging that exude dampness, and finally stop in front of a building with metal gates.
"You wait here," the woman's voice is very calm, even carrying a hint of detachment, "When dawn breaks, the people inside will come out. They will take you in.
Don't follow me, or you'll see if I kill you." 
The woman turns and leaves, her similarly thin and slightly stooped figure quickly disappearing into the darkness. The girl helplessly clutches her hands, watching the place where the woman left, wiping her tears with her sleeve.
Dim light appears behind her, stretching the shadows of the iron gate and herself. A hand lands on the girl's shoulder, startling her.
"Poor child, why are you here alone?" The newcomer is a young woman dressed in a nun-like robe, "Come, Sister Sarah will take you inside. You won't be cold for long."]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127132_Title = {
    Text = "Winter's Requiem"
  },
  CollectionHall_127133_Desc = {
    Text = "\"My masterpiece? Hmm—so curious, huh? Alright, alright, after all, it's a request from a VVIP. But a plain narration wouldn't suit my title as a master magician, so let me present it to you through a grand performance!\nCome, come, please take your seat in the VIP area. The suspenseful magical memory show filled with money and betrayal is about to begin!\"\n-------\nWith a snap of her fingers, the lights came on, and Casiah's magic hat floated in mid-air. Its yellow opening opened and closed, surprisingly emitting Casiah's voice.\n\"Not long ago, in a not-so-distant place, there was a circus with rabbits, clowns, lions, and elephants—\"\nAs the hat shook, out tumbled a rabbit, a clown, a lion, and an elephant. The drumbeat grew increasingly urgent, accompanied by the sound of cannon blasts. Casiah, dressed in splendid theatrical attire, emerged from the hat and placed it on her own head.\n\"Most importantly, there was a talented and gifted magician's apprentice!\"\n-------\nThe apprentice's growth was met with applause, even attracting a lavishly dressed investor. Strangely, ever since the investor joined them, rabbits, clowns, lions, elephants... many people and animals disappeared one by one. The stage emptied significantly, yet the apprentice seemed oblivious, repeating her former routine until the investor handed her a glass of wine.\nThe apprentice drank the wine, fainted, and the stage instantly went dark. Faint sighs drifted from the darkness.\n\"That was when I first understood regret.\"\n-------\n\"But is regret enough? I want to know how it feels when the benefactor cries, how it feels when the audience laughs. I want to know more, much more. At that moment—\nI opened my eyes.\"\nPaper confetti exploded in the air, fragments fluttering down. Casiah suddenly appeared in the center of the stage. She tapped the brim of her hat, and the top hat opened wide, revealing a dazzling light.\n\"I opened my eyes and realized that all emotions are light, all can be stored in my magic hat.\nNow, please relax, my dear VIP. The next segment won't hurt at all—it will only make you feel a bit numb, a little indifferent to life...\""
  },
  CollectionHall_127133_Title = {
    Text = "Happy Magic Show"
  },
  CollectionHall_127134_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Clementine was not a strong child, so when afflicted by a strange illness, tormented by pain and the looming death, she would often awake in the dead of night, crying silently.
And each morning after her cries, a "Gift" would appear at her bedside.
A few pieces of lavishly wrapped candy, trendy hair accessories, and adorably stuffed bears...
But what left the deepest impression was a specimen of a cocoon.
At that time, she was gravely ill, bedridden, struggling to lift up the specimen to gaze at the life within the light-pierced cocoon.
That life was sleeping, but that life had achieved eternity.
While she was nearing true death.
Thinking of this, her tears silently fell. But a pair of hands wiped her tears away.
"Don't cry, Clementine. Someday, you too will be reborn like these cocoons."
"I will give you new life."
Her father never lied, at least not to her, so Clementine had no doubt in his words.
She trusted her father, and so when she entered that profane mountain, she did so without hesitation, and when she endured the agonizing pain of dissolving flesh, she did so without complaint.
Because she believed all this was the price and necessary process for rebirth.
When all the pain and despair were over, she would heal, return to the place called "home," and reunite with her only family.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127134_Title = {
    Text = "Veiled Anguish"
  },
  CollectionHall_127135_Desc = {
    Text = "She never dreams.\n\nThe young apprentice sculptor firmly believes in absolute rationality and order, just like her cold, lifeless works.\nFrom the moment she first laid eyes on it, she was captivated.\nSoft, pure—it was the perfect coloring material.\nUnder the moonlight, she worked tirelessly, bringing the black goo from the graveyard back to her studio.\n\nA week later, a sculpture titled \"@2\" was exhibited at the fair.\nThat night, she heard waves from afar.\nFor the first time, she dreamed.\nUnder the tranquil morning light, the dust-covered underwater palace lay peacefully asleep.\nShe wandered through the white coral clusters, breathing in an atmosphere thick with loneliness and forgetfulness.\n\nWhen she awoke, her fingers were curling, turning black, and eventually sprouted white coral.\nShe inhaled repeatedly, sensing the murmurs of ancient times, the countless whispers of long-departed creatures.\nIt was a truly soft fossil.\nNervously, she began to laugh—so this is what dreaming feels like.\nShe locked herself in the studio, starting to create obsessively.\nMolding, sculpting, coloring...\nChaotic yet orderly. Inorganic yet organic.\n\nShe will forever dream."
  },
  CollectionHall_127135_Title = {
    Text = "Death of Ms. Coral"
  },
  CollectionHall_127136_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Mother. Mother.
Murphy has lost most of the memories related to her.
It is said that her dying mother protected her, blood choking in her throat.
Then people rushed forward, rudely separating them.
In that moment, Murphy saw her mother's face. That face was frantic, yet very beautiful.
After she began to remember, she had a new "mother".
Gentle and cautious, she would fulfill all of Murphy's unreasonable demands while maintaining a distance that was neither too far nor too close.
Just as Murphy thought their relationship would continue like this forever, like Miryam's unchanging expression, she was lifted high upon the dark Throne and saw the glowing "Egg" in her dreams.
It sparkled in the dark night, like an eye or a star. Ethereal songs surrounded the sanctuary:
<Italic:From the @1 of her daughter, the God descends @1...>
She was given a great mission, both related and unrelated to her: to become the mother who brings the God back to life.
How strange. She still does not understand what a mother is, what a daughter is, yet she must begin to learn to be a "mother".
Murphy recalled that frantic, beautiful face, and the sweet yet bitter taste on her tongue.
That beautiful person does not want me to fall into the grave like this, right?]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127136_Title = {
    Text = "Shrouded Birth"
  },
  CollectionHall_127137_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The exact origins of Wanda are widely debated among the locals of Cambrian.

Some say they have seen Wanda sitting on a giant stone sinking into the lakeside.
Others say she is a pharaoh from Lemmash, who he once saw with the same spine needle on a mummy.
Still, some say she is a duchess from the Franco Highlands, who inherited a vast fortune after killing her four husbands in succession.
..

Rumors blew away like the wind, and the villagers continued to farm, weave, and grind.
In those hard years, heavy taxes hung overhead like a razor, cutting off all the budding branches and illusions.
Only... whenever passing by the lake area where the queen resides, the music from the thicket easily captivated everyone's hearts.
That was a melody that shouldn't be here.
It was too pleasant, too lazy, making it seem evil, like a devil's whisper.

"Come, cast all this aside."
"Merciful king sits at the lake's center, waiting for the service of blind servants..."

So, on a windless night, the weary villagers put down their tools and decided to satisfy their curious desire to sneak away.
He circumvented the forest, crossed the small bridge, the path blooming with flowers, not a glance spared.
He saw the green lake.
It connected to the low-hanging starry sky, with an ancient castle rising at the edge.

The thorn-crowned queen sat in the center of the lake, patiently awaiting the pilgrims.
She extended her hand, enjoying the kisses and worship of mere mortals.
The dark clouds dispersed, the bright moon rose.
The queen drove the spine needle into his back.
The paralyzing liquid spread through his veins, and he knelt on the ground, dismembered and gouged of his eyes.

At this point, the heavy gravity from the earth could no longer attract him, all his poetry and dreams were solely tethered to that queen.
He finally welcomed his destiny]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127137_Title = {
    Text = "Queen's Edict"
  },
  CollectionHall_127138_Desc = {
    Text = "\"O you who walk in lifelong penance, may this gift warm your soul, may the Father's love soothe your agony, and bring you sweet, peaceful dreams.\"\n\nThe silver-frosted night neared its end, and the candlelight flickered low.\nFor the first time in a long while, Salvador set aside the heavy stone tablets.\nHe exchanged his solemn, austere robes for a warm, crimson-velvet outfit.\nIn preparation for the coming Solstice Passage, he had visited Daffodil's shop to prepare holiday surprises for the students of Mythag.\n\n\"This is the last gift box...\"\nSalvador settled quietly onto an old chair in a corner of the campus.\nExhaustion finally overtook him, and he unconsciously drifted into a deep slumber.\nIt was a sweet dream.\nThe gift box at his feet mysteriously opened—four gingerbread girls leaped out, their frosting-dotted eyes shining brightly.\nThe scents of cinnamon and clove whirled in a circle in the cold air.\nThat fragrance stirred long-buried memories.\nHe found himself once more in the cathedral cloisters of his childhood, the melting toffee on his tongue sending quiet signals of sweetness.\nAll the blessings once tainted by suffering and plague now quietly awakened, twirling softly to the rhythm of this sugary waltz.\n\nMeanwhile, four sneaky little figures crept toward the sleeping Salvador.\n\"Master... will Master think we are naughty...?\"\n\"Hehe... Aurita's getting so, so curious! Hurry, open it! One, two... wow, so many gingerbread cookies!\"\n\"You, you said your name out loud...! What if... people are gonna hate us...!\"\n\"Then we can just push it on Brown! We're good girls! Didn't do anything!\"\n\nSalvador heard the little gingerbread girls chattering, and felt one of them hop onto his lap, the distinct scent of cinnamon brushing against his wrinkled hand.\nHe realized with a gentle jolt that these were not the phantom sweets of his dream, but the mischievous children of reality.\nHe could easily imagine their happy, glowing faces as they snuck open the gift box.\nFor this moment of beauty, happiness, and peace, he was willing to bear any pain.\n\n\"Oh... my beard, are they tying it to my hair?\"\n\nSalvador pretended to remain fast asleep, allowing the children to continue their joyful \"secret mission.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_127138_Title = {
    Text = "Dear Papa Noel"
  },
  CollectionHall_127139_Desc = {
    Text = "You and Ramona couldn't promise to meet again.\nAs the Gate slowly closed, the temporary farewell you'd envisioned in your hearts solidified into an inevitable eternity.\n\nSo, when she lightly hooked your little finger in those final, fleeting moments...\nit was already an unexpected and fortunate reunion.\n\n\"You haven't changed at all,\" she says.\n\nFor these words—for the faint warmth of her fingertip—you would give everything to leap across the galaxy and meet her, even across two worlds.\n\nNext year on this day, you vow with a pinky promise."
  },
  CollectionHall_127139_Title = {
    Text = "We Will Meet Again"
  },
  CollectionHall_127140_Desc = {
    Text = "\"Retreat, retreat!\"\n\"Retreat to @3! Move quickly!\"\n\"Help, help me! Don't abandon me!\"\n\"Leave him behind, retreat now—Alva!\"\nThe soldier wielding the gunblade surged forward, explosions erupting around her, blending with the clamor of battle, screams, and the blaring war horn. Blood drenched the earth, its stench overpowering even the smell of gunpowder. Lifeless soldiers lay scattered, their uniforms dyed a vivid red regardless of their original colors.\nAlva clenched her teeth, pushing forward against the relentless onslaught of enemies. She spotted him—a young man crying for help, pinned to the ground, desperately fending off a towering enemy's dagger.\nA deafening gunshot and searing pain struck simultaneously; the nearby enemy collapsed slowly. Alva spun around and slashed, enduring the agony in her leg as she lunged forward, driving her blade into her opponent's chest and pulling the trigger.\nBlood sprayed everywhere; she hastily wiped her face, only to realize the young man was gone.\nShe glanced down—a knife protruded from her left knee, blood gushing out.\nTearing a strip of cloth from her cloak to staunch the bleeding, she used her gunblade as a makeshift crutch and limped after her unit."
  },
  CollectionHall_127140_Title = {
    Text = "Will Unyielding"
  },
  CollectionHall_127141_Desc = {
    Text = [[
History has always been a one-sided narrative of the victors; the Mother Tree perished, nations fell, and everything about the past is quietly changing.
The poet sings the tale of the Nineveh beauty, while travelers gather around the campfire to listen intently.

"Traversing the silver desert, the foreign beauty intruded upon Nineveh.
The waters of the Milky Way slipped from her shoulders, Sinai pearls fell from her eyes.
In her golden pupils, gazing at the past of another land.
Upon her honey-colored skin, the future of Nineveh is inscribed."

And then? Did this beauty become a queen?
The aged poet plucks the strings of his seven-stringed lute, releasing a long sigh.

"She is a soporific, causing all beings to fall under her spell.
She is a poison, penetrating the lungs of kings and ministers.
She is a flood, from which no one can escape.
She is the harbinger of the black plague, bringing illness, nightmares, death, and the end of Nineveh."

Before the lute is set down, a figure stands up from the table, drawing the attention of the patrons.
The slender fingers of that person let slip some coins for wine, gold and silver rolling and clinking.
Wherever she goes, gazes follow, lights flicker.

"Time is fleeting... but it matters not, He will not respond to these nonsensical words.
One day, you will understand His mercy and generosity... just as I do..."
She pushes open the worn little door of the tavern, like opening a jewel box, moonlight falling on her bare shoulders, reflecting a scintillating glow.
The beauty, basked in moonlight, indeed has skin as sweet as honey.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127141_Title = {
    Text = "Merciful Nurturing"
  },
  CollectionHall_127142_Desc = {
    Text = [[
When she opened her eyes in the greenhouse, the fire had already engulfed the entire garden, coming right before her.
The door of the greenhouse was locked from the outside, and the strong smell of alcohol and grease filled the air. She called out loudly for Colette's name until her voice was hoarse from the smoke, and all that responded to her was the roaring of the flames.
She felt relieved. Fortunately, Colette had gone out; otherwise, with such a large fire, she would also be in danger.
She felt sad. In her last moments of life, she couldn't see her best friend one last time. When Colette returned and saw the burned garden and herself, she would surely be very sad, right?
She felt regret. Their lives were just getting better, but this fire would put an end to them.
Burning. The house is burning. The sky is burning. The leaves are burning. The petals are burning. The scenes experienced in the garden play out and flow before her: she brought her to the garden, she handed her a rose, she brought her soft bread after a day's toil. They frolicked, chased, lay under the tranquil sunlight, dreaming of the day they would move into the Countess's room.
Burning. The past is burning. The future is burning. The garden, with all its stories and emotions, burns fiercely.
Tears slid down her face, quickly disappearing under the scorching flames.
She felt beauty. In poetry, pain and regret are beautiful. She searched around and found the paper and pen that had been almost entirely consumed by the flames.
Gratitude, affection, reluctance, blessing, beauty. She wanted to leave this most beautiful everything to Colette.
"...To Colette. Horla, in the fire."
At the end of the poem, she left her final signature.
A hundred meters away, on the road opposite the garden, Colette seemed to sense something. She looked up, the fierce flames reflecting on her face.
Tears slid down her face, quickly disappearing under the scorching flames.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127142_Title = {
    Text = "The Last Verse"
  },
  CollectionHall_127143_Desc = {
    Text = "They rowed through the dark river—pale, silent, exhausted.\n\nA hazy mist stretched out its tendrils and pulled them into the darkness, leaving them to wander an endless night.\n\nThen, they saw a beam of light.\n\nIt was the dawn light from a distant shore, flickering, yet bright enough to reach their dim souls.\n\nSo they followed it, rowing clumsily through the dark, until they reached the break of dawn;\n\nuntil they stood before you.\n\n\nPerhaps this is just a fleeting encounter, but they wave and shout with all they have.\nEveryone is bathed in the sacred light.\nEveryone is smiling.\n\nThey say—\n\nMay every gathering be cherished like a feast.\nMay sincere hearts never cease to beat.\nMay the Silver Key light our path."
  },
  CollectionHall_127143_Title = {
    Text = "Dusk and Dawn"
  },
  CollectionHall_127144_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Wind surges from all directions as you stand at the entrance of the maze with a candle in hand.

You feel a bit lost.

It seems that just a moment ago, you were in Mythag's cafeteria, listening to Charlotte tell tales about the library's underground maze.

And now, you are wandering through one passageway after another in your pajamas, bleary-eyed.

"Charlotte, Charlotte..."

A rustling fills the air as white spiders pour in like a tide, coalescing into a pale girl.

She sits on a swing fashioned from chunks of flesh, swinging back and forth.

"Here you are," she says.

"I'm looking for my friend, Charlotte.
She got lost, and I have to find her..."
You are on the brink of tears.

The girl giggles.
She jumps off the swing and steps toward you.

"Don't you remember? Our deal..."
She places her hand on your belly, then her eyes light up as if she suddenly realizes something.

"Oh, right. You've already become my offspring, so you don't remember anything."

"Offspring...?" 
You look down and feel where your skins touch.

The warm sensation, like spider silk, burrows beneath your skin and threads its way deep into veins.

The girl gives a sly blink and leans close, whispering in your ear:
"Charlotte... is right inside you."]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127144_Title = {
    Text = "Pale Descendant"
  },
  CollectionHall_127145_Desc = {
    Text = "On a grand stage, a young girl is dancing.\nHer hair is tightly coiled into a bun, adorned with white feathers and a delicate crown. Her pure white dress flares out with her movements, twirling gracefully to the mournful sound of violins.\nWith arms extended and toes pointed, the white swan lowers its neck, sharing its sorrow and grief with the prince.\nYoung Liz watches with her mouth slightly open, captivated by the graceful figure on stage. That dancer is her cousin, who came to live with them before Liz was born and trained rigorously under their grandmother. Usually plain and quiet, her cousin has never appeared so vibrant, like a swan ready to take flight. She, along with everyone else in the theater, is entranced by her cousin's Shadow.\nLiz's heart beats faster and faster—how enviable! She too wants to be that swan, to leave her mark on the eternal stage. She knows she can do it. Didn't her grandmother praise her long, straight legs when she thought Liz wasn't listening? Didn't her cousin, the former prima ballerina, say she had great potential? Yes, once she starts, once she puts on those pointe shoes, people will come from distant cities to watch her perform. She will be the greatest dancer of this century, a shining star in the world of ballet!\nAt that time, she didn't know the only thing awaiting her was scorching flames."
  },
  CollectionHall_127145_Title = {Text = "Fouetté"},
  CollectionHall_127146_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A year has passed since you first arrived at Mythag.

The memory of that initial day remains vivid, stepping into the halls of this ancient school still dazed from the aftermath of that cataclysmic explosion.

You were given a uniform that fit as though tailored by fate itself, and a dorm room that slowly became a sanctuary.

That first visit to the cafeteria, devouring two towering stacks of plates, feels both like yesterday and another lifetime.


Those effortless days ended abruptly.

Soon enough, it became clear that your knowledge was meager, your mind as untrained as a newborn's.

You were assigned to a year of preparatory classes: language drills, grueling physical training, Silver ability assessments, and intense lessons in special biology.

You endured it all, with mixed results.


You failed your Standard Leonian language class spectacularly, but you also achieved the extraordinary by linking with three Awakeners at once.

Overnight, you became something of a legend on campus.

Yet it was your raw, peculiar talent that ultimately saved you, propelling you past the threshold to become a full Investigator and sparing you another year in preparatory limbo.


Your weaknesses, jagged and undeniable, were slowly softened, covered by the growing trust and skill of your teammates.

Ah, your team; devils, perhaps, but reliable and gentle ones.


This place, often shrouded in mist and frequent rain, where sunlight is a rare gift, is home to countless souls; some forgotten, some soon to be.

Yet they persist.

They sacrifice.

They move forward.


On just such an ordinary, cloud-threaded day, Mythag welcomes another School Day.

You stand before the mirror, adjusting your collar, smoothing each wrinkle into place.

Then you push open the heavy door of the dormitory.


"Yawn.

Finally here.

I was almost asleep."

"What were you doing, hatching in your room?

Studying, freshman?"


You offer a sheepish chuckle to Lotan, shrink reflexively from the pink-clad figure that stirs a primal unease, and take shelter behind the calm presence of Ramona and Ogier, already smiling in quiet amusement.

Five shadows lengthen and sway in the pale morning light.


"Let's go, partner."

"From today, you are truly a part of Mythag."]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127146_Title = {Text = "School Day"},
  CollectionHall_127147_Desc = {
    Text = "Follow the Taym downstream, turn right onto Beckman Street, walk about a hundred feet, and you'll find the \"Ryker Detective Agency\" tucked in an unassuming corner.\n\nDespite being Londinium's most successful detective agency, it has no bookshelves crammed with professional tomes, no walls plastered with clippings, and certainly no elegant afternoon tea.\n\nMost likely, you'll only find an \"Back Soon\" sign on the door and a tired old dog curled up beside it.\n\nIf you're lucky, on a clear Sunday morning, you might catch the famous detective returning from a night of drinking.\nHe is fresh from a gambling table, his pockets nearly empty, and that's when you can throw him any requests: finding a lost cat, rescuing a mother who joined a cult, gathering evidence of an affair...\nIf you've got the fee, he'll take the case.\n\n\"I enjoy those moments right before death, and that's why I was born to be a gambler.\"\n\"And a detective? I must say, I don't see how finding a cat relates to dying.\"\n\"No, you don't get it... The search for truth is captivating in itself—big case or small. It's like...\" \n\"Like heading to a date with death.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_127147_Title = {
    Text = "Hour of Fortune"
  },
  CollectionHall_127148_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Pollux dreamed.


He was clad in silver armour, receiving a sword, smooth as moonlight, from the hands of a majestic king.

He mounted a tall white horse and galloped into a cavern, the trees at its mouth whispering as he plunged underground.


In the depths lurked a shadow, dark green and monstrous, a mountain of flesh with strange, glowing eyes.


"Creature that harms the kingdom," Pollux declared, "I cannot suffer you to threaten our sacred realm. Today, this blade of justice will end you."


The monstrous mountain shuddered, answering with a terrifying roar.

Pollux did not understand its language, nor did he care to.

He raised the sword and fought the evil-tinged thing.

Its tentacles writhed in the dimness, clashing against the radiant blade with a sound like a cracked bell.


And as in every hero's tale, the brave knight mounted the creature's back and, with a fierce cry, drove the sword deep into its chest.


The monster collapsed.

Pollux, breathless, stared at the mark spreading beneath the blade.

How could such a warm, bright red blood flow from something so ugly and evil?


He woke suddenly. The sticky sensation of blood on his hands seemed impossible to scrub away.

From the corner of his eye, he saw the old book Castor cherished, hidden in a gap behind the bed.


He flipped through it idly, the pages falling open to the knight's tale Castor loved so.

There, in the centre of the page, was a prophecy:


*When the evil monster is defeated by the warrior, all will see a vision in the sky; the sun will turn to darkness, and the moon to blood.*


Pollux frowned and tossed the book back into its hiding place with disdain.

Beneath the moonlight, he murmured a prayer.


"The Light's servant is sent here to bless you, to cleanse you of your sins, to return from darkness to light, and to join all pure and righteous souls in the promised land..."


But the Lightbearer offered no comfort to his devout squire.

The nightmare's unease still trembled in his heart, where his slumbering soul wept silently.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127148_Title = {
    Text = "Twisted Knight Ballad"
  },
  CollectionHall_127149_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Bold:January 24>
I smell terrible.
Today, while riding home with Teresa the housekeeper, we passed through the South Anpus District.
It was not a pleasant experience.
It's a dangerous place. Some people have strange wounds, like triangular holes.
Teresa the housekeeper says it's the punishment from the Arrival for the heretics.

<Bold:February 22>
I've had a fever for a month.
Finally, I ate something today. Fresh steak, tender, juicy...
Yes, juicy.
Red, sweet, and delicious.
All the mirrors at home have been removed, and even Bobby doesn't dare look at me.
Hehe. They don't know that at night, I can see my reflection in the window's shadow.
On my face, neck, chest... from top to bottom, densely packed,
grown with black triangles.

<Bold:March 17>
My cornea feels as if covered with a red veil.
The world turned the color of blood.
Father yelled at me from within the blood mist, the first time he spoke to me so loudly.
He was close, but his voice was distant. I smelled despair, disgust, and blood.
Do not take me away, do not...]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127149_Title = {
    Text = "The Glutton's Tale"
  },
  CollectionHall_127150_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The Erivinian people reside in the gray stone city, adjacent to a green lake. 

The lake has no name; it has existed here since the Erivinians have memory. 
It is said that an evil hag is sealed deep within the waters of the lake. 
She is as ancient as the lake, a terrifying existence crudely shaped at the dawn of creation. 
Naive and timid, the Erivinians fear the hag, attempting to appease her to ensure she remains quietly at the bottom of the lake. 

"What should we do?" 
"Yes, what should we do?" 
"Then let's dance! Dancing is always good, after all." 

Thus, on every full moon, the Erivinians gather by the lake to dance gracefully before a paper effigy. 
In those moments, with the moon shining bright and the stars sparse, all is peaceful. 

Hundreds of years later, the Erivinians forget their history, forget their fables, and forget their effigies. 
During the millennium celebration of the stone city, they indulge in raucous laughter and drink fine wine. 
The noisy sounds are cast into the lake, like stones hitting water, spreading in endless circles from the center of the lake, ultimately reaching the depths. 
Thus, on a full moon, the Erivinians hear sounds beyond the range of their hearing and see the moon and flames beyond the range of their vision. 
They also become a part of the silence. 

This infinite silence within endless space fills the Erivinians with fear. 
They are forced to sit still like mystics, watching a new tribe laugh and drink in exuberance before them, coming and going in cycles. 
So the universe will continue to expand forever, the galaxies will drift further apart, and all things will perish. 
That's just how it is. 
Whether the Erivinians feel lonely about this is of no importance.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127150_Title = {
    Text = "Silent Banquet"
  },
  CollectionHall_127151_Desc = {
    Text = "The girl opens her eyes to find herself in darkness.\n\"Hey!\" she shouts, \"Is anyone there?\"\nThe echo wavers and fades in the space with no visible boundaries as she takes a deep breath and shouts again, \"Sister, Brown, Westie!\"\n\"Is anyone there—\"\nA louder question than before drifts away and slowly returns. A few strands of bluish light seem to be drawn in by the echo from afar, formed by countless hovering, dust-like particles, winding through the air like serpents, rising and falling like waves. A continuous stream of light passes by the girl standing still, quickly turning the entire realm into a sea of stars, the tiny particles swishing through the girl's fingers and hair, leaving no trace.\n\"What is this...?\"\nThe glowing dust undulates slightly around her, offering no response.\n\"I remember the wax museum, I remember my sister, I... seem to have died. Is this heaven?\" She looks around, \"Why is there not even an angel here? It can't be hell, can it!\"\nHer voice falls beside her ear, and this time, even the echo does not appear again.\nAn inexplicable sense of loneliness arises from deep within her heart, and in a daze, she feels as if she has returned to before she met her sister and Brown. The foul odor from the dark sewer permeates, she is cold and hungry, yet unable to leave because someone pushed her down and a large barrel pressed down on top of the sewer.\nShe slaps her face and steps forward.\nThe dust parts in front of her, then gathers behind her. Lift a leg, set it down, lift a leg, set it down. She keeps walking and walking, unsure how long she has been walking or how far. Ahead of her are more dust and darkness, and behind her, whether the direction she came from or the path she had walked, has already left no trace until —\n\"Awake succeeded, Jenkin, Jenkin, can you hear me?\""
  },
  CollectionHall_127151_Title = {
    Text = "Path Forsaken"
  },
  CollectionHall_127152_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The Father of All Beginnings came from gulfs beyond the stars. 
His feet trod upon the flames, and He spoke, "Let the fire fade."
The molten earth grew still, and upon its face, the Father inscribed the First Law: 
"Let the land be the bedrock of existence."
Thus were the valleys cloven, and the plains unfurled vast. 
And the Word was wrought in stone, the First Tablet decreed.

Then the All-Father turned His gaze unto the burdened clouds, and He proclaimed: "Let the clouds pour forth weeping."
The waters amassed, and upon them He carved the Second Law: 
"Let the waters be the cradle of being."
And the waters begat lakes, and lakes swelled into seas, and the seas consumed the margins of the earth. 
And the Word was wrought in stone, the Second Tablet anointed.

Then the All-Father beheld the waters, black and voiceless, and He intoned: "Let there be light."
Light burst forth, and upon it He carved the Third Law: 
"Let the light sustain."
And warmth stole across the depths unplumbed. 
And the Word was wrought in stone, the Third Tablet consecrated.

Then the All-Father saw earth, water, and light forged, and He declared: 
"Let life awaken."
He let fall His blood, and upon it He carved the Fourth Law: 
"Let the blood hasten life."
And His blood rained upon the waters, and the deep teemed with life.
And the Word was wrought in stone, the Fourth Tablet Exalted.

Then the All-Father saw life take root, and He spake: 
"Let life transmute without end."
Minute beings crept upon the land where waters receded, and upon them He carved the Sixth Law: 
"Change shall not slumber."
And they waxed in roots, in limbs, in forms manifold.
And the Word was wrought in stone, the Sixth Tablet sealed.

Then the All-Father saw life and change abound, and He ordained: "Let death also descend." And death arose. 
The hoary and feeble faded, and upon them He carved the Fifth Law: 
"The dead shall return unto the genesis."
And their flesh melted, drawn back to the All-Father's unseen fold. 
And the Word was wrought in stone, the Fifth Tablet inscribed.

Then the All-Father beheld life, death, and change entwined, and He spake: 
"These are My deeds, and I shall grant a boon."
He took of His own bone, and upon it He carved the Seventh Law: 
"At the end of all, My bone shall hold My dominion. Let flesh be the cost, and life be rekindled."
And the Word was wrought in stone, the Seventh Tablet hallowed.

And the All-Father looked upon all He had shaped, and He reposed.
The waters enwrapped Him, the light lent Him solace, the earth veiled Him.
And the All-Father slumbered. All things endure by His Word.
So it standeth, even unto this age.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127152_Title = {
    Text = "Tablet of Scriptures"
  },
  CollectionHall_127153_Desc = {
    Text = [[
He is the king who knows all, the supreme ruler of Lemuria.

Lapis Lazuli serves as his throne, gold as his crown. Souls are his scepter, and he rests at the pinnacle.

Priests who serve the gods also serve him, kneeling before him,

loyal subjects and devout believers.


At night, the gods send moonlight, inviting him to the eternal palace,

where they share the food of souls, bestowing upon him divine wisdom.

Endless dreams allow him to witness the beginning of all things and the end of time.

He has learned: All beginnings stem from chaos; the gods awoke and built floating palaces in the darkness.

He has learned: The end of time is darkness, and all returns to chaos.


King of kings, beloved of the gods,

Who can compare to you?

Who commands in dreams as you do, wielding your majesty?

Noble god-king, youthful sovereign,

Sleep soundly.

Your subjects and followers will patiently await your return, bringing back the prophecy of the gods.

Respected ruler of the Nereids, master of the abyss,

Let us call upon your name and grant us protection,

Tulu, Tulu.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127153_Title = {
    Text = "Hymn of the Sovereign"
  },
  CollectionHall_127154_Desc = {
    Text = [[
For years, I have been thinking about Uvhash.
But it was only among the ruins of these temples that I truly saw him for the first time.
I saw him bound by heavy shackles, forced to lie on the ground, stretching his neck to desperately reach the already spoiled food.
Like a dog.

After Caligula died, as a co-conspirator of the tyrant, he has been locked in the ruins of the temple ever since.
I dragged the chains in my hand, bringing a slave of Torres forward.
He immediately stood upright, his pupils dilating, making a rapid swallowing sound in his throat.

"Wait."
I pulled the chain, bringing the slave to a distance just out of his reach.
"Help me kill someone."
He grinned, revealing a row of sharp beast teeth.
"You are the 19th human to say that to me, and I have to refuse you."
I struggled to keep a straight face, not letting him see my disappointment:
"Why?"
"If you want me to kill a thousand people, I would be more than happy. Killing one? Your bargaining chip is far from enough."
"What if that person is the current emperor?"
I took a deep breath.
"Is this bargaining chip enough?"
Uvhash laughed heartily:
"This is a math problem, my old buddy. One is one, a thousand is a thousand."

"Fire! The Golden Palace is on fire!"
In the distance, roaring flames erupted.
Tyrant, tyrant......
I cried in despair, for Seneca and for the magnificent palace that was about to become ruins.
"Are you that sad?"
Uvhash leaned closer.
He had already enjoyed that Torres slave, satisfying himself as he smacked his lips.
Yes, I promised him that as long as he could kill the tyrant, besides freedom, he could also enjoy a thousand innocent lives.
Could he understand what this fire meant?
Could he understand what it meant to serve an irredeemable tyrant?
Probably not.
He's just a beast.

"Rome is like a ruin," the beast said.
"Or rather, your country, the world......
In my view, it is a meaningless and endless ruin.
You weep for it, kill each other, doing everything futile and pointless......
To be honest, I don't understand."

I looked at his battered body.
This is a golem forged from millions of flesh and blood, shattered and reassembled over the hundreds of years, just like Rome.
"What about you? Are you also a ruin?"
"Perhaps." 
He stretched lazily, golden light from afar danced in his narrow eyes.
"But I don't care."]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127154_Title = {
    Text = "Bloody Feast"
  },
  CollectionHall_127155_Desc = {
    Text = [[
O Master of Lemuria, hear my prayer.

Grant me your prophecy, bestow your insight,

So I may restore your kingdom.

In this faithless land, upon this ice-field ringed by sea,

Erect your pillars, and build your temple.


O Master of Abyss, receive these offerings.

Pure flesh from a full-moon lamb, a strong heart from a grown bull,

Sharp eyes from a soaring eagle, and hard bones from a cruising whale.

Lapis is your throne, gold your crown,

Grant me your dream, tell me your divine words,

So I may restore your form.

In the abyss under the ice, in the realm beneath the waves,

I offer the mother born at the right time.


O All-knowing King of Lemuria, please answer my prayer.

Centuries have passed since you descended into your long slumber.

In your name I act, and your glory I proclaim, never ceasing.

My faith is firm, my heart devout.

You are the only Godking, the embodiment of immortality.

May you end my wait, return to the world, and let me hear your words of wisdom.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127155_Title = {
    Text = "Power of the Pious"
  },
  CollectionHall_127156_Desc = {
    Text = "When Aurita was born, the impact of the great flood on the city had completely faded, but in the remote towns, people were still struggling to survive.\n\nThe flood made people begin to fear the sea and rivers; those who could leave had already departed, and those who remain in this small fishing village are mostly women and children who find it difficult to establish themselves elsewhere.\nIn this dull and quiet place, Aurita is the only child.\n\nShe stubbornly believes in the fairy tales her grandmother told her—that her parents have returned to the sea, waiting for Aurita to grow up. Once she grows up, they will all be reunited and become a happy family again.\n\nWhen she was still unable to speak, it felt as if she had once slept in a warm embrace, but Aurita can no longer remember many things about her parents.\nHowever, as a child who grew up in a silent place, Aurita does not understand \"loneliness\" or \"desolation\"; she has her own group of friends.\n\nUnlike those adults who were terrified by the flood, Aurita has never feared the sea.\nAs a resident of the Ocean King's domain, she naturally has to befriend the sea.\nAurita learns to play with the \"locals\".\nShe mimics the way clams move and dances, learning from clownfish as they swim through the seagrass.\nShe lies on the shellback of a leatherback turtle, drifting away from the land with the waves.\nIn the sea, bathed in moonlight, she plays with a swarm of jellyfish.\n\nShe is joy, she is imagination, she is a sprite.\n\nShe is a dream.\n"
  },
  CollectionHall_127156_Title = {
    Text = "Dream of the Sea"
  },
  CollectionHall_127157_Desc = {
    Text = "A countryside village girl wearing an extravagant gown, gold and silver jewelry, and a feather fan sneaks into the world of the elite...\nNothing could be more improper than this. A person of lower status trespassing into our ranks is simply scandalous...!\nI say, there should be mandatory identification badges indicating their status, so they are not mistaken for one of us.\n—Duke Philip Harold\n\nIf you live in Londinium, you must be familiar with the so-called \"Sorel Effect.\" \nStill worried that your clothes won't sell? You'd better pray you have some connections to gain the favor of Lady Sorel—yes, even a ridiculously silly pig-tail dress hat, if placed on Lady Sorel's head, will sell like hotcakes.\nShe is the pop idol of the new era.\n—\"The Fame Quiz of Lady Sorel,\" The Lady's Guide\n\nIt was a clear summer night.\nWe sat together on the marble-paved terrace, sipping aged noble botrytis wine, discussing poetry and world peace.\nAnd then something happened @4\nGet to the point? Ahem, my apologies...\nIn short, this woman cheated me out of three thousand Leo Fang, two properties in Soreland, and a sincere heart!\n—A heartbroken viscount who wishes to remain anonymous"
  },
  CollectionHall_127157_Title = {
    Text = "By Rose Alone"
  },
  CollectionHall_127158_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Separate. Experience. Flood in. Invade.

Scholars have long debated the true meaning of the Semitic root "p-l-sh" among the Perishites.
For the first time in his life, Goliath felt that these old scholars possessed some genuine insight, for these four brief words almost encapsulated his life as a Perishite.

The Perishites are indeed a maritime people.
They are like schools of long-tailed sharks, drawn to inhabitable islands by the scent of blood, then slaughtering all the natives there.

The Perishites never tire.
They never linger; when everything settles, their restless instincts drive them to move on, seeking new prey.

The Perishites don't care about tomorrow.
They squander their plundered wealth at an astonishing speed, drinking the last drop of wine, then breeding, fighting, and betraying with reckless abandon...

As they set sail, Goliath looked back at the trail left by the ships on the sea.
The blood of the Perishites, the blood of the natives, the blood of enemies, the blood of seabirds...
It merged into one, like dark red ink spilling into an endless blue.

The next day, the sun rose as usual, the sea shimmered like countless shards of broken gold, and everything vanished without a trace.
They were in the ocean, yet the ocean had forgotten them.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127158_Title = {
    Text = "Blade of the Titan"
  },
  CollectionHall_127159_Desc = {
    Text = "In Cathuria, legends tell of a sunken civilization.\n\nIt is said that before recorded history, an abnormal shift in the stars caused a prehistoric civilization to sink beneath the sea, and the Cathurians are its descendants.\nAside from trading and fishing, one major reason Cathurians venture into the sea is to search for their lost ancestral civilization.\nThey believe that girls born under specific star alignments can sense this ancient civilization, guiding them to its location and protecting the fleet from storms.\n\nCeleste was chosen for this purpose.\nBound to the mast of a ship with white sails, she watched the people below bustling about.\nShe felt neither interest nor curiosity.\n\nCeleste could sense the weather at sea through the wind and birds, and sometimes even catch a faint trace of the distant sunken land.\nShe felt as though she belonged to the sea and the ship—often thinking that her captivity did not stir any emotion within her.\nSometimes she would leave the mast, chasing the white birds flying across the sky, with the ship closely following her.\nThe people believed that the girl symbolized safe voyages, bringing blessings to ships so they could return safely laden with wealth and advanced knowledge.\nBut she knew nothing of this."
  },
  CollectionHall_127159_Title = {
    Text = "Sail of Providence"
  },
  CollectionHall_127160_Desc = {
    Text = "Tap, tap, tap.\nFootsteps approach. A gentleman in a top hat walks through the ruins, standing before a dying guard.\nGentleman: What are you doing here?\n\n(The gentleman suffers from severe stuttering, while the guard likes to beat around the bush. For your reading convenience, only the key points of the conversation are recorded.)\n\nGuard: I'm guarding the prison.\nThe gentleman looked around the deserted field and the slowly collapsing ruins tainted with dissolution.\nGentleman: But there is no prison here, nor prisoners. Your kingdom no longer exists.\nGuard: I'm guarding the prison.\nGentleman: Why?\nThe guard lifted her head, a childlike face filled with confusion and determination.\nGuard: I don't know... I want to go home.\nGuard: I'm guarding the prison for that lord. If the lord is pleased, I can go home.\nShe doesn't even know who that lord is or why she should guard it.\nThe gentleman doesn't ask further, as if it were the most natural thing.\nGentleman: What is your hometown like?\nGuard: It's only winter and night there, with endless forests and seas.\nGentleman: Doesn't sound livable.\nGuard: I hate daylight. Do you see? I'm made of wax. If I touch the sun, I will disappear.\nGuard: So I hide here, unable to go home by myself.\nThe gentleman nods thoughtfully. Suddenly, he becomes excited.\nGentleman: What a coincidence! You're made of wax, and I happen to be a wax sculptor.\nGentleman: Let's make a pact—I can let you walk in daylight and help you find your way home. In return, you will be my assistant.\nGuard: Assistant, what's that?\nGentleman: You can guard my wax museum for me. It's different from this prison; it's art, and art never collapses.\nGuard: Is art that powerful?\nThe gentleman laughs happily.\nGentleman: Yes, it is that powerful.\n\nAt the end of the story, the guard followed the gentleman muddleheadedly, just as she had come to this prison muddleheadedly.\nShe has always been someone who goes with the flow."
  },
  CollectionHall_127160_Title = {
    Text = "Drifting in Desire"
  },
  CollectionHall_127161_Desc = {
    Text = [[
You step onto a barren, lifeless wasteland.

All traces of humanity have long vanished. Withered souls trudge through ash and smog, barely clinging to breath.

Survival here is no triumph. 
No one knows where the journey ends. They wander, and wander, and wander still, trapped in an eternal loop of desolation.

Until their steps falter, and they collapse onto the scorched earth, eyes turned skyward, hands reaching out to plead:

May my journey's end become a new beginning.

Let these bones be soil, be sustenance, be spring, so that fragile shoots may rise again through dust.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127161_Title = {
    Text = "Annihilated Rebirth"
  },
  CollectionHall_127162_Desc = {
    Text = [[
She once questioned countless times in the dead of night: Why must she endure this endless pain?
No one answered.
Her hoarse whispers turned into fragments, never reaching the ears of any god.
Her pain festered, turning into pus and brewing deeper hatred.
One day, she noticed black liquid oozing from the people around her, resembling her own blood.
They quickly descended into madness, just like her.
Perhaps it was their pain; she watched coldly, feeling a faint sense of satisfaction.
But if that was pain, hadn't she long been consumed by the darkness?
She approached the lingering blackness and unexpectedly found freedom.
Yet the freedom brought no relief; she was like a demon exiled to Hell for millennia, her desires corroded by hatred.
Her body bound in shackles, her soul weighed down by lead.
Only the eerie screams could cleanse her heavy soul, allowing her to breathe freely.
Come, taste what I have tasted, and become me.
She found red to be a marvelous color.
She finally understood: Pain has no reason.
Either drink it yourself or invite others to share.
Tonight, she poured the bitter wine, inviting the entire town.
]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127162_Title = {
    Text = "Drowning in Crimson"
  },
  CollectionHall_127163_Desc = {
    Text = "My boat was tightly entwined by something; the propeller struggled strenuously, making terrifying sounds.\nCumulonimbus clouds gathered above us, with lightning surging through the dark clouds.\nThe moment a thunderbolt struck the mast, the propeller broke free and started spinning again.\nI sighed with relief, but the chief engineer began to scream.\n\nA viscous liquid mixed into the seawater, and in the wild storm outside, the smell was carried away by the wind, leaving only the scent of death in my nose.\nBut I realized that the glowing liquid was some kind of blood.\nMy dearest companion, my most trusted ship, gave her all before sinking—her blades, which should have sliced through the water, had severed the monster's tentacles.\n\nThis is a good omen! We'll soon be out of the storm!\nI was about to comfort my crew with this thought when, as I looked up, a light appeared in the center of the dark sea.\nA lighthouse? How could it be? No, impossible.\nWe're in the middle of the ocean. The nearest land is hundreds of miles away. How could anyone build a lighthouse here?\n\nMy sailors began to cry, pray, and sing songs of home in unison.\nThen, the lighthouse abruptly went out.\nAll light vanished, and the roaring storm turned into a drizzle on the deck.\nThe sailors praised the merciful Lord, immersed in the joy of surviving the ordeal.\nBut I saw it clearly.\n\nThe figure that disappeared in the light was indeed a graceful woman."
  },
  CollectionHall_127163_Title = {
    Text = "Amidst the Downpour"
  },
  CollectionHall_127164_Desc = {
    Text = [[
When the hero finally concludes his grand journey, and people close the last page of the picture book and drift off to sleep.

As the long night falls, Helot's story begins.

She travels north along the lengthy coastline, crossing streams and scaling mountains, until she reaches the edge of the frigid land.
Years have passed since the shocking rebellion, where Helot brought peace and prosperity wherever she went. A delicate balance was maintained between slaves and masters, making violent rebellion seem awkward and ridiculous.
She was questioned, mocked, and eventually forgotten.
But she never defended herself.

The warrior Helot came and went like the wind, planting the seeds of freedom in the heart of the Mare Internum. Five years, ten years, a hundred years...
One day, they will break through the soil and flourish.

No one knows where this Spartan killer was laid to rest, though it is said her old friend Epaminondas took care of her remains.
Years later, if you pass by a jasmine-covered grassy knoll, you might see a small tombstone that reads:

Under this grass lies a warrior, or rather,
She once was a warrior.
She is the daughter of old Pericles and the pride of Tilos.
Poet Thracius praised her battle prowess.
And the dark-haired Spartans knew her achievements better.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127164_Title = {
    Text = "Chains Unbound"
  },
  CollectionHall_127165_Desc = {
    Text = "A.F.@1/@1/@2\n\n08:00\n\nAssemble parts numbered 107 to 133.\n\nC-type components just need this final adjustment, and once completed, they'll be used as the energy core for the automaton \"Tick-tock Man.\" \n\nI wanted to assemble it personally, but @2 said the supervisor needs to learn to trust their coworkers.\n\nHow shameless! It's obviously her who checks the parts until midnight.\n\n-------\n\nA.F.@1/@1/@2\n\n00:21\n\nThe MF311000 motor has been assembled; the gears fit, and the pipes flow freely. Currently, all skills are functioning normally. Final adjustments are about to commence.\n\n13:07\n\nSpecial energy S has been connected. The MF311000 motor is running well and fits perfectly with the EA307850 artificial body, which is functioning normally.\n\n@2 is quite optimistic. She thinks we can go farther this time than before. I reminded her not to forget what happened during the fifth awakening attempt, and she just plugged her ears and said she couldn't hear. If I hadn't reacted quickly then, the flames from the self-igniting energy core would have scorched her hair.\n\nShe really should experience the feeling of being bald—maybe that way, she'd learn to be cautious.\n\n-------\n\nA.F.@1/@1/@2\n\n14:55\n\nFinal preparations completed. Energy ready. Containment device activated. Containment state: good. The torso will be installed after awakening is completed.\n\n15:00\n\nCommenced the 13th activation attempt of \"Tick-tock Man.\" \n\n15:05\n\nThe torso EA307853 is operating normally, and the MF311000 motor is functioning correctly. The neck joint of \"Tick-tock Man\" is moving well, and the head components are operating normally.\n\n15:15\n\n\"Tick-tock Man\" successfully executed blinking, gaze-following, and mouth-opening commands. The motor exhibits a heating phenomenon, but it remains within acceptable limits.\n\nPreparing to install the limbs. May the heavens bless us for success this time.\n\n18:07\n\nWhile executing walking commands, the motor core melted, and the circuits burned out. Special energy S remained intact.\n\n@2 is very protective of this special energy. Even I am forbidden to touch it. I think I can understand—it truly is a mysterious object. It looks just like ordinary metallic silver and doesn't seem capable of energy storage, yet it can power the automaton, and such high temperatures haven't damaged it. It's simply incredible.\n\nIf this thing could be mass-produced or extensively mined...\n\nPerhaps I should find a day to ask her again. I don't know how much longer she'll spend on this automaton. If one day she herself turns into an automaton, I wouldn't be surprised.\n"
  },
  CollectionHall_127165_Title = {
    Text = "Core Meltdown"
  },
  CollectionHall_127166_Desc = {
    Text = "\"With mundane copper and iron, we measure the trajectories of stars, but the endless abyss has its own algorithm, ever-changing.\"\n\nIn the gradually sinking cruise ship, Corposant recited the \"Elegy of the Coxwain.\"\n\nShe had long been aware of her fate and had already chosen her destiny; thus, facing death, she felt no fear, only calmness—calmly burning, calmly completing her last navigation.\n\nBut the burning flames were too intense; she could not see the way ahead, could not make a sound, nor wave a flag. In such imperfect guidance, could the ship navigate correctly?\n\nShe did not know, and thus felt fear and worry.\n\nAt this moment, the \"Elegy of the Coxwain\" offered guidance: \"Young navigator, you shall be embraced by the brine, becoming the guiding phosphorescence.\"\n\nGuiding phosphorescence? Corposant fell silent. She had indeed heard the tales of St. Elmo's Fire among sailors, but how could a mere mortal body transform into the sacred light illuminating the world?\n\nYet even with hope fading, Corposant continuously prayed within her heart: praying that she could fulfill her duty, completing the final guidance.\n\nNo one could hear this prayer except for Corposant herself, but that was enough—\n\nIn the darkness, the Silver core, nourished by Dissolution slime, burst forth with intense light, fulfilling her final wish.\n\n\"The Tidal Black Book will record your name, causing the raging waves to compose an eternal requiem for you.\"\n\nUltimately, she died to the sea as foretold in the \"Elegy of the Coxwain.\"\n\nBut she transcended the \"Elegy of the Coxwain.\"\n\nThat was the arrogance and counsel of human navigators when facing the sea, yet now, she had become St. Elmo's Fire, eternally guiding the ships."
  },
  CollectionHall_127166_Title = {
    Text = "Flamebound Navigator"
  },
  CollectionHall_127167_Desc = {
    Text = [[
She is called the cursed child born with death, an unblessed daughter. 
The "cradle" belonging to her and her sister has just shattered, and brilliant light spills out from the cracks, taking root on the ground. In an instant, green grass withers, flowers fade, and even distant trees and fish in the lake lose their vitality, becoming soulless husks. 
Her family gasps in horror and hurriedly relocates all other cradles. She struggles to break free from the cradle, like a chick hatching from an egg, but her outstretched hands are repulsed with disgust, and all she sees are faces of contempt. 
Only her sister, who was born that night and matured earlier than her, will forever hold her. She sings lullabies with a voice like a spirit bird. 
"Sleep, sleep, my dear sister; 
Sleep, sleep, sweet dreams will surely come." 

She should not exist, and if she did not, her shimmering sister would not be stained by the shadow of sin. 
My poor sister, she always thinks that you bear the cost of existence you shouldn't have to shoulder. 
My poor sister, she always thinks that as long as the sister can do it, she will surely give her all for you. 
"Sleep, sleep, my dear sister; 
Sleep, sleep, I love you even in dreams."]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127167_Title = {
    Text = "Lullaby Devoured"
  },
  CollectionHall_127168_Desc = {
    Text = [[
He saw the church spire melting like a candle, dripping down onto the priest's pure white wings.
The saints in the stained glass rotted into skeletons at high speed, then instantaneously regressed into infants.
Sharp and soft geometric shapes were recited from the mouths of the faithful, filling the entire hall.

He saw the train station's space folding repeatedly into non-Euclidean space, the distant platform just within reach, while the nearby ticket gate was impossibly far away.
The clock in the hall rotated counter-clockwise, and the bony crowd walked backwards, pulled by invisible lines, as thick violet smoke drifted from the clouds into the mouth of the train.

He saw the "void" in the forest take shape, with trees, rocks, and vines merely outlining the translucent contour drawn by the "void".
The swan's feathers were constantly changing mosaic colors, and where they swam, the lake water solidified into translucent stained glass.
Beneath the bench where couples cuddled, a vivid orange-yellow shadow was trying to gnaw at its owner's ankle.

He saw the notes of the opera hall beating down on the audience like raindrops, and he saw the graveyard gently rise and fall, like the skin of a breathing giant beast...

He saw a lot, so much. He told what he saw to his mother, teachers, and friends, and painted what he saw into his artwork.
He wanted to bring the world he saw before people, but the number of people around him grew fewer, and one world drifted further from him.

But why is this? He merely recorded what he saw.
Pickman couldn't understand.

Sad Pickman stood before the mirror.
He saw a ghoul grinning at him with sharp, toothy jaws.

"There is nothing more important than witnessing the real. Madness, chaos, greed...
Do you want to see, Pickman?"

The enlightened Pickman smiled at him and stepped into the mirror.

He only wanted to witness the most extreme madness of reality with his own eyes and faithfully depict it on his canvas.

He is neither human nor ghoul.

He is just Pickman, the realist painter.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_127168_Title = {
    Text = "Paradoxical Realism"
  },
  CollectionHall_127169_Desc = {
    Text = "When someone knows all of the past and future, they are met not with joy but with endless sorrow and despair.\nHer eyes see the threads behind everything—one end linked to the past, the other to the future.\nThese threads are called fate.\nHow does she view those around her?\nPeople are kind and loving, yet arrogant and doubtful.\nBut their fates, as well as humanity's destiny, are sealed from the moment they meet.\nShe must love them; otherwise, why would she repeatedly offer help and give them fire?\nShe must hold expectations for them; otherwise, why would she walk into the shadow of reincarnation amidst destruction?\nBecause of love, she feels sorrow.\nBecause of expectation, she often feels disappointment.\nShe is deeply trapped in a black swamp, tirelessly sorting through countless black threads.\nThe wheel of fate turns again and again.\nShe sees greedy flames sweep across the sky.\nShe sees blind stubbornness leading to self-destruction.\nShe sees insane delusions accelerating destruction.\nChaos will always come.\nHope and despair rotate in vain, endlessly.\nUntil she sees a fleeting starlight in the darkness.\nThat light, though faint, shines powerfully in her long night.\nIn that moment of seeing it, she sheds a tear.\n"
  },
  CollectionHall_127169_Title = {
    Text = "Wheel Unseen"
  },
  CollectionHall_127170_Desc = {
    Text = "In the new year, you decide to hold an unprecedented ceremony to solemnly welcome the passage of time.\nTo this end, you have been preparing for a long time. You light candles, letting their warm glow illuminate the winter night on campus; you set up a high platform in the center of the training ground, covered with a deep red velvet cloth adorned with intricate patterns. you even cut countless colorful ribbons wrapped in gold foil and silver gauze by hand, hoping that this countdown moment transcends the melancholy of farewell, transforming into an everlasting mark embraced by the year-end and the new year.\nBut... something is still missing.\nYou walk deep into the old warehouse, brushing away layers of dust, and finally find that antique clock. Its shell is worn, the hands have long since broken and fallen due to the erosion of time, and it is clearly unusable.\nJust when you are at your wits end, Thais appears, quietly standing behind a brand new clock.\nThat clock feels incredibly familiar. She still smiles playfully, but there is a certain gentle certainty hidden in her eyes.\n\"What do you think? This clock, paired with my dance, will surely be the grandest ceremony.\"\n\"This... can't be Tavi's clock, can it?\"\n\"Oh, you know she has been all alone in the pool, it's too dull for her.\"\n\"Letting her join our ceremony and feel my love might spark her interest a bit~\"\nMidnight quietly arrives, and Thais stands before the giant clock, like a gft wrapped by time itself.\nThe ribbons swirl around her body like unburned fireworks, creating golden-red and silver-blue ripples in the flowing light. The plump bow at her waist is the last knot tied by the new year—she is the grandest gift of the year-end, wrapped in joyful satin, waiting to be unsealed by time.\nHer arms slowly rise, her fingertips tracing the light and shadow, ultimately pointing to the hanging clock behind her. Twelve numbers connect in a halo on the clock face, dancing at her fingertips.\nThe congregation gazes at Thais's exuberant dance, seemingly infected by the joyous atmostphere, beginning to sway in rhythm with her.\nAnd as the chime falls, she lightly taps with her fingertip, touching the beginning of eternity. The bound gift opens its arms, transforming all the celebration stored at year-end into a shower of blessings that scatter across the world."
  },
  CollectionHall_127170_Title = {
    Text = "Countdown Moment"
  },
  CollectionHall_127237_Title = {
    Text = "Huangpu Whispers"
  },
  CollectionHall_127239_Title = {
    Text = "Panlong Empire"
  },
  CollectionHall_129601_Desc = {
    Text = "A cheerful and wildly energetic girl living on a remote, secluded island.\t\nDue to her lively personality and innate monstrous strength, many people find it hard to get used to her overly enthusiastic friendliness when they first meet her. But if they spend some time with her, they will realize she simply wants to help others as much as possible.\t\nSometimes her methods of helping are... unconventional, but judging by the results, she does manage to solve the problems most of the time—probably?\t\nOnce her restraints are lifted, she loses control of her power and often causes explosions in the laboratory.\t\nDue to a lack of formal education, Vortice often has to gesture for quite a while to make herself understood. Of course, she doesn't need others to gesture back—her extraordinary intuition usually bridges the gap just fine.\t\nShe is very close to Nautila and the Keeper. According to her, the three of them once made a pact to go on an adventure together. Nautila, however, has no memory of it whatsoever, while the Keeper refuses to speak a word about that experience.\t\nOccasionally, a sea otter wearing a Mythag hat can be seen by her side. She calls it \"Coalsie II\". Whenever it appears, certain assignments that were supposed to be done mysteriously vanish without a trace."
  },
