  CollectionHall_134293_Desc = {
    Text = "Master of the Theater of Fate, playwright, actor, the eternal weaver and the perpetual captive...\nFrom the moment of her birth, Arachne possessed the ability to perceive the Threads of Fate. Seated before the spinning wheel known as \"Moirae,\" she wove the destinies of the world without respite, upholding the precarious balance of fate. To this end, she banished every tenderness and vulnerability from her soul, culling the most righteous paths for all existence, and bearing the crushing guilt of every destiny alone.\nShe had long known that at the terminus of the Web of Fate, ruin was inescapable. Yet still she wove on, tireless and unceasing, watching all that she had ever loved sink slowly toward that final, all-consuming point of annihilation.\nShe wove. She waited. Waited for the one thread she had never foreseen—the thread that might extricate the Web of Fate from the abyss."
