  CollectionHall_145434_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Event: \"Leviathan's Game: Greed and Bloodlust\""
  },
  CollectionHall_145434_Title = {
    Text = "Leviathan's Game: Greed and Bloodlust"
  },
  CollectionHall_145460_Desc = {
    Text = "Since the day of its birth, It had been trapped in eternal hunger.\nCarcasses of stars cracked between Its teeth; the wreckage of civilizations rotted in Its belly. Its hunger was a curse older than time itself. Again and again It devoured power, driving Its slaves through endless games of power and desire—yet never once did It understand what Its own existence meant.\nUntil the warrior named Lotan came before It.\n\"Leviathan.\"\nIt could not remember the last time Its name had been spoken. Kneeling kings dared not utter it; mad priests could only veil it in hymns.\nBut she spoke It with ease—as if hailing a long-awaited rival.\n\"Your turn.\"\nIt had existed for twelve thousand years. Through that vast eternity, planets were sustenance, living beings mere ants, and even the mightiest warriors no more than fleeting amusements. Nothing had ever sated it. Nothing had ever made it afraid.\nUntil today.\nThis mortal, this warrior, raised her greatblade and struck like a storm.\nThe blade tore through its scales. In its ears echoed the roar of Its birth from the chaos. Its wrath sundered celestial bodies; Its hunger swallowed nebulae whole.\nThe blade severed its claws. It remembered—the goddess in the white veil, who had come before It and torn Its power from Its will.\nAnd the instant the blade pierced Its heart, Leviathan laughed.\nTwelve millennia. Its lost will had finally returned to It—to shatter, conquer, and devour It. Now she would lead It onward, across every domain and into the farther reaches of the cosmos, to conquer every power that dared stand in their way.\nOn that day, the ancient Beast of Chaos was reborn. In the instant It returned to her, It finally understood: both of them had been born of one thing alone—pure, absolute strength.\nStrength itself was the only meaning there had ever been."
  },
  CollectionHall_145460_Title = {
    Text = "Cetus Occasus"
  },
  CollectionHall_146400_Desc = {
    Text = "Unable to quell the primeval fury of the Astral Cetus, the ancient deity severed Its spirit from Its flesh. Thus Its will fell upon the barren land, incarnating as a warrior named Lotan: Cetarchon.\nWarlike by nature, she regarded the pursuit of ultimate strength as her sole instinct and honor. She entered the Astral Cetus’s trial and forged a pact with It. Then, at the zenith of her power, she struck down her own master with her greatsword, claiming the power of the star-devouring behemoth as her own.\nSharp whalebone pierced her flesh; dark bone armor encased her form. Those eyes that once held the cosmos now reflect nothing but cold scrutiny for her foes.\nShe takes no pleasure in destruction, nor does she deign to engage in meaningless slaughter. She craves nothing but more thrilling foes and ever-greater strength.\nThe purest warrior hunts the shadows of the mighty across the starry cosmos—until all of them fall beneath her blade, and every path has been walked to its very end."
  },
  CollectionHall_146400_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Till the Cetus Falls\""
  },
  CollectionHall_146400_Title = {
    Text = "Lotan: Cetarchon"
  },
  CollectionHall_146412_Title = {
    Text = "Till the Cetus Falls"
  },
  CollectionHall_146867_LockTip = {
