  CollectionHall_48968_Desc = {
    Text = [[
There are many speculations circulating in the Mythag campus about Lord Dexter's staff.

"There's no doubt that the lord's staff hides as many secrets as his smile.
Is it inlaid with silver capable of harnessing the power of the Awakeners, or is it secretly filled with gunpowder, ready to transform into a firearm?
Let Lord Dexter reveal it for us!"

After quickly noting down the opening remarks, Hannah aimed her camera at Lord Dexter, eagerly awaiting the words from the holder himself.

"This? Nothing special, just the daily staff custom-made for the Dexter family.
The gem used on mine is even less precious than my brother's.
If I had to say what makes it special...
It has once been stained with my parents' and brother's blood; does that count?"]]
  },
  CollectionHall_48968_Title = {
    Text = "Nobleman's Staff"
  },
  CollectionHall_48969_Desc = {
    Text = "A story circulates in the underground world of Londinium.\n\nAt the busy docks, in secluded alleyways, and noisy taverns...\nYou never know when or where you might find that girl with a camera, wearing glasses, and dressed in uniform. But as long as you find her, you can buy any information you want, and the only cost is one—\n\nTo provide a secret known only to you.\n\nSome traded a drunken truth they overheard at the bar for a deadly weakness of a competitor.\nSome exchanged their own weakness for the untold past of a lover.\nThe girl possesses countless bits of information, but there is one that cannot be traded for any secret.\n\n\"About me? Sorry, that's not for sale.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_48969_Title = {
    Text = "Data is Flesh"
  },
  CollectionHall_48970_Desc = {
    Text = "At Mythag, the person you must not provoke is none other than Ms. Sylvia, assuming Doll ranks second.\n\nAs the only psychologist at Mythag, this mysterious woman not only comforts investigators traumatized by missions but also calms the turbulent emotions of Awakeners. She does not fear Awakeners; instead, she confronts them mentally—what a formidable figure.\n\nDriven by curiosity and lacking proper respect, some freshmen sneaked into Ms. Sylvia's clinic late at night.\n\nThen, they lost consciousness. The next morning, they woke up in the campus square with throbbing headaches but an unprecedented clarity of mind.\n\nSomeone picked up a note that had fallen from their pockets:\n\n\"If you need psychological counseling, please make an appointment with Ms. Erica in advance—\nSylvia\""
  },
  CollectionHall_48970_Title = {
    Text = "Mind Barrier"
  },
  CollectionHall_48971_Desc = {
    Text = "The noblewoman, with a mix of pity and disgust, covered her nose with a handkerchief and had her servant hand her the unwanted jewelry.\nShe thought:\nThat's great—the children in the workhouse can have meat for once.\n\nAfter sharing all her food with the children and fainting from hunger in the corridor, she said:\nI'm fine. Don't call the doctor; the fee would buy several loaves of bread.\n\nWhen the kind-hearted artist visited with a doctor he knew and offered a long-term arrangement, she thought:\nThey must try it on me first. I won't let the children receive their so-called treatment until I'm sure it's safe.\n\nSarah could bear any hardship herself.\nBut she could not bear that everything she did eventually led to tragedy."
  },
  CollectionHall_48971_Title = {
    Text = "Critical Point"
  },
  CollectionHall_48972_Desc = {
    Text = "A hand gropes in the dark, searching for its master.\n\nOn that bloody night, it was cruelly torn from its owner.\nNow, the culprit flows around it, emitting a peculiar hum.\n\n\"Give up and come with us. The Wax Sculptor will forget you entirely.\"\n\nThe hand remains unmoved, flexing its proud, slender fingers.\n\n\"Master will not forget me.\nI am his only means of artistic expression—\nYou don't understand what I mean to him.\"\n\n\"Just as one may forget a lover, forget time, but never forget oneself.\"\n\nA sympathetic laugh echoes in the darkness.\n\"Quite the contrary, the first thing one forgets is oneself.\nBut that's alright—\"\n\nTime will explain everything, and the hand will eventually learn:\nNothing is beyond forgetting.\nThey have flowed for centuries, witnessing human stories unfold, only to be forgotten the next day.\nAnd they continue to flow."
  },
  CollectionHall_48972_Title = {
    Text = "Hand of Oblivion"
  },
  CollectionHall_48973_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Since being taken in by Mr. Ward Philips, Alistair has accompanied him to numerous high-level meetings of Mythag.

Though termed high-level, it feels more like a monthly debate competition:
Mr. Philips speaks gently and leads the discussion;
Khlarcus is sharp-tongued and unyielding.
They take turns as the affirmative or negative side, arguing endlessly about the future of Mythag or the resource allocation for the Awakening Studies Department next month.
Miss Tawil is a silent observer, never easily offering her suggestions.
He himself strives to be an impartial scorekeeper, occasionally doubling as a referee, and even had to use some combat skills once to prevent the small conference table from facing mishap.

Now, only two members remain in the meeting: one can never leave the Black Pool, and the other can no longer leave the underground in pursuit of that possible "future."
As for that table, it has been lost since that incident.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_48973_Title = {
    Text = "Moment of Reunion"
  },
  CollectionHall_48974_Desc = {
    Text = "Tawil sleeps at the bottom of the Black Pool.\n\nThere, it is eternally silent and dark, filled only with a despairing blackness.\nNo guests have ever visited here, and no sounds have ever reached here.\nThis is a place where Destruction cannot reach—\n\nBecause the Cataclysm have already arrived.\n\nAs the master of time and sequences, she has witnessed far too many painful ends.\nAs a part of the rules, she is powerless to stop the night from falling.\nIn this case, she can only lie dormant in the realm of non-existence, awaiting the arrival of the one who can be called a \"variable.\"\n\nThat person will undoubtedly come."
  },
  CollectionHall_48974_Title = {
    Text = "The Land of Nonexistence"
  },
  CollectionHall_48975_Desc = {
    Text = "Science is spectral analysis; art is photosynthesis."
  },
  CollectionHall_48975_Title = {
    Text = "Photosynthesis Ritual"
  },
  CollectionHall_48976_Desc = {
    Text = "Spin, then forget—this is all of her life."
