  CollectionHall_48984_Title = {Text = "Paradox"},
  CollectionHall_48985_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The acting dean is an oddity on the Mythag campus.

Almost each Mythag investigator has unique abilities, while she is one of the very few with no powers beyond ordinary human limits.

Yet she holds this vital role.

Born into an ordinary family in the Elke Kingdom, she grew fierce and tenacious, shaped by local traditions.

Later, her fellow prisoner in the camp, Sophia, ignited her passion for academic research.

Her remarkable academic achievements made her the most trusted student of her mentor, the former dean of the Mythag University Biological Institute.

Thus, after her mentor disappeared, she naturally stepped in as acting dean.

Under her steadfast leadership, the institute's research continues to run smoothly.

"Fear no violence, fear no power. And so, fear no duty."]]
  },
  CollectionHall_48985_Title = {
    Text = "Duty's Gravitas"
  },
  CollectionHall_48986_Desc = {
    Text = [[
There is a custom among investigators:
On the night following the Keygrave Ceremony, senior investigators gather newcomers in the dormitory backyard.

They light candles and sit in a circle around their Silver Keys.

The seniors then share the unique story behind the uniquely numbered key they now hold.

Such gatherings always end up turning into storytelling sessions, and the two keys representing the "first generation," I-0001 and K-0001, naturally become the focus of conversation.


Few people know that K-0001, the Silver Key crafted by its owner, the first Keeper, now rests underground with him.

There, in timeless dark, it listens to his whispers for someone long departed.

"You know he's not really here, Alistair," says Doll.
"It might be made from your teacher's Silver Core, but it's not his soul."

"It's just a way to focus the spirit, Doll," Alistair smiled.
"Don't worry, I'm stable. I can't break down before our new Keeper grows up, right?"]]
  },
  CollectionHall_48986_Title = {
    Text = "Elevated Focus"
  },
  CollectionHall_48987_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The first half of his life was chaotic, dark, and bloody.

Eat. Sleep. Repeat.
Then he opened his eyes and gained awareness.

They say he devoured all his siblings and became the sole survivor.

They say he is the offspring of the Great Serpent and a human.

A black, cursed collar encircles his neck.
It keeps him alive, controls him, and ensures he can never defy the Church.

He is full of questions, curious about the world, yet at the very moment of his birth, he was stripped of all other possibilities.

Beautiful, dangerous.
Secretive, flamboyant.
He is all of these.

Sadly, these barely scratch the surface of his essence.

Any pity you feel for Albino because of this account will lead you to ruin.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_48987_Title = {
    Text = "Cursed Binding"
  },
  CollectionHall_48988_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A doctor's duty is to heal.

But there happens to be a treatment that demands the sharpest blade: to cut through skin, pierce muscle, and open the chest.
It requires removing the rot, and then trusting the body to heal on its own.

This should not count as her sin.
Yet after every surgery, she would find herself telling the girl some stories, as if to make up for it.

She wasn't a good storyteller; her words were fragmented, disjointed.
Still, the girl listened intently.

Where her hands once cut, the flesh seems to draw strength from those words, slowly and stubbornly mending itself...]]
  },
  CollectionHall_48988_Title = {
    Text = "Sever and Scar"
  },
  CollectionHall_48989_Desc = {
    Text = "The giant beast lurks in the night.\n\nInside the cabin, a mother wails for her lost daughter, finally breaking through the restraint she held all day.\n\nEvery midnight, her grief bursts forth, raw and unhidden.\n\nIt begins with sobs and rises to howls, then comes the calling of the name that no longer belongs to the beast.\n\nThe agony in her voice pierces the beast's heart, a heart that remains entirely human.\n\n<Italic:Come home, Lisa.>\n<Italic:Oh, my Lisa.>\n\nThe beast remains silent.\n\nIt curls up in the darkness and falls into a deep sleep.\n\nOne day, it will return—to the place called \"home\"."
  },
  CollectionHall_48989_Title = {
    Text = "Cloaked in the Night"
  },
  CollectionHall_48990_Desc = {
    Text = "No one is born a captain; at least Elton wasn't.\n\nBefore becoming a captain, he drifted between the navy and merchant ships, nearly turning pirate more than once.\n\nFortunately, he finally settled aboard an exploration vessel.\nThe ship sailed around the polar continent, each landing a new adventure.\n\nHis job was to carry the gears for the frail scientists.\nHe was proud of it: what he carried might be the keys to changing the world.\nAnd the scientists might be the ones to rewrite history.\n\nThat was what Elton believed—until an ice storm trapped them in a cave, and until a band of cultists attacked them under the cover of night."
  },
  CollectionHall_48990_Title = {
    Text = "Adventurer's Pack"
  },
  CollectionHall_48991_Desc = {
    Text = "He'd always been a quiet, diligent student.\n\nAt 8:00 a.m., when other researchers hurried in with bread stuffed in their mouths, he had already finished a lab report.\n\nHe would stay until midnight, when the last light in the lab building was out, then slowly pack up and leave.\n\nHe also fed the nearby stray cats every day.\n\nLater, the stray cats vanished—no one knew where they had gone.\n\nProfessor Crowley reviewed his lab notes and reports.\nThey were concise, meticulous—unremarkable, yet flawless.\n\nThis student puzzled him.\n\nPuzzlement is good; it often leads to curiosity.\n\nOf course, Crowley did not realize then: it could also lead to something else—death."
  },
  CollectionHall_48991_Title = {
    Text = "Analysis of Death"
  },
  CollectionHall_48992_Desc = {
    Text = "\"You've been gone so long, and I didn't even notice.\n\nI still keep dreaming of that day—the gunshot pain in my left arm, the blood loss haze, the frenzied rats chasing us...\nThen you appeared, in your Mythag uniform, getting me out of that cursed old castle.\n\nAt the dream's end, you stood beside my sickbed and told me:\nfor investigators, death is always close behind.\n\nI can no longer tell reality from dream.\n\nWhenever I am confused, I reach for my left arm—if I feel the cold, intricate metal, I know I'm awake.\n\nBut most times, I grasp nothing but air.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_48992_Title = {
    Text = "To My Dearest Friend"
  },
  CollectionHall_48993_Desc = {
    Text = "Crowley held the title of \"Most Popular Mentor\" every year he taught.\n\nHis slightly awkward West Constante accent and genuine smile won over countless students, including Herbert.\n\nIn A.F.2@1, Crowley defied objections and took Herbert, who was unremarkable at that time, as his student.\n\nTogether, they crossed mountains, forded streams, and trekked deserts, leaving footprints outside one D-Rift after another.\n\n\nHerbert can still remember the shock of seeing a D-Rift for the first time.\n\nCrowley stood before the billowing black mist, his silhouette small against it.\n\n\"Shh—can you hear that?\"\n\nHerbert closed his eyes.\nAll he heard was the sound of a silent, rolling ocean; the world seemed to drift away.\n\nCrowley was thrilled.\n\"This is poetry,\" he said.\n\"The most mysterious, profound poetry in the universe.\"\n\nYears later, Herbert's memories of Crowley had mostly faded—\nhow they worked together, argued, and even how he \"accidentally\" killed him.\n\nBut he would always remember that smile beneath the black mist.\nIn that moment, he saw the poetry."
  },
  CollectionHall_48993_Title = {
    Text = "Memory Syndrome"
  },
  CollectionHall_48994_Desc = {
    Text = "As long as our brains remain a mystery, it's no big deal if they're filled with tentacles."
  },
  CollectionHall_48994_LockTip = {
    Text = "Unlocked in: Investigation"
  },
  CollectionHall_48994_Title = {
    Text = "<WhiteQuality:Severed Head Worm>"
  },
  CollectionHall_48995_Desc = {
    Text = "Dreams are the stars and the sea!"
  },
  CollectionHall_48995_LockTip = {
    Text = "Unlocked in: Investigation"
  },
  CollectionHall_48995_Title = {
    Text = "<WhiteQuality:Submersible Helm>"
  },
  CollectionHall_48996_Desc = {
    Text = "See that which cannot be seen; hear that which cannot be heard."
  },
  CollectionHall_48996_Title = {Text = "Epiphany"},
  CollectionHall_48997_Desc = {
    Text = "The root of all evil."
  },
  CollectionHall_48997_Title = {Text = "Punishment"},
  CollectionHall_48998_Desc = {
    Text = "All things become mine."
  },
  CollectionHall_48998_Title = {Text = "Gluttony"},
  CollectionHall_48999_Desc = {
    Text = "Neither dwell on the past nor yearn for the future."
  },
  CollectionHall_48999_Title = {Text = "Frenzy"},
  CollectionHall_49000_Desc = {
    Text = "Offer love and death to the world."
  },
  CollectionHall_49000_Title = {Text = "Favor"},
  CollectionHall_49001_Desc = {
    Text = "After a great many years of amassing tremendous power, we hereby declare—"
  },
  CollectionHall_49001_Title = {Text = "Emerge"},
  CollectionHall_49002_Desc = {
    Text = "Call its name: Erexis."
  },
  CollectionHall_49002_Title = {Text = "Delirium"},
  CollectionHall_49003_Desc = {
    Text = "A conversation with \"Him.\""
  },
  CollectionHall_49003_Title = {Text = "Whisper"},
  CollectionHall_49004_Desc = {
    Text = "Blessings for the birds and the bees."
  },
  CollectionHall_49004_Title = {Text = "Hope"},
  CollectionHall_49015_Desc = {
    Text = [[

After the disaster vanished without a trace and the crisis was temporarily resolved, the Mythag Special Operations Team departed from Yakutsk with "unexpected gains."
Miss Dexter glanced back at the massive pit at the explosion site, noticing that unknown plant sprouts had quietly broken through the soil without her realizing it.
She sighed in relief, feeling lighthearted.
The vast forests of Yakutsk will surely welcome its spring.
The willows will bud when the next spring arrives, and the lilies of the valley will bloom quietly after the next rainy season, with all life embracing new beginnings.
And their journey against the unknown will embark on a new starting point.
]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49015_Title = {
    Text = "Spring in Yakutsk"
  },
  CollectionHall_49018_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A.F. 314, on a deep winter night, the sound of an explosion echoed through the Yakutsk Forests.
The earth trembled, and the woods were illuminated as if it were midday. Accompanied by the shrieks of life and the wails of nature, the village was razed to the ground.
According to Dexter, a pre-college student majoring in Awakener Studies who participated in the investigation, among the flames shooting into the sky that night, colors of black and silver shone brightly.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49018_Title = {Text = "Sunfall"},
  CollectionHall_49025_Desc = {
    Text = "Blood-dark sacrifice. May the Twins bless your body."
  },
  CollectionHall_49025_Title = {
    Text = "Twisted Twins: Black"
  },
  CollectionHall_49026_Desc = {
    Text = "Mist-white prayers. May the Twins bless your soul."
  },
  CollectionHall_49026_Title = {
    Text = "Twisted Twins: White"
  },
  CollectionHall_49027_Desc = {
    Text = "Feast amidst the carols; celebrate the ruin of the world we once called home."
  },
  CollectionHall_49027_Title = {
    Text = "Feast from Afar"
  },
  CollectionHall_49028_Desc = {
    Text = "The fabled architect of the automatons, who nourished his creations with his own blood."
  },
  CollectionHall_49028_Title = {
    Text = "Crimson Pulse"
  },
  CollectionHall_49029_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The machine is purity absolute; the divine is supreme.
What descends is no mere thread, but Ariadne herself.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49029_Title = {
    Text = "Deus Ex Machina"
  },
  CollectionHall_49030_Desc = {
    Text = "Proliferate, proliferate! Let the souls infused with the blood of the Mother Tree spread across the world."
  },
  CollectionHall_49030_Title = {
    Text = "Re-evolution"
  },
  CollectionHall_49031_Desc = {
    Text = "The fabled architect of the automatons, who destroyed his creations with his own hands."
  },
  CollectionHall_49031_Title = {
    Text = "Scarlet Embrace"
  },
  CollectionHall_49033_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The strings of time snap one by one, and the flowing keys shatter in turn.

Standing beyond reality, They repair the rifts with the fabric of reality itself, so the unending symphony may sound again in the high heavens.

As for where the tears shed upon waking flow, no one knows.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49033_Title = {
    Text = "Birth of a Soul"
  },
  CollectionHall_49082_Title = {
