    Text = "Soul Shepherd"
  },
  CollectionHall_49740_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Investigation Stage 7-0"
  },
  CollectionHall_49740_Title = {
    Text = "Mother of Million Offsprings"
  },
  CollectionHall_49747_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Outgrowths from Dissolution scars.
So far, there is no discernible pattern to whether these outgrowths grow or how different types of outgrowths are distributed.
They could be extra limbs, tentacles, or even inorganic materials such as gears and metals.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49747_Title = {
    Text = "D-Hyperplasia"
  },
  CollectionHall_49748_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Definition and Characteristics>
A massive D-mark with a diameter exceeding 5 meters that may continue to expand.
D-Rifts are classified into C, B, A, S, SS, and SSS types based on their size.
Over time, they will continue to expand, causing not only regular dissolution spread but also abnormal natural phenomena such as tsunamis and hurricanes.

<Title:Response Methods>
Silver Keys refined from Silvers can suppress or even "close" D-Rifts to a certain extent.
Keepers amplify their spirits using Silver Keys, resonating with the spirit dimension to form a high-dimensional barrier over the D-Rift, temporarily "closing" it.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49748_Title = {Text = "D-Rift"},
  CollectionHall_49749_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The core of the D-Rift is usually also the primary enemy that Keepers must deal with during field missions. 
It can spread D-Phenomenon, influencing nearby D-Phenomenon based on its characteristics and causing regional traits.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49749_Title = {Text = "Cataclysm"},
  CollectionHall_49750_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Definition and Characteristics>
The D-Phenomenon causes transformation, dissolution, and death in individuals.
It affects organic entities such as humans, animals, and plants, as well as inorganic materials like minerals and metals. Individuals near D-rifts are more susceptible to the effects of the D-Phenomenon.
No substance has been found to be immune to the D-Phenomenon so far.

<Title:Phases>
Early Stage: An inverted triangular black D-Mark appears on the body surface, accompanied by the extrusion of D-slime.
Mid Stage: The D-Mark expands, with continuous extrusion of D-slime. Mental damage occurs, and D-hyperplasia may develop.
Late Stage: The D-Mark rapidly expands, and the extrusion of D-slime accelerates. Most individuals lose their sanity completely at this stage.
Final Stage: The body collapses, resulting in physiological death. Mental corruption continues until the individual is fully corrupted and disappears entirely, with no possibility of awakening.

<Title:Special Cases>
Body Cases: Enhanced physical abilities and senses. Some individuals develop special abilities such as flight, mind control, or other effects caused by D-hyperplasia and disaster.
Spirit Cases: Minimal mental impact, retaining basic sanity. Some individuals behave normally, similar to those unaffected by the D-Phenomenon.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49750_Title = {
    Text = "Dissolution Erosion"
  },
  CollectionHall_49751_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Definition and Features>
Individuals lose their bodies due to dissolution, transforming into D-Slime and Dissoluted Dust.
After Dissolution, their existence will be erased from the world.

<Title:Stage Characteristics>
Early Stage: Those unfamiliar with the affected individuals will forget their existence.
Mid Stage: The memory of the affected individuals held by acquaintances weakens, and written records begin to show d-marks, becoming blurred.
Late Stage: The memory of the affected individuals held by acquaintances further diminishes until they completely forget them, leaving only a vague impression.

<Title:Existence Erasure>
At the final stage, the existence of the affected individuals, including all traces, will be completely erased.
Nothing can prove they ever existed, just like most people.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49751_Title = {Text = "Dissolve"},
  CollectionHall_49752_Desc = {
    Text = "Silver may be the endpoint of Dissolution: it is a reflective substance that forms probabilistically when life is eroded by Dissolution. It not only contains immense physical energy but also establishes a connection with the Spirit Dimension. In certain cases, this connection can even interfere with the \"Spirit Dimension.\" Silver is one of the key elements in humanity's fight against Dissolution. However, due to the unique nature of its formation, Silver is not only scarce in quantity but also extremely valuable."
  },
  CollectionHall_49752_Title = {Text = "Silver"},
  CollectionHall_49753_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Overview>
All technologies that utilize Silver are collectively referred to as Silver Technology.
The vast majority of people in the world are unaware of the existence of Silver; only Mythag University possesses knowledge of Silver Technology and offers a major in silver chip research and applications, continuously researching and developing Silver.
According to the Mystia Treaty, Mythag University will provide Silver Technology to the Mystia Treaty Committee in order to jointly resist dissolution and respond to crises.

<Title:What is an Awakener?>
In the Awakener technology at Mythag University, the creation of Awakeners revolves around Silver.
Although the creation of Awakeners is not documented in the Silver Technology Manual, many Awakeners humorously self-deprecate:
"Hey, aren't we a kind of Silver Technology?"

<Title:Dissolution Observation Device>
Available in various styles such as glasses and masks. Made of Silver, it allows the wearer to observe domains and see dissolution.

<Title:Mythag University Communicator>
The most common style is a badge shaped like the school emblem. Its core is a specially treated silver chip, and the communicator can not only connect with each other but also achieve ultra-long-distance communication within the Mythag campus. The signal is stable and <Italic:generally speaking>
is not interfered with by natural phenomena.

<Title:Mythag Access Credential>
A special credential containing Silver; only those holding the credential can avoid getting lost in the mist barrier of Mythag University.
Those without a credential will find themselves trapped in endless perceptual disorders in the woods outside the university, waiting to be expelled by the duty investigators.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49753_Title = {
    Text = "Silver Technology"
  },
  CollectionHall_49754_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Principle>
Awakened from Silver Core, transformed through experimentation, or born from an accident...
They are ancient yet new. Ancient, because wizards secretly recorded the Awakener's presence in the world on papyrus texts many centuries ago.
They are new, as we have yet to fully understand the nature of Awakeners while embarking on a journey to save the world alongside them.
Aside from placing trust in them, remember: Do not let your guard down.

<Title:Characteristics>
Awakeners possess complete personalities and retain their memories from their "previous life," but due to their unique abilities, they have been treated as humanoid weapons.
To maintain societal stability, the existence of Awakeners is highly classified in various countries.
Currently, only Awakeners awakened by Mythag University are recognized by the "Pact." Any Awakeners not awakened by Mythag University are considered violations of the "Pact" and require official documentation and containment.

<Title:Realm>
Awakeners exhibit varying abilities, but researchers consistently find certain similarities among different abilities.
Based on these similarities, Mythag University has artificially categorized several realms of Awakeners.
Awakeners within the same realm can better cooperate with each other, while there may be some degree of mutual exclusion across different realms; only the Chaos realm does not exhibit this phenomenon.
The reason for the inter-realm exclusion remains unclear. According to Professor Doll from Mythag University's Awakened Department, it may relate to the influence of certain unknowable entities on the spirit dimension, although no evidence currently supports this hypothesis.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49754_Title = {
    Text = "Awakener Cognitive Basis"
  },
  CollectionHall_49755_Desc = {
    Text = "<Title:Overview>\nA key-shaped item made exclusively from Silver. It has the ability to focus and amplify the user's spirit, assisting in connecting with and affecting the spirit dimension.\nThe Silver Key is a symbol of identity for Mythag investigators and Keepers, each with a unique serial number. An ordinary investigator's Silver Key serial starts with 'I', while a Keeper's starts with 'K'.\nIf an investigator can no longer engage in field operations for some reason, the Mythag faculty will reclaim the Silver Key they hold and reassign it to another investigator in the future.\nUnfortunately, records show that in a century, fewer than ten Silver Keys capable of normal functioning were reclaimed. Most Silver Keys were destroyed along with their owners' demise.\n\n<Title:Manufacturing and Acquisition>\n■■ Confidential Document No. ■■■\nThe formation of the silver ■ key requires processing in the Black Pool by ■■■■■.\nOnce ■■■ is formed, it is engraved and bestowed upon the corresponding user during the Keygrave Ceremony."
  },
  CollectionHall_49755_Title = {Text = "Silver Key"},
  CollectionHall_49756_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Overview>
Domain, a unique area formed by the intersection of the real world and the spirit dimension.
Mr. Phillips of Mythag University once noted in his writings: All anomalies in the world, if not arising from the human mind, are born from the Domain.
Here, life and death, reality and illusion intertwine. It repels the truth, it conceals the truth.

<Title:Definition and Characteristics>
The Domain is the closest space to the spirit dimension that humans can physically enter, yet people know very little about it, much like their scant understanding of Dissolution.
What is certain, however, is that Dissolution and the Domain always appear together: the more severe the D-Phenomenon, the larger the Domain's dimensional coverage.

<Title:Entities in the Domain>
As a fragile junction, the Domain is highly susceptible to influence.
Special entities appearing in the Domain, such as Illusions, D-marks, and Mist, are considered projections of emotions and thoughts. Leveraging this unique projection mechanism, Mythag University has been able to project some Junctions in the Domain to stabilize Investigators' spirits and mend Awakeners' wounds.
However, real-world entities like ground and buildings are usually unaffected in the Domain. (Don't worry, the roads in the Domain are <Italic:mostly>
safe.)]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49756_Title = {Text = "Domain"},
  CollectionHall_49757_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Founding Date>
Before the Flood

<Title:Founder>
Unknown

<Title:Overview>
The most widespread faith across the Pan-Laurasia Continent. 
It boasts a large number of followers and operates on a grand scale. Celebratory rituals are held in various locations during specific times of the year, with the most prominent being the Silverfrost Eve and the Solstice Passage Festival. 
Clerics within the organization refer to themselves as "Emissaries of the All-Father," tasked with carrying out the Father's will to alleviate the world's suffering. 
They believe that after death, one can return to the embrace of the All-Father, dwelling eternally in boundless bliss, free from worldly suffering. 
With such universal teachings, it has naturally become a popular religion.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49757_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"The Color of Blood: Repentance\""
  },
  CollectionHall_49757_Title = {
    Text = "Chantry of Life"
  },
  CollectionHall_49758_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Founding Date>
Before the Flood

<Title:Founder>
Miryam

<Title:Overview>
An ancient organization originating from the Old Continent. 
Members typically exhibit fish-like upper bodies and human lower bodies, primarily active in Oceans and coastal regions, never venturing inland. 
It is said that they traverse the seas to follow the King's path and to bring about the Divine Realm. 
All sacrifices are for the lost Kingdom of Lemuria and its slumbering King.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49758_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 5: \"Eye of the Storm\""
  },
  CollectionHall_49758_Title = {Text = "Seafarer"},
  CollectionHall_49759_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Founding Date>
During the Flood

<Title:Founder>
Unknown

<Title:Overview>
A secretive religious organization. 
They regard Dissolution as a Divine Gift and the Silver as the body of God, believing that Dissolution purifies sins and leads to the Innocent Pure Land. 
Though numerous, their movements are concealed; wherever Dissolution occurs, traces of them can be faintly detected. 
It is rumored they originated from an ancient and prestigious family whose collective disappearance remains a debated historical enigma.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49759_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 4: \"Where Silence Reigns\""
  },
  CollectionHall_49759_Title = {
    Text = "Church of the Lightbearers"
  },
  CollectionHall_49760_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Gnosis Index>
A numerical value quantifying the stability of spirit fragments within the Silver.
Awakeners with high Gnosis indices possess stronger stability of spirit fragments, lower levels of madness, and are less prone to losing control. In the event of loss of control, the potential casualties would also be fewer.
Different Awakeners exhibit varying Gnosis indices; some may experience fluctuations in their Gnosis index or even face difficulties in accurate measurement due to unique individual circumstances.

<Title:Awakener's Loss of Control>
As the core, the Silver grants Awakeners powers that should not exist in the world, but it also plants the seeds of madness within them.
Awakeners are often shaped amidst uncontrollable madness, and without timely links from investigators, their loss of control could lead to unimaginable destruction of the world. Thus, linking serves not only as an "amplifier" but also as an indispensable "stabilizer."
According to archive records from Mythag University, currently, only Doll: @2 has retained rationality during the early stage of becoming an Awakener.
Additionally, "the Thing Within the Door" Tawil and the first Keeper Alistair have maintained the stability of the giant Silver under the L-01 D-Rift, allowing the Awakeners within Mythag University to maintain their rationality for a long time. Even if the link is severed, they will not lose control.

<Title:Awakener's Death>
Awakeners surpass humans in bodily functions, yet they can still be harmed and have their bodies destroyed when faced with threats from aberrants, disasters, or even D-Rifts and the dissolution itself.
Researchers believe that when an Awakener's body is destroyed, the consciousness within the Silver will return to the spirit dimension, awaiting a second awakening.
Damage to the Silver may signify true "death."

<Title:Second Awakening>
After a second awakening, an Awakener's appearance, personality, preferences, and abilities generally remain unchanged, and memories are preserved as well. However, some Awakeners may perceive their former selves as two separate individuals, and Mythag University adopts a reserved stance on these opinions.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49760_Title = {
    Text = "Awakener Cognitive Advance"
  },
  CollectionHall_49761_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Overview>
Certain Awakeners exhibit a high degree of consistency in abilities and physical anomalies. Researchers thus speculate that some unknown entity may have influenced the Awakeners' spirits during the awakening process (some believe it to be pollution), endowing them with tremendous Power.
Currently, researchers refer to the Power that has affected the existence of Awakeners as "Genesis." 

<Title:Genesis Awakener>
Genesis Awakeners are "another self" of the eponymous Awakeners.
They share similar traits but possess entirely different life experiences; their personalities, hobbies, performances, and even Powers bear more characteristics of "Genesis." 
Records concerning Genesis Awakeners are very limited, and Mythag knows little about the causes of this phenomenon. Some researchers speculate and develop the theory of the existence of "parallel worlds" based on the emergence of Genesis Awakeners, though this theory has yet to be published or further researched.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49761_Title = {Text = "Genesis"},
  CollectionHall_49762_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Silver Core>
The Awakeners cannot function without their Silver Core. Even if the body is completely disassembled, as long as the Silver Core remains, an Awakener can be reawakened.

<Title:Body>
The body of the Awakener can be made of various materials. The specific components and structure are related to the preferences and characteristics of the Awakener itself.
The Body of the Awakener is not provided in advance by the staff of Mythag University but is instead formed from the spiritual energy in the Silver Coreduring the Awakening ceremony. Therefore, in the Awakening ceremony, in addition to the necessary Silver Core and Silver Key, a large amount of materials must be prepared for the Awakener to synthesize their body. Common materials can be found in Appendix 3.
Additionally, Mythag University has specialized departments and researchers responsible for maintaining and repairing the Body of the Awakener.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49762_Title = {
    Text = "Awakener Composition"
  },
  CollectionHall_49763_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Daily Life>
Awakeners enjoy the same rights as staff within Mythag University. They have the right to use campus facilities and receive investigation rewards.
When partnered investigators do not have field tasks, Awakeners can freely move around the campus. Most Awakeners choose to follow their past hobbies and habits to find things they want to do; some may choose to enter classrooms to learn about the current era or socialize with Investigators.
Except in a few special cases, Awakeners generally do not need to eat or sleep. However, if Awakeners wish to do these activities, it will not cause any negative effects.

<Title:Combat>
To balance the energy expenditure between combat command and maintaining Links, Mythag University developed a special device called the "Gnosis Transfer." 
The "Gnosis Transfer" built into the field suitcase can transfer Awakeners' Abilities into card form, thereby enabling the command of Awakeners.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49763_Title = {
    Text = "Awakener Behavior"
  },
  CollectionHall_49764_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Founding Date>
A.F.306

<Title:Founder>
Herbert Rosenthal

<Title:Overview>
A radical private research organization.
Attempts human evolution by merging humans with dissolution entities to survive the disasters.
Comprising around 20 radicals who consider innocents as experimental subjects, employing brutal methods.
Founded by Herbert Rosenthal, the notorious traitor of Mythag University, closely collaborating with Church of the Lightbearers.
Their symbol is a sculptor's flat chisel, supposedly honoring the Cypriot king who fell in love with a statue.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49764_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 3: \"Beware of Hounds\""
  },
  CollectionHall_49764_Title = {
    Text = "Sculptors' Association"
  },
  CollectionHall_49765_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Overview>
Professionals selected and trained through special processes at Mythag University possess powerful spirit power, allowing them to withstand the exhaustion brought by linking with Awakeners and issue spiritual commands to them.
They face Dissolution directly, fighting for the survival of humanity, yet remain unknown. Investigators who die from Dissolution leave behind not even their names or complete files.
Their names may be unknown, but may their contributions endure forever.

<Title:Selection>
Based on the theoretical foundation of "The Psychological Composition and Potential of Investigators," Mythag selects individuals with strong spirit power by observing the intensity of spiritual Resonance between individuals and Silver Keys for training.

<Title:Training>
After selection, Investigators must first enter a preparatory class for one year of training.
Training content includes basic theory of Dissolution, introduction to Silver Technology, theories of Awakeners, and foundational courses, as well as combat-related training in basic physical abilities, Awakener Linking, and Awakener Commanding.

<Title:Keygrave Ceremony>
After one year of studies and passing assessments, Investigators will participate in the Keygrave Ceremony held on the school's anniversary.
During the ceremony, Investigators recite oaths and have their names engraved on a gravestone.
Subsequently, each Investigator will be granted a Silver Key with a unique number, all starting with the letter "I." 
From this moment, they will bid farewell to their past as ordinary individuals. After they die, this stone bearing their name will become proof of their existence.

<Title:Resignation>
If an Investigator cannot perform an outdoor mission for various reasons, Mythag will respect their decision and transfer them to safer departments such as logistics or information support.
Even so, these resigned Investigators often suffer from mental and physical torment.
For those who have glimpsed a true corner of the world, living out their remaining years is a luxury fantasy.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49765_Title = {
    Text = "Investigator"
  },
  CollectionHall_49766_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Overview>
Special individuals among investigators, possessing stronger spirits than ordinary investigators.
They hold higher authority than investigators, granting them access to deeper secrets. The tasks they undertake are often the most complex and arduous.
In this prolonged war against dissolution, they stand at the forefront of humanity.

<Title:Selection>
Typically, special individuals selected by mythags during the investigator screening process.
When an individual reacts particularly strongly to the Silver Key, selectors will evaluate whether that individual can be trained as a keeper, based on the descriptions and entries in the "Keeper's Spirit Composition and Potential," supplemented by a period of observation.

<Title:Training>
Apart from basic theoretical courses and combat training, keepers undergo additional spirit power training.
They engage with Awakeners and execute field tasks earlier than other investigators to hone their abilities.

<Title:Keygrave Ceremony>
After evaluation, keepers participate in the Keygrave Ceremony alongside regular investigators to acquire their own Silver Key.
Unlike investigators, the Silver Key numbers of keepers begin with "K".
From then on, the Silver Key becomes a marker of the keepers' identity and provides significant support for future field tasks.

<Title:Keepers and Awakeners>
Keepers can use the power of Awakeners to combat dissolution. Thus, the ability to command Awakeners in battle is particularly crucial.
They undergo rigorous command training in the preparatory phase, and after the Keygrave Ceremony, must partake in a supervisor-led field task with their assigned Awakener to ensure they can independently execute future field tasks.

<Title:Retirement>
If a keeper is unable to perform field tasks for any reason, mythags respect their decision and transfer them to safer departments such as logistics or information support.
Keepers can retire by returning their key, sealing their files, and signing confidentiality agreements, but so far, very few have done so.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49766_Title = {Text = "Keeper"},
  CollectionHall_49767_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Awakener Linking>
During the shaping process, Awakeners are exposed to unknown pollution, making them highly susceptible to madness. As a result, Investigators must establish spiritual links to stabilize their minds. However, for the majority of Investigators, forming a Link with Awakeners requires the power of a Silver Key.
A Silver Key enhances the holder's Spirit, enabling them to maintain long-term Links with Awakeners, command them in battle, and provide Spirit Power assistance. Additionally, holders can also offer certain support to Awakeners through the Silver Key.
In theory, the stronger the holder's Spirit Intensity, the more Awakeners they can Link with. However, so far, only one person has been able to endure the mental strain of Linking with multiple Awakeners.

<Title:Awakening Ceremony>
The Awakening Ceremony conducted using a Silver Key is a mandatory course for every Investigator.
During the Awakening Ceremony, the Silver Key amplifies the user's perception of the target Silver, aiding in the enhancement of the Core's shaping, ultimately resulting in an Awakener with special Abilities.

<Title:Spirit Trace and Localization>
When separated from an Awakener, the holder can use a Silver Key to roughly locate Spirits matching the Awakener's characteristics through "Spirit Trace".
However, this does not guarantee that every located Spirit is an ally. Therefore, remain calm when performing "Spirit Trace".

<Title:Rift Closure>
Holders can use Silver Keys to close Dissolution Rifts. For further details, refer to Dissolution Rift - Response Methods.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_49767_Title = {
    Text = "Silver Key Application"
  },
  CollectionHall_49768_Desc = {
    Text = "<Title:Overview>\nEach Keeper possesses unique special abilities.\nAccording to Mythag's archives, the known abilities of Keepers include memory reading, emotion sharing, and psychological perception, among others.\n\n<Title:The First Keeper>\nThe first Keeper ever is Alistair Owens.\nTo most people, he is but a fleeting shadow in the crevices of history, known only to a select few who are aware that he still resides in the depths of Mythag.\nUnable to walk upright, it is said that this was a \"necessary sacrifice\" made for Mythag.\nAlistair is the most cost-effective personnel in Mythag: His stomach has already been completely removed, eliminating the need for food and significantly reducing meal expenses.\n\n<Title:New Keeper>\nThe abilities of the new Keeper are undoubtedly the most unique.\nThey can trigger insights through a certain object, emotion, or memory, stimulating the Silver Key to unleash new powers—this has nearly overturned the understanding of professional scholars and historians.\nEveryone knows this Keeper is destined to stir a new wave of turmoil.\nThe question is, where will this storm lead them?"
  },
