  CollectionHall_56369_Title = {
    Text = "World of Poetry"
  },
  CollectionHall_57597_Desc = {
    Text = "The current Bishop of the Londinium District and an Awakener accidentally Awakened by the previous bishop.\nA devout believer in the All-Father, he lived by the All-Father's teachings through his life, treating all living beings with compassion and tolerance, earning great respect among the crowd—some believers even called him \"the Saint of Londinium.\"\nIronically, it was precisely this compassion and mercy toward all living beings that cost him his life as a human.\nBefore his death, he attempted to cure Dissolution, sacrificing his own flesh to the Tablets of Life in an effort to alleviate suffering and prolong the lives of the \"patients\" in his diocese. After his death, the Tablet vanished—until he arose once more as an Awakener.\nHis eyes, hidden beneath cloth and bandages, can perceive the radiance of souls; thus, upon seeing the Keeper, he became certain: the Keeper is the Pale Messenger foretold by the All-Father, destined to save this world on the brink of darkness."
  },
  CollectionHall_57597_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"The Color of Blood\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57597_Title = {Text = "Salvador"},
  CollectionHall_57598_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The youngest king of the prehistoric civilization of Lemuria.
Gifted since birth, he slept over twenty hours a day and always appeared weary when awake.
Occasionally sensing the gods' emotions and dreaming fragments of various times and spaces, he was worshipped, revered, and honored as king.
The young king did not care. He merely passively evaded the gods' revelation and prophecy.
Ultimately, he foresaw the fate of Lemuria's destruction, yet knew not how to change it, and thus remained silent.
Until the day disaster struck and people fell into despair. To meet his subjects' expectations, he fabricated a false prophecy.
A prophecy concerning the Immortal King, and his return to the world.
In the end, the old world was submerged by floodwaters. Oceans turned to fields, and new humanity once again proliferated across the land, with no one left to remember the prehistoric era.
Perhaps he never expected his careless prophecy to be continuously emulated.
He ultimately underestimated the power of faith.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57598_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Tulu\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57598_Title = {Text = "Tulu"},
  CollectionHall_57599_Desc = {
    Text = [[
An outsider envoy of the Aramites, claiming to have come to Remouahe following the Dream Revelation.
Leading a group of Aramites who have long lingered outside the Storm Wall, she seeks the possibility of reviving the Aramites' sacred Mother Tree.
She is actually affiliated with the Church of the Lightbearers. No one yet knows the hidden truth behind her eternal compassionate smile; perhaps, as the journey continues, a glimpse may be caught.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57599_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 7: \"Desire's Flow\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57599_Title = {Text = "Juliette"},
  CollectionHall_57600_Desc = {
    Text = "Living in the prehistoric civilization of Lemuria, her entire family were devout spiritual practitioners.\nShe diligently cultivated her spirit from childhood, and upon growing up, she fulfilled her dream by entering the capital's Temple as a priest.\nShe yearned for a miracle, for ethereal experiences, yet they never came.\nWhen Tulu ascended the throne, she became the High Priestess serving beside him.\nThe first time she saw the new king, she felt overwhelming dizziness and joy; she instantly understood—he was the embodiment of the divine she had longed for.\nYes. The meaning of her existence was to serve this young king.\nEven when the flood submerged the continent and Lemuria's civilization beneath the sea, she never wavered in this belief."
  },
  CollectionHall_57600_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Dreamscape: \"Desecrate\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57600_Title = {Text = "Miryam"},
  CollectionHall_57601_Desc = {
    Text = "To scatter seeds across the boundaries between dimensions—and then, for the sake of love, to forsake the very reproductive imperative her kind was born to fulfill.\nSaya drifted into this universe by accident, awakened from a Silver Core discovered by Tinct, a traveler between the stars. Lost and searching, she lingered on a desolate planet—until she encountered the Keeper of Mythag. Through exploration and deep conversation, two utterly unlike beings arrived at the same answer to the question of what love means.\nMemory may blur. Memory may fade. But the bond once formed with those who matter will find her again. In a world saturated with forgetting, she holds fast to her affliction—the one she calls love."
  },
  CollectionHall_57601_LockTip = {
    Text = "Unlocks after Awakening \"Saya\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57601_Title = {Text = "Saya"},
  CollectionHall_57602_Desc = {
    Text = "In ancient legends, two great beasts exist in the world, dwelling respectively in the abyssal depths and east of Eden.\nThese two beasts can only meet when time reaches its end, and they will be offered as sacrifice to the Mother of Life, Tiamat, in exchange for the cycle of life.\nLotan is the \"Beast\" hidden behind the legend.\nShe is a natural product of the planet, and unlike the legend, she is both the Abyssal Waters and the Soul of Eden.\nShe is pure Chaos power, a wild free soul, and undefined order.\nDestruction and Rule are the powers bestowed upon her by the world; these two opposing instincts collide within Lotan. To balance the forces powerful enough to tear her apart, she must release her desire for destruction through battle.\nLotan has been entrusted by the Planet with the duty to guard history. Her \"work\" is to follow the Planet's will, eliminating and defeating those who influence the Planet's fate—though such individuals rarely emerge across millennia.\nIn the endless, boring wait for her mission to descend, Lotan yearns for the appearance of a rival.\nFor this reason, she once turned toward Lemuria's young king, even summoning the calamity of falling stars.\nYet none of this has diminished her surging battle will; they have only intensified with her revive."
  },
  CollectionHall_57602_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Lotan\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57602_Title = {Text = "Lotan"},
  CollectionHall_57603_Desc = {
    Text = "Once the crown prince of Necrovia, he is now revered as the god of deaths, the King of the Ghouls.\nA wise and fair young man, he was nonetheless regarded with suspicion by the royal family due to his unique \"taste\"—necrophagy.\nThe night before his abdication, the king poisoned Doresain. As his body was disassembled and devoured, his consciousness merged with the entity enshrined in the temple, allowing him to taste his own flesh.\nThe astonishing sweetness has haunted his dreams ever since.\nHe regards eating as a romantic art, not merely satisfying a primal hunger, but acting as a commemoration for what has been forgotten.\nDissolution destroys everything, letting the past fade with the wind.\nBut Doresain will bear witness to the legends and ordinariness of all living beings, preserving their blood and flesh within his memories—forever."
  },
  CollectionHall_57603_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Doresain\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57603_Title = {Text = "Doresain"},
  CollectionHall_57604_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Formerly a queen who ruled over a territory.
It is said that after her homeworld was destroyed by Dissolution, she crashed into the Cambrian Valley aboard a massive meteorite.
Skilled in livestock management, land consolidation, and risk investment management.
Whenever she travels, a vast procession of undead servants follows behind.
One serves as a footstool, two minstrels provide entertainment, and four act as carriage drivers...
Even the Pope would feel ashamed of his modest entourage upon seeing this.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57604_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Feast of Flames\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57604_Title = {Text = "Wanda"},
  CollectionHall_57605_Desc = {
    Text = "Tinct's sister, born with a dangerous \"Talent\" that stunted her growth within their shared womb.\nExiled as an infant for bringing misfortune, she survived only through Tinct's sacrifices—scavenging resources from the upper class while giving most to Faint's care.\nWhen disaster struck, Tinct secured their escape \"ticket\"—but at departure, Faint staged her first rebellion:\nShe emerged from the womb, threatening to drain the life energy of Everyone unless Tinct took the salvation meant for her.\nPlagued by self-loathing over her \"defective\" nature, she hides in basements and dark corners.\nEven her picky eating stems from childhood attempts to starve herself—one less burden for Tinct to bear."
  },
  CollectionHall_57605_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Faint\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57605_Title = {Text = "Faint"},
  CollectionHall_57606_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Kathigu-Ra is an orphan born in a desert region. When she was still a maiden, she had already taken in many local children who shared similarly tragic fates.
To lead these children in their struggle for survival, she meticulously crafted a false exterior to shield them from malicious harm.
To many, she is the embodiment of cruelty and madness.
In any conflict, she responds to those who dare stand before her gun with the most frenzied passion and the cruelest means.
Over time, even the babbling infants of the region came to know that upon the endless sea of sand, there exists an amber-colored reaper.
In a confrontation with N, she unsurprisingly lost that game, and thus lost everything.
But even N did not know that she had long been watched by an Old One from among the stars.
After experiencing her fated death, she duly inherited His power, as well as the mission He had set for her.
Within her resides a being from among the Stars; she has long been capable of becoming one of Them.
When that final moment inevitably arrives, she will cast aside everything and return once more to the highest heavens, becoming the first and last sanctuary.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57606_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Everburning Vex\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57606_Title = {Text = "Kathigu-Ra"},
  CollectionHall_57607_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Doll: Inferno was once the pride of Mythag. In the prolonged battle against Dissolution, she realized that while Dissolution was eroding the body, it also paved a path toward truth.
After accidentally coming into contact with an ancient tablet inscribed with cryptic words, she resolved to walk this dark and boundless path, forsaking the chance to prolong her life by replacing her doll body, and allowing Dissolution to corrode her brain case.
In the end, she got what she desired, gaining insight into the nature of Dissolution, but at the cost of complete destruction and oblivion.
Once the beacon-like belief and rationality that had guided everyone vanished, Doll: Inferno began unleashing destruction in places unseen by the school's faculty and students. After "assisting" in several fatal incidents, she was discovered by Mythag and placed under the highest level of surveillance and suppression.
Yet behind the collapsing mannequin, the immortal soul of a genius seemed to still be resonating with something far deeper and darker beyond the world.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57607_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Doll: Inferno\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57607_Title = {
    Text = "Doll: Inferno"
  },
  CollectionHall_57608_Desc = {
    Text = "A singer who rose from poverty to high society through beauty alone.\nWhen the disaster struck, mercy and favors earned her the last escape \"ticket\"—though everyone assumed she'd keep it for herself, she secretly intended it for her sister Faint.\nAt the final moment, Faint rebelled. With her supernatural power, she threatened to leave their protective cradle unless Tinct took the seat instead—forcing her sister's survival as the planet died.\n\nAwakening brought crushing guilt. Tinct now believes Faint survived... or perhaps revived in some form.\nShe searches obsessively, sparing no expense or danger in her quest."
  },
  CollectionHall_57608_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Tinct\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57608_Title = {Text = "Tinct"},
  CollectionHall_57609_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A genius scholar known as the "Brain of Mythag"and one of Mythag's external advisors. She was admitted at the age of 14 and revolutionized Alistair's life-support systems.
After contracting Dissolution during fieldwork, she spent her final days composing an 80-page Awakening manual.
Her followers obeyed its instructions, placing her Silver into the Awakening Device to create the "Awakener version of Doll".

She Awakened herself without fanfare: dressed herself, walked to the lab, and resumed her research.
Genius, it seems, cannot be interrupted even by death.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57609_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Doll\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57609_Title = {Text = "Doll"},
  CollectionHall_57610_Desc = {
    Text = "A spirit being who fled her Dissolution-devoured world by possessing a dead human.\nWhen Dissolution infected this new body, she became trapped—her essence bound to decaying flesh.\nPanic drove her to Mythag, where she traded her race's knowledge for Awakener conversion.\nNow she researches mechanics and spiritual energy, avoiding darkness and sleep—too terrified of Dissolution to study it directly."
  },
  CollectionHall_57610_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Winkle\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57610_Title = {Text = "Winkle"},
  CollectionHall_57611_Desc = {
    Text = "A spiritual entity formed in the gray seas of the astral plane.\nAfter millennia adrift, it followed psychic travelers to Earth, sampling desires and amassing heads in its Deep Sea to absorb their wisdom.\nSixteen centuries ago, when it possessed an Awakener who she subsequently beheaded, its true nature emerged—a spirit parasite that hunts more for sport than need.The original Shopkeeper of Daffodil's Shop tamed it, forging a bond so genuine the monster came to crave her death—to inherit her face, her shop, her legacy.\nNow it runs Daffodil's Shop properly, taking heads only through occult contracts, soothing its loneliness with customer chatter while guarding its beloved's city."
  },
  CollectionHall_57611_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"Phantom of the Rainy Town\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57611_Title = {Text = "Daffodil"},
  CollectionHall_57612_Desc = {
    Text = "She was once a traveling magician in life.\nGrowing up in a circus, her life was filled with many \"outcasts\"—thieves, fugitives, orphans, the disabled, and the deformed...\nCasiah belonged among them—born without capacity for emotion or empathy.\nA prodigious performer who kept enchanting audiences even after becoming a departed heretic. Her \"wonderland\" shows left spectators feeling hollow, their lives grayer until many chose suicide.\nBehind the curtain, she sips the sweet emotional essence harvested from their despair.\nThe price of spectacle? Merely sustainable nutrition."
  },
  CollectionHall_57612_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Casiah\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57612_Title = {Text = "Casiah"},
  CollectionHall_57613_Desc = {
    Text = "A timeline anomaly. Another possibility of Ramona, from an alternate dimension.\nDuring the crisis, she surrendered to her Awakener powers to preserve the Keeper's safety.\n@2's consciousness persists within her, warring for dominance and subjecting her to unending torment.\nShe maintains perfect appearances—impeccable hair, orderly routines—while secretly battling lapses into dazed states or sudden vocal shifts.\nWorry not: though born of different paths, her every action serves the Keeper and world's peace."
  },
  CollectionHall_57613_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"One Step Away\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57613_Title = {
    Text = "Ramona: Timeworn"
  },
  CollectionHall_57614_Desc = {
    Text = [[
She was born in a land of poetry and roses; she is the spirit of poetry.
The spirit wanders in dreams woven by words, rejoicing at the bloom of every ray of sunlight, weeping at the withering of every flower.
She muses, she grieves, she yearns for the companionship of another soul.
Later, in a courtyard blooming with flowers, a young gardener placed a rose before her.
And so she blushed and smiled, gently taking the flower.
"At last, I'm not alone anymore."
At that moment, she believed it wholeheartedly.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57614_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"Rose's Abode\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57614_Title = {Text = "Horla"},
  CollectionHall_57615_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The sole queen of the Aramites since ancient times.
As a child, she was revered as the messenger of the Holy Tree, delivering the Aramite king's decrees. After her first act of defiance, she was cast into the Aramites' Holy River as a sacrifice, yet Awakened the will of the tree.
Her flesh merged with the sap of the tree, and her blood flowed through the tree's roots. She is the Mother Tree, and the Mother Tree is her.
However, the power of Dissolution polluted the Aramites' lineage, and she willingly used her body to bear the corruption in place of the Mother Tree, seeking a sliver of hope for the Aramites.
Now that the Aramites have been lost to the tides of history, only the rise and collapse of the Mother Tree stands as a silent witness to the stories tied to her.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57615_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Thais\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57615_Title = {Text = "Thais"},
  CollectionHall_57616_Title = {
    Text = "Among the Stars"
  },
  CollectionHall_57617_Desc = {
    Text = "Mythag University's mental health specialist, tending to Investigators' psychological needs.\nWhile beloved for her gentle demeanor and kindness, certain members regard her with visceral terror.\nPerhaps it's the unidentifiable herbs in her tea, or perhaps it's that no one has ever seen her without a smile—either way, the effect chills to the bone."
  },
  CollectionHall_57617_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Prologue"
  },
  CollectionHall_57617_Title = {Text = "Sylvia"},
  CollectionHall_57618_Title = {Text = "The Fools"},
  CollectionHall_57619_Title = {Text = "Hybrid"},
  CollectionHall_57620_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Pickman\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57620_Title = {Text = "Outlanders"},
  CollectionHall_57621_Desc = {
    Text = "William is a senior investigator at Mythag, deeply respected by the junior Keepers. Once, for reasons he could scarcely bring himself to name, he had been too afraid to step beyond the campus walls, burying himself in research while quietly serving in the intelligence group. But after his friend's death, everything changed. He abandoned his old ways, throwing himself onto the front lines—doing what his friend once did, as if carrying out his unfinished work in his stead.\nNow, William keeps a broken Silver Key with him at all times, a fragile talisman against the slow erosion of memory."
  },
  CollectionHall_57621_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Prologue"
  },
  CollectionHall_57621_Title = {Text = "William"},
  CollectionHall_57622_Desc = {
    Text = "A gardener from Cité, Horla's childhood bosom friend.\nWhen Horla was most helpless, Colette brought her the most unforgettable joyful moments with a garden.\nWhen Horla's talent began to take root, Colette took away her wealth, fame, and life with a raging fire.\nShe collaborated with Herbert, using Horla's Poem to create the World of Poetry. Perhaps to memorialize her friend, perhaps to seize control. No one knows.\nColette has always claimed that among those beautiful verses, the only thing she ever understood was desire.\nShe suffers from it. She takes pride in it."
  },
  CollectionHall_57622_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"Rose's Abode\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57622_Title = {Text = "Colette"},
  CollectionHall_57623_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Miryam once encountered two Deborahs: one was a priestess of Lemuria, the other a maid of the Ornn family. One was her bosom friend, and the other was also her bosom friend.
Two eras separated by tens of thousands of years, two different individuals, yet the same name, the same face, the same kindness. It was a rare coincidence, and to Miryam, it was also a sacred omen.
Miryam witnessed the fates of both Deborahs: one sank beneath the sea with Lemuria, the other was sent by her own hand to the altar, disemboweled and slain.
Within this grand narrative about the Divine Realm, Deborah's story is merely two brief, crimson footnotes.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57623_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Dreamscape: \"Desecrate\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57623_Title = {Text = "Deborah"},
  CollectionHall_57624_Desc = {
    Text = "Mythag University's top information broker and a member of the school's Detective Association.\nPossesses unparalleled information gathering and excavation abilities, earning a modest reputation throughout Londinium.\nOriginally from the Aglo Republic, she came to Londinium due to family circumstances and successfully enrolled by leveraging the Mythag secrets she holds.\nDon't be deceived by her cheerful smile—her understanding of Mythag runs far deeper than most people realize."
  },
  CollectionHall_57624_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 1: \"East District's Enigma\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57624_Title = {Text = "Hannah"},
  CollectionHall_57625_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Former researcher of the Green Foundation, director of Rye Sanatorium.
After her husband and daughter died, she has been searching everywhere for a way to revive her daughter.
In the long quest, she forgot her daughter's face, and also forgot the love and warmth that once sustained her.
She only remembered the pain itself.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57625_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 4: \"Where Silence Reigns\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57625_Title = {Text = "Francis"},
  CollectionHall_57626_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Captain of the ship named Sona-Nyl.
His hometown was Dissoluted and wiped from people's memories, yet he alone remembers everything. Thus, people call him the madman.
The seaside town, family, siblings... these are all fragments of the past the madman desperately seeks to reclaim.
He made an agreement with Miryam: transporting the cargo she needs in exchange for her help in Awaken a long-dormant Memory.
And so, he saw the Maiden surrounded by gentle Wind and white birds.
"My name is Celeste. As long as you need me, I will remain here."
She is the trace of a homeland once real, a fairy tale he heard from the elders in his childhood.
So it was true, he thought. Those longed-for memories of the past were indeed real.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57626_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 6: \"Twisted Stars\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57626_Title = {Text = "Elton"},
  CollectionHall_57627_Desc = {
    Text = "An administrator of the Church of All-Father's Redemption in Londinium, responsible for assisting the Bishop and other clergy in maintaining the Church's daily operations.\nAfter her father's death, her capable older sister took over the family business and became a moderately successful merchant—everything seemed to be going so smoothly—until that meticulously orchestrated fraud.\nIn a single night, the mother and her three daughters were left with nothing. But that was alright; the Bishop of Londinium had extended his help, and as long as she had her family by her side, she feared no hardship.\nThen her sister died.\nHer mother, overcome with grief, fell into despair and passed away.\nMeanwhile, that shameless man who had seized her ancestral home was hosting art salons and indulging in pleasure.\nConfusion, anger, disbelief... countless emotions crowded in her chest, coalescing into hatred that threatened to crush her into Ashen Remains. But she shouldn't feel this way—the Bishop had said that those bound by the past could never move forward, and only forgiveness could bring liberation.\nShe couldn't do it.\n\n\"Don't force yourself to endure,\" the woman who called herself Lady Lantern whispered to her, gently persuading, \"To forgive is to condone. The righteous should be vindicated, and the wicked—the wicked deserve to be punished accordingly.\"\nAnd so she took the mirror from that lady's hand and began the ritual of Judgment."
  },
  CollectionHall_57627_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"The Color of Blood\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57627_Title = {Text = "Sophia"},
  CollectionHall_57628_Desc = {
    Text = "A slave of unknown origin, who once succeeded Goliath as the tribe's leader.\nAt the age of 8, he killed his master and hid inside a wooden barrel, drifting all the way to the Philistines' island.\nHe carries a base bloodline—weak, vulgar, and ambitious.\nHe was beheaded within a month of taking power, with his reign ranking 13th in terms of length compared to other leaders.\nBeing a Philistine leader isn't a position anyone can hold until retirement."
  },
  CollectionHall_57628_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"The Fall of A Giant\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57628_Title = {Text = "Iglenn"},
  CollectionHall_57629_Desc = {
    Text = "She was once the relay station of the eternal kingdom, controlling the gateway between the realm and the outside world, responsible for guiding lost subjects back home.\nWhen the kingdom fell into slumber and continuously plunged deeper into the sea vortex, Faros lost her link to her homeland.\nShe could no longer contact the capital, nor find any trace within the vast ocean.\nAs a lighthouse at sea, yet unable to illuminate the path home—how ironic.\nOver long and lonely ages, she gradually went mad and became dysfunctional, causing multiple marine disasters throughout history, until she was finally defeated by an ancient hero after exhausting her power.\nLater research even led some scholars to speculate that it was Faros's madness that caused the sinking of Atlantis.\nAll remains mere conjecture. To this day, the past of this fanatical believer remains a mystery."
  },
  CollectionHall_57629_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Faros\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57629_Title = {Text = "Faros"},
  CollectionHall_57630_Desc = {
    Text = [[
He was the son of a minor noble family from a duchy. Though born into nobility, his father achieved nothing, and his future seemed destined for an utterly ordinary life.
That changed when, during a Christmas banquet, his father brought him to meet the Duke. His attentive care for a sick Princess of the same age caught the Duke's attention, and in a moment of jest, the Duke named him a prepare knight of the duchy, marking the start of his formal training with the knightly order.
When war came, the duchy's weak army could not withstand the invading cavalry. Amidst the carnage, Ogier became the last "knight" to guard the Princess.
Clutching a spear still too tall for him, he stood forever before the Princess's private chamber.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57630_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"A Knight's Wish\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57630_Title = {Text = "Ogier"},
  CollectionHall_57631_Desc = {
    Text = "A genius ballerina who dances in flames.\nFor hundreds of years, her family has existed as court dancers. Thus, even as kingdoms changed and schools disappeared, she never lost her elegant and beautiful dance soul.\nAt the age of eighteen, she joined a local ballet troupe and quickly became the undisputed prima ballerina.\nHowever, after a successful debut, the troupe manager sent Liz into a wealthy merchant's room under the guise of \"introduction.\"\nIt turned out ballet had long ceased to be pure—its elegance had become capital for girls to raise their value.\nSo she ran away, was caught and brought back, then ran away again... Finally, her \"aloofness\" enraged those powerful figures.\nThey tormented Liz in both body and mind. She had to keep spinning, keep dancing, never stopping even as her toes shattered and blackened blood dripped onto the floor.\nFinally, during an ordinary performance, as the dance reached its climax, flames rose from the soles of her feet, spreading upward.\nShe would burn away all injustice and sin."
  },
  CollectionHall_57631_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Liz\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57631_Title = {Text = "Liz"},
  CollectionHall_57632_Desc = {
    Text = "Enslaved, adopted, abandoned... Up to this point, the story holds no difference from that of Helot in another timeline. Yet with the same blood, a divergent withered branch has finally been watered.\nIt was not until she fell into prison that true Hell began. To her horror, she discovered that her own people, who should have shared hatred toward the slavemaster, were now hating her as well—perhaps even more intensely.\nDay after day, she fell into eternal torment and pain. A gift of fate, with interest, crushed her spirit utterly.\nHer hatred, originally directed at the slavemaster, transformed into hatred for everyone, and in turn, she was hated by all, losing her place of existence.\nBy the time she escaped the prison through Dissolution, madness had completely consumed her heart. Clutching the strength she suddenly obtained, she eagerly unleashed her boundless resentment.\nThat night, the entire city was showered in crimson blood rain. Standing in the red river, she threw her head back and laughed heartily."
  },
  CollectionHall_57632_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Helot: Catena\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57632_Title = {
    Text = "Helot: Catena"
  },
  CollectionHall_57633_Desc = {
    Text = "Founder and leader of the Sculptors' Association.\nChildhood spinal meningitis confined him to home study, where he first contemplated the body's limitations. At Mythag, his mentor helped him discover his research focus—and inadvertently cure his own condition.\nBehind his perpetual warm smile lies complete emotional detachment.\nHis unkempt hair mirrors the chaos of his workspace, though one exception exists: Crowley's archived papers, meticulously organized in his desk drawer—the most orderly project Herbert has ever undertaken."
  },
  CollectionHall_57633_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 1: \"East District's Enigma\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57633_Title = {Text = "Herbert"},
  CollectionHall_57634_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The most valiant leader ever in the eyes of the Philistines.
Towering and powerfully built, within just a few years of rising to power, he led the Philistines to sweep through surrounding tribes, remaining undefeated to this day.
Amid praise and accolades, his renown grew, yet he ignored his people's warnings and committed the grave error of underestimating his enemy.
A minor mistake led to the Philistines' crushing defeat. Thus, he willingly accepted punishment and went into exile at sea with his sole follower.
Resentment, reluctance... This humiliating moment will be forever remembered. He would rather offer his fragile neck to the "Witch," if only to reclaim everything that was his.
He has already taken the bloody path of vengeance.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57634_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"The Fall of A Giant\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57634_Title = {Text = "Goliath"},
  CollectionHall_57635_Desc = {
    Text = "Once a lowly slave, her childhood brilliance and beauty seemed to seal her tragic fate.\nYet sudden fortune allowed her to take the place of the deceased daughter of the Regent family, becoming their obedient adopted daughter, and no one ever looked at her as a slave again.\nShe left home too young, and years of living together made her regard the gentle lady as her true mother—until she accidentally extended help to her former kin. The Regent, who deeply despised alliances among slaves, immediately cast her aside.\nFate cruelly revealed its unchanging face; overnight, she became a prisoner, fermenting hatred in her cage throughout her adolescence.\nWhen Dissolution erupted in the prison, she discovered that the black liquid could corrode her shackles, and thus the goddess of vengeance finally left her cell. Upon her return, she claimed the head of the Regent and brought full liberation to the Tyrians.\nThe rest of her life was spent hunting down former slave masters, until she turned into an anonymous grave inscribed with hymns of praise."
  },
  CollectionHall_57635_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Helot\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57635_Title = {Text = "Helot"},
  CollectionHall_57636_Title = {
    Text = "Dwellers of Darkness"
  },
  CollectionHall_57637_Desc = {
    Text = "Unlike the women of her time, who mostly served as medics on the battlefield, she was a valiant warrior in life and took great pride in it.\nShe firmly believed her homeland was holy, and that its conquest of other lands would bring a better future to the world.\nIn a fierce battle, she suffered severe injury while rescuing a young recruit. Though she barely survived, she was left with a permanent limp. Determined to continue serving her country, she remained in the military, leaving the front lines to become a trainer for new recruits.\nOver time, arrogant recruits who resented having a \"crippled\" instructor began gossiping about her within the ranks.\nWhen she realized this, she attempted to confront the very recruit she had saved—now a major. Yet even that soldier mocked her injured leg like the others.\nHumiliated, she stormed out of the military in rage.\nBeyond the army and battlefield, she finally saw the full picture of the world: \"war heroes\" betrayed by their own people, and the \"liberation\" she once took pride in had only brought colonization and suffering to the local residents.\nHer beliefs were shattered. From then on, she devoted herself entirely to true liberation, guided by a fierce sense of justice and guilt toward doing what was truly \"right.\"\nTragically, the infection in her wounded leg never healed, and she died in agony before her atonement was complete.\nAfter being Awakened once more and moved by Thais's kindness, she has always done her utmost to help the Aram Tribe endure and survive."
  },
  CollectionHall_57637_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Alva\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57637_Title = {Text = "Alva"},
  CollectionHall_57638_Desc = {
    Text = "Once the ancient Roman golem, a star gladiator, and the last remaining warrior.\nBorn to carry out the deranged will of Emperor Caligula, he eliminated all of the emperor's political rivals: his uncle, his brother, his sister...\nThe youth emperor knelt before the mountain of his relatives' corpses, arms raised high, both weeping and laughing.\nUvhash felt confused: the golem could cry, could laugh, but could not laugh heartily while tears poured down like rain.\nLater, the tyrannical emperor was executed. Before his execution, he embraced Uvhash.\nBut he said nothing.\nThe weapon, now masterless, wandered endlessly—until he found a new master.\nStill, he remains perplexed by humanity."
  },
  CollectionHall_57638_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Blood and Sand\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57638_Title = {Text = "Uvhash"},
  CollectionHall_57639_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Known as "Londinium's most dazzling Lustrous Pearl," every word and action is under the spotlight of countless eyes.
Once forged a contract with the most evil deity, then achieved rebirth through her own "death."
Regarding her identity, people have endless speculations.
Socialite, mistress, merchant, politician, queen of fashion...
Her hidden truth has long been blurred.
Or perhaps, this ever-changing nature is precisely her true self?]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57639_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"Tribute to the Rose\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57639_Title = {Text = "Sorel"},
  CollectionHall_57640_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Formerly a noblewoman of ancient Rome, her father ran a gladiator training camp.
Relying on the powerful gladiator slaves surrounding her, she wreaked havoc and acted arrogantly in Capua.
Ironically, in the end, she had to beg the slave she despised most to kill her.
Even more ironically, after becoming an Awakener, she unfortunate ran into that "Slave" again at Mythag.
Unsurprisingly, the scene that awaited them was anything but warm and tender.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57640_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Pale Descendant\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57640_Title = {Text = "Agrippa"},
  CollectionHall_57641_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A ship's saintess shaped by the ignorant traditions of sailors, she was in reality just a daughter sold by her impoverished family, bound to the mast day after day to safeguard the voyage.
A life devoid of freedom and choice left her neither sorrowful nor joyful, almost devoid of self, with the ship being her most familiar refuge.
Despite her powerless existence, people placed beautiful wishes upon her. Forbidden from speaking with the crew, she grew accustomed to spacing out, her gaze drawn only by the strongest of yearnings and the seabirds soaring beside the mast.
Eventually, when the ship she was meant to protect fell victim to Dissolution and suffered heavy casualties, the enraged people sentenced her to death by drowning.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57641_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Celeste\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57641_Title = {Text = "Celeste"},
  CollectionHall_57642_Desc = {
    Text = "A sculptor from Cité.\nReportedly born into a prestigious family, they broke ties with their kin in pursuit of art, journeying alone to Cité to study under the renowned master sculptor August.\nPossessing talent so extraordinary it borders on despair, yet never leaving a single word in the annals of art history.\nAfter becoming an Awakener, they gained a new understanding of sculpture and carving, transforming into the kind of \"mad artist\" everyone knows.\nThey now regard the Keeper as a fresh source of insight, their gaze toward the Keeper always carrying a faint trace of eerie tenderness.\nAh, that is the pure, unadulterated look of someone appraising a beloved material."
  },
  CollectionHall_57642_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Melodic Sculpting\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57642_Title = {Text = "Sanga"},
  CollectionHall_57643_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Once a maid of the ancient Achaemenid Dynasty.
Failed to be chosen to serve guests at the Centennial Banquet, she drowned her companion in the lake and took her place.
Finally transformed into a hideous green monster during the banquet.
Possesses a nimble mind and agile body, capable of carrying ten plates at once while weaving through the crowd.
Her definition of cuisine is severely disconnected from contemporary culinary culture.
She occasionally wonders if her transformation into a monster is punishment for murder.
But she never learns from it, quickly pretending nothing happened.
After all, the only lesson Erivan people ever take from history is:
Erivan people never learn lessons.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57643_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Karen\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57643_Title = {Text = "Karen"},
  CollectionHall_57644_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The prison guard stationed at @2. She takes great pleasure in tormenting prisoners.
Her superiors once promised her a transfer back to Londinium after three years, but due to the worsening of the Dissolution Phenomenon and shifts in the Ley Lines, she was forgotten in this remote land.
Pandia did not lose heart. She remained steadfast in the ruins, waiting for the day she would be recalled.
Until the last prisoner died, she became the only living being on the island.
What difference is there between a guard without prisoners and a prisoner?
Pandia refused to ponder. She continued to wait for the day of her recall.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57644_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Pandia\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57644_Title = {Text = "Pandia"},
  CollectionHall_57645_Title = {
    Text = "Out of the Aeons"
  },
  CollectionHall_57646_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Francis's "pet."
Originally a lively Maiden named "Lisa," she was transformed by the Sculptors' Association into a Distorted human-animal hybrid, and later adopted by Lily, temporarily living within the asylum.
Despite losing her human appearance and ability to speak, Koum retains part of Lisa's mind, capable of conveying her intention through simple physical gestures.
She has made her own choice.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57646_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 4: \"Where Silence Reigns\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57646_Title = {Text = "Koum"},
  CollectionHall_57647_Desc = {
    Text = "An enigmatic pharmacist, currently serving as the scientific advisor to the Sculptors' Association.\nIt is said his mother was a rural peasant woman, chosen to bear the offspring of the Great Serpent God.\nHe inherited his mother's albinism and gentle disposition, making him the only friend Herbert truly trusts.\nPassionate about anatomy, aromatic hydrocarbons, and the scent of burning belladonna.\nProlific author, best known for \"Materia Medica,\" hailed as the bible of toxicology.\nLong-term immersion in various poisons has rendered even his exhaled breath highly toxic. Keep your distance—this is your last warning."
  },
  CollectionHall_57647_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 2: \"Waxen Legacy\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57647_Title = {Text = "Albino"},
  CollectionHall_57648_Desc = {
    Text = "Ward Philips' protégé and Mythag's inaugural Keeper.\nHe dwells in secret underground chambers unknown to most, sustaining himself through extraordinary spiritual power and esoteric means to protect Mythag.\nConvinced that the Keeper will prove pivotal in coming upheavals, he grants them unprecedented access to his counsel: both to nurture their talent and to observe their every move."
  },
  CollectionHall_57648_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 2: \"Waxen Legacy\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57648_Title = {Text = "Alistair"},
  CollectionHall_57649_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A human born with a faint Seafarer bloodline, hailing from the ancient House of Ornn. This family once suffered a disease wherein some members would gradually transform into hideous monsters after reaching adulthood, ultimately dying in agony; his father, unable to bear the mutation, committed suicide shortly after his birth.
Growing up under his mother's disdain and peers' bullying, he became dark and reclusive in personality.
At sixteen, upon discovering obscure references to the family's noble bloodline in his uncle's remaining manuscripts, he attained a sense of spiritual victory, spending each day fantasizing about one day gaining transcendent power, interpreting others' cruelty as trials destined for a chosen one, eagerly anticipating the day they would grovel before him.
Upon reaching adulthood, he hid in a cave to undergo metamorphosis, yet remained stuck halfway between human and fish, and was shrieked at and driven away by his mother, unable to return home.
In the end, he leapt into the sea in desperate search of his kin, only to drown due to underdeveloped gills.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57649_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Caecus\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57649_Title = {Text = "Caecus"},
  CollectionHall_57650_Desc = {
    Text = [[
From the oldest Cavendish family in the kingdom, once the cherished Lustrous Pearl of her parents, she unfortunately contracted Dissolution.
Locked underground for three years, her craving for Bloodfeast grew stronger each day.
Her brother thus ordered people to scour the East District for stray homeless men and streetwalkers, using them as his sister's daily "food."
For a time, panic spread throughout the city, and the police force launched a full-scale operation, finally arresting the siblings.
Thus, the "Vampire Event," which had shocked the city of Londinium, finally came to an end.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57650_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Leigh\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57650_Title = {Text = "Leigh"},
  CollectionHall_57651_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A textile worker from the East District of Londinium.
Infected with Dissolution, she was abducted by the Sculptors' Association and turned into a wax sculpture.
"24" is both her experimental number and the initial count of her diagnosed personalities.
As this report is being written, the number of her personalities continues to grow.
Given time, the kingdom composed of "24"s will surely flourish in population.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57651_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"Serene Fission\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57651_Title = {Text = "\"24\""},
  CollectionHall_57652_Desc = {
    Text = [[
She was infected with Dissolution along with her father, enduring treatment obediently amidst her family's suffering.
After losing both her husband and daughter, her mother's personality changed drastically. During an exploration in Elworth, she accidentally stumbled upon a Church of the Lightbearers ritual and inadvertently Awakened Lily. Due to the abnormal Awakening, Lily became a blank-eyed doll, only responding when given commands.
Her mother, her memory of Lily's appearance lost to Dissolution, regarded the awakened Lily as a Monster and continuously performed experiments, hoping for the true daughter's Revival.
Eventually, she followed the Keeper to Mythag, calling the Keeper her "Mother" and becoming deeply dependent on them.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57652_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"The Magic of Stories\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57652_Title = {Text = "Lily"},
  CollectionHall_57653_Desc = {
    Text = "Rogers' wax doll.\nJust like those noisy kids in the carriage, he's a spoiled brat.\nAll he relies on are his gray-green eyes—the only thing \"Mr. Wax Sculpture\" left to Rogers.\nHe once encountered an irresistible force in \"24\"'s Artificial Domain and got smashed into a flat piece of George, successfully provoking Rogers' anger."
  },
  CollectionHall_57653_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 2: \"Waxen Legacy\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57653_Title = {Text = "George"},
  CollectionHall_57654_Desc = {
    Text = [[
An orphan from the Lilian's Workhouse and Jenkin's closest companion.
Once a human experiment subject of the Sculptors' Association and witnessed the Amber-Tinted Death of other orphans, she feels immense guilt over her survival and silence.
Ultimately, she jumped from the clock tower and finally freed herself from the suffering.
Always holds a teddy bear in her arms, which she named "Bobo."
Loves A Gift, little skirts, and golden candies.
Afraid of the dark, she only dares to sleep while holding "Bobo." If you could sing her a lullaby, the Girl will forever be grateful to you, love you.
Just as Jenkin once did for her.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57654_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Aigis\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57654_Title = {Text = "Aigis"},
  CollectionHall_57716_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Originally a researcher obsessed with creating automatons, she received a Silver-based power unit from Daffodil.
Due to her researcher friend's coveting of the power unit, they argued repeatedly, ultimately causing a laboratory explosion during a fiercely angry struggle. She awoke in terror within the automaton's body, realizing with horror: inside the lifeless automaton, alongside her, existed another consciousness.
No one knows what belief drove her to save her friend from the burning ruins, or what belief led her to the outskirts. This unknown mechanical genius vanished from the world, leaving only a news report about the explosion, scattered parts across the ground, and one surviving Silver.
What kind of being has been Awakened from it?]]
  },
  CollectionHall_57716_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Twisted Core\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57716_Title = {Text = "Erica"},
  CollectionHall_57717_Desc = {
    Text = "@2's emissary who walks the world in human guise.\nA pure demon devoid of future, faith, or ideals, nourished by desire and chaos.\nHis contracts always damn their signers—no loophole exists, no lawyer outwits Him.\nSometimes He wears a child's face, though none mistake this for innocence.\nAfter all, true terror needs no monstrous visage."
  },
  CollectionHall_57717_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"Tribute to the Rose\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57717_Title = {Text = "\"N\""},
  CollectionHall_57718_Desc = {
    Text = "A psychiatrist specializing in epilepsy, hysteria, and anxiety induced insomnia.\nHer hypnotic techniques extract patients' deepest secrets—coincidentally, her clients invariably die by elaborately \"artistic\" suicides.\nDubbed \"Londinium's secret-keeper\" for her celebrity clientele, she always reinvents herself before authorities intervene.\nRogers numbered among her long-term patients; some speculate his morbid artistry stems from her influence."
  },
  CollectionHall_57718_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 1: \"East District's Enigma\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57718_Title = {Text = "Clementine"},
  CollectionHall_57719_Desc = {
    Text = "Rogers, a wax sculptor dedicated to excellence and the current director of the Rogers Wax Museum.\nAs a child, he was ostracized due to his stutter and was mocked with the phrase \"so poor he's left with nothing but money.\"\nWith a high-ranking father, a mentally unstable mother, and that nationally shocking kidnapping case...\nUnder the combined weight of these tragic circumstances, Rogers lived up to expectations by transcending his mother, becoming Scarborough's foremost madman.\nThe most popular member among ladies in the Sculptors' Association—a gentleman of extreme emotional stability, as long as art is not discussed."
  },
  CollectionHall_57719_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 2: \"Waxen Legacy\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57719_Title = {Text = "Rogers"},
  CollectionHall_57720_Desc = {
    Text = "Nautila's mother was an outstanding mechanic, widely sought after for her skill and affordable prices.\nWhen she was eight, her father went out to sea and never returned. From then on, Mother and she ran the repair shop together, relying on each other. Using salvaged parts they saved up, she tried building a unicycle motorcycle, dreaming of riding it together one day—fulfilling her mother's long-held wish.\nWhen she was thirteen, her mother passed away from illness. To obtain more parts and finish the motorcycle, she took on a high-paying mission to accompany a ship.\nOn the return voyage, the ship was caught in a storm and swept into the current. She gave the only diving suit to her friend, and holding her mother's Nautilus pendant, died in the waters of Dissolution. Only her wreckage and silver core drifted through the ocean currents, traveling endlessly."
  },
  CollectionHall_57720_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Nautila\""
  },
  CollectionHall_57720_Title = {Text = "Nautila"},
  CollectionHall_58148_Desc = {
    Text = "A little princess reared by the High Priestess of the Deep Sea, revered as their \"Holy Maiden.\"\nRaised in pampered luxury since childhood, she is a true lady. The small parasol in her hand not only protects her delicate skin but also keeps all impurities and ominous things at bay.\nEven though she knows deep down that she herself is a product of some \"ill omen\"—her birth defying natural laws, destined to become the \"Mother\" and give birth to the prophesied child.\nEndless pastries, the latest fashionable gowns, countless servants revolving around her... She moves through this world of abundant material comforts, locking away her inner fear and unease.\nThis attempt ultimately fails, for a free heart accepts no compromise."
  },
  CollectionHall_58148_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Murphy\""
  },
  CollectionHall_58148_Title = {Text = "Murphy"},
  CollectionHall_59454_Desc = {
    Text = "A little girl from a coastal fishing village, her parents crew members who worked on long-distance fishing vessels, lived with her grandmother, naively believing the fairy tale her grandmother made up—that their family were descendants of Atlantis, and as long as she grew up obediently and made many friends, those friends would help her return to her homeland beneath the sea.\nAfter her grandmother passed away, the owner of an aquarium hired her as a cheerful and lively tour guide when coming to collect fish, allowing her to luckily enjoy a colorful childhood.\nWhen polluted fish suffering from Dissolution contaminated the entire aquarium, it was forced to declare bankruptcy. After losing her job, she took her favorite jellyfish, sealed in a bottle, back to her remote village. But soon, Dissolution corroded her, and then the entire village...\nAfter being awakened, her memories became fragmented and chaotic. She firmly believes she is one of the so-called \"Deep Sea People,\" and tirelessly extends the invitation to friends, urging them to visit her underwater homeland."
  },
  CollectionHall_59454_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Psyche Deepdive: \"Eadem Omnia\""
  },
  CollectionHall_59454_Title = {Text = "Aurita"},
  CollectionHall_59455_Desc = {
    Text = "A man hailed as possessing \"absolute luck.\"\nWith such a talent, becoming a gambler was only natural.\nYet he was also a fairly skilled detective.\nMoreover, he was penniless, as he could always squander his winnings at the fastest possible rate.\nParadoxical, complex. This is our complete assessment of the man.\nThe goddess of Fate favored him, the mysterious \"N\" favored him, and even the stingiest tavern owner was willing to give him a discount.\nEveryone favored him, yet he never stopped—instead, he launched into a new round of adventurous games.\nHe only favored the unknown."
  },
  CollectionHall_59455_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Special Ops: \"Happy Hunting!\""
  },
  CollectionHall_59455_Title = {Text = "Ryker"},
  CollectionHall_59456_Desc = {
    Text = "Born into a declining noble family, she had been given abundant love and care by her parents despite suffering from severe asthma since birth.\nConfined to the house due to her illness and frequently plagued by suicidal thoughts, her parents took her on a rare long journey to lift her spirits, only for her to unexpectedly contract Dissolution.\nUpon returning home, her parents, filled with guilt, sent her to a sanatorium while they traveled the seas to earn medical expenses and searched the world for a cure.\nAs Dissolution advanced, her desire for death grew stronger, yet burdened by guilt over troubling her parents, she continued to endure her longing for death and release.\nAfter receiving news that her parents had drowned in a shipwreck while en route to visit her, having no further attachments to the mortal world, she quietly left the sanatorium at night, walking step by step into the depths of the sea.\nAt the moment the seawater covered her head, the black fluid dripping from the triangular D-Mark dispersed, and her long-suffering body experienced indescribable relief—this was the first time, and the only time, she was able to breathe freely."
  },
  CollectionHall_59456_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Nymphaea\""
  },
  CollectionHall_59456_Title = {Text = "Nymphaea"},
  CollectionHall_61045_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Investigation Stage 8-1"
  },
  CollectionHall_61045_Title = {
    Text = "A Minor: Final Symphony"
  },
  CollectionHall_62183_Title = {
    Text = "08 Last Symphony"
  },
  CollectionHall_62184_Desc = {
    Text = "World-renowned conductor and musician whose youth belies his global acclaim.\nWhile the public knows nothing of Hameln's origins, the Mystia Treaty Committee noticed his concert venues overlapped suspiciously with Lightbearer Church activities.\nDuring their investigation, the Church assaulted Mythag—with Hameln conducting the invasion.\nHis true stage was never the concert hall."
  },
  CollectionHall_62184_LockTip = {
    Text = "Unlock after completing Main Story Chapter 8 \"Last Symphony\""
  },
  CollectionHall_62184_Title = {Text = "Hameln"},
  CollectionHall_65503_Title = {
    Text = "Elworth's Returnee"
  },
  CollectionHall_65509_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A street kid from East Londinium, and also the younger sister of "24."
She possesses three unique skills: stealing, arguing, and fleeing at the first sign of trouble.
No one ever gets the better of her.
Oh, right. She also has a little mouse named "Brown" who's always by her side.
Brown is mature and steady, forming a perfect complement to Jenkin's personality.
Therefore, even though there are tragic cases in Londinium's East District of starving people cooking mice, Jenkin has never entertained such thoughts.]]
  },
