  },
  CollectionHall_70839_Desc = {
    Text = "Flattery, pettiness, hypocrisy. The matron of Lilian's Workhouse was like a clumsy actor, playing the role of a humble beggar in Londinium's social arena.\nShe ran around tirelessly, using awkward flattery to beg for scraps of money from celebrities, struggling to keep the Workhouse running. She swallowed insults and mockery alone, soothing the Children of the Workhouse to sleep with gentle songs.\nLondinium had abandoned them, but Lilyan Workhouse had not. Sarah was ready, determined to do everything in her power to protect these children and help them survive the mist and cold winds of Londinium.\nBut her humble dream failed. She and the Children perished in the conspiracy of the Sculptors' Association. To the Sculptors' Association, she and the Children she cherished were mere grains of sand beneath their grand edifice—devoid of value, lacking in beauty. Their lives meant nothing; their deaths were not worth mentioning.\nShe burned herself completely. The flame quickly extinguished, leaving only the icy wind of Londinium as bitterly cold as ever."
  },
  CollectionHall_70839_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 1"
  },
  CollectionHall_70839_Title = {Text = "Sarah"},
  CollectionHall_70884_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:A.F.185>
Representatives from various countries signed the "Mystia Agreement" at the Constante Federation, deciding to cooperate to resist the disaster and suppress Dissolution fractures, while reaching a consensus on concealing the existence of hidden disaster and the guidelines regarding the D-Phenomenon.
This agreement states that the academy will remain independent, not belonging to any one country, and will have the right to establish branches in various countries, communicate directly with the leaders of each country, and obtain information related to the disaster and Dissolution from each country.
Mythag officially becomes a completely neutral transnational organization.

<Title:A.F.186>
The personnel involved in the revision and signing of the Mystia Agreement established a permanent Committee, which holds its own action team to ensure the implementation of the agreement. A closed-door meeting was established, fundamentally establishing the organizational structure.

<Title:A.F.187>
Mythag College was formally renamed Mythag University.
In the time that followed, the D-Phenomenon occurred more frequently and increased in scale. Mythag University stood on the front lines, becoming the backbone of humanity's resistance against Dissolution.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_70884_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 9-13"
  },
  CollectionHall_70885_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:A.F.75>
Alistair foresaw the emergence of a massive fissure within the Kingdom of Leo, and Ward led the investigators to respond. Many investigators sacrificed their lives during this incident.

<Title:A.F.77>
The rift cannot be closed, but it is gradually stabilizing. With the cooperation and support of the government, Ward has built the "Eye of Truth" base above the massive fissure.
The massive fissure is officially designated as L-01, also known as the "Black Pool."

<Title:A.F.88>
The "Black Pool" suddenly mutated and began to spread outward. At this time, the "Eye of Truth" in the surrounding areas suffered heavy losses, and Ward was also injured during the response.
Due to the inability to close the Black Pool, Tawil personally descended into it to maintain a temporary stability.

<Title:A.F.90>
The Eye of Truth base expansion, Mythag College was established, with Ward as the first Principal.
At this point, people began to systematically train Investigators with sufficient spirit power to better resist the escalating threat of Dissolution.

<Title:A.F.92>
Ward's injuries from the Black Pool incident further deteriorated, leading to his death.
The remains of Ward are buried within the academy, with the tombstone shaped like a key, marking the beginning of the Keygrave tradition at Mythag.
The Silver extracted after death was crafted into a Silver Key by Alistair, assigned the ID K-0001. Thereafter, Alistair became the first Keeper, active in the outside world.
In the same year, Khlarcus, who went to Remouahe to investigate the healing methods of Ward, went missing and has since been untraceable.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_70885_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 9-13"
  },
  CollectionHall_70886_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:A.F.306>
Herbert receives funding from the Green Foundation and, with the help of the Church of the Lightbearers, establishes the Sculptors' Association.
In the same year, Doll enrolls at Mythag University. As a genius scholar, Doll directly participates in the research conducted by graduate students and PhD candidates upon joining, greatly advancing the development of Silver chip technology at Mythag in the following days.

<Title:A.F.307>
Herbert and the Church of the Lightbearers attack Mythag University, attempting to retrieve the "Saintess" who was swapped out years ago.

<Title:A.F.309>
William, a survivor of a Dissolution event, joins Mythag University under the recommendation of Investigator Fingal.

<Title:A.F.310>
The Mythag University Joint Review Committee arrests most members of the Sculptors' Association before it can further expand. Herbert and several core members escape and go underground. Later, Herbert approaches Rogers to collaborate.
In the same year, Salvador succeeds as the Bishop, and Czort serves as the acting dean.

<Title:A.F.313>
At Herbert's instruction, Rogers donates to Lilian's Workhouse, becoming its sole benefactor.

<Title:A.F.314>
The Yakutsk explosion occurs.
At the behest of Alistair, William and Ramona go to Yakutsk, finding the amnesiac @3 in the ruins after the explosion, and bringing them back to Mythag University for special training.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_70886_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 9-13"
  },
  CollectionHall_70887_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:A.F.263>
Francis was born.

<Title:A.F.289>
After losing her daughter, Francis joined an expedition team and journeyed to Elworth. In the same year, the entire expedition team perished.

<Title:A.F.290>
Rogers was born. In the same year, after accidentally summoning Lily in Elworth, Francis traveled to Rye, where she established a Sanatorium with the help of the Foundation and froze a small space in time.

<Title:A.F.292>
Doll was born.

<Title:A.F.297>
Herbert enrolled in Mythag as a new student at the age of 17.

<Title:A.F.298>
The Church of the Lightbearer attempted a Ritual of Descent with their Twin Divi. Dexter sneaked into the ceremony, secretly taking away Ramona, who was about to be used as the Divine Vessel, and stopped the Ritual. 
The Ritual was declared a failure. Ramona became Dexter's adopted daughter.

<Title:A.F.300>
Rogers was kidnapped by "Mr. Wax." Mr. Wax later died, and Rogers was rescued. 
In the same year, Salvador was Awakened by the bishop of the Church of All-Father's Redemption and began serving as an assistant priest in the Church.

<Title:A.F.304>
Czort enrolled in Mythag as a new student.

<Title:A.F.305>
Herbert Rosenthal, a Mythag Awakening Major student, illegally created an experimental Awakener. After his actions were exposed, Herbert killed his mentor Crowley and fled, at the age of 25.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_70887_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 9-13"
  },
  CollectionHall_70888_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:B.F. ???>
A global disaster destroyed vast land areas. Earthquakes, floods, magnetic field disturbances, and abnormal climates occurred in succession, with cities and settlements sinking into the water, and solid rocks that were once buried deep in the sea becoming new peaks. Human Civilization suffered a heavy blow.

<Title:A.F. 0>
The old land was submerged by the sea, while new land surfaced. 
In this world that has been completely transformed, people abandoned the Old Calendar, struggling to rebuild using the remnants of Civilization, entering a new era: After Flood (A.F.).]]
  },
  CollectionHall_70888_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 9-13"
  },
  CollectionHall_70888_Title = {
    Text = "B.F.???—A.F.0"
  },
  CollectionHall_70889_Desc = {
    Text = [[
<Title:A.F.55>
Khlarcus actively sought out the Silver Key Society through his investigations and other means, successfully joining in the hope of leveraging the Society's power to aid humanity in rebuilding.
That year, Khlarcus noticed the actions of Ward and Tawil, and began to pay attention to their movements.

<Title:A.F.58>
Khlarcus created a disposable Silver Key, becoming the new leader of the secret society: the Keymaker, who began to quietly spread knowledge to help humanity rebuild.
That year, Khlarcus contacted Ward and Tawil, promising to provide Ward with certain financial and manpower assistance.

<Title:A.F.62>
Alistair Owens was born into an ordinary family of village doctors in the suburbs of Londinium.

<Title:A.F.64>
Khlarcus, having completed the investigation, acknowledged Ward's pursuit. Faced with Ward's unwillingness to be bound by the rules of the Silver Key Society, both parties reached an equal cooperative relationship under Tawil's suggestion and Silent Witness.
After receiving assistance in funding and manpower for the secret meeting, Ward's research advanced further, confirming the characteristics of Dissolution and the relationship between Dissolution and Mutants. He also initially summarized the different stages and characteristics of Dissolution Erosion.

<Title:A.F.65>
Khlarcus, Ward, Tawil, along with several members of the secret meeting, formed the first Investigator team dedicated to tracking down and preventing the spread of Dissolution, naming it the "Eye of Truth."

<Title:A.F.70>
Ward summarized the characteristics and patterns of dissolution and dissolution erosion again, initially recording the regional characteristics of dissolution, and wrote "Preliminary Study on Dissolution and Its Patterns" for the new members of the investigation team to review and use.

<Title:A.F.72>
Ward rescued Alistair from a family destroyed by dissolution and took him as a student.
On the same year, Ward's "Eye of Truth" gradually expanded, attracting the attention of those in power.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_70889_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 9-13"
  },
  CollectionHall_70890_Desc = {
    Text = "<Title:A.F.30>\nWard Philips was born into a wealthy merchant family in the ancient city of Shalom in the eastern part of the Aglo Republic. \n\n<Title:A.F.38>\nKhlarcus was born. Shortly after birth, his parents passed away, leaving him to rely on his sister as they struggled to survive. \n\n<Title:A.F.48>\nFrom a young age, Ward showed a talent for chemistry and physics, and at 18, he was admitted to the chemistry department of Moswetuset State University, becoming a student of the renowned chemist Nathaniel Milton. \n\n<Title:A.F.50>\nWard's grandfather, old Roger Phillips, the priest, passed away, and soon after, his father went missing. Ward investigated at the family home and followed in his father's footsteps to the Kingdom of Leonia, where he discovered a long-hidden family secret—a mysterious formula obtained from the pagans (Silver Key Society) during the witch-hunting era. \nThe ancient formula was recorded on a piece of parchment, much of which was damaged, and after years of experimentation, Ward managed to piece it together. \n\n<Title:A.F.53>\nBased on the completed formula, Ward successfully created the first Silver Key. Due to flaws in the formula, this Silver Key was destroyed after a single use and could not be used again. \nRegardless, with this one-time Silver Key, Ward met the Proxy of the Aeon of Sagacity, Tawil, and learned from Tawil that the world was about to face a \"Dark Catastrophe.\" \nDetermined to prevent the disaster, Ward reached an agreement with Tawil, linking with him to obtain the method for creating an Awakener and the complete Silver Key formula. \nIn the time that followed, Ward traveled extensively, studying Dissolution and fissures, naming them, and attempting to find ways to resist Dissolution."
  },
  CollectionHall_70890_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Chapter 9-13"
  },
  CollectionHall_70891_Desc = {
    Text = [[
After a year of preparatory study and training, @3 officially assumed the role of Keeper and began leading Awakeners and other campus forces in investigating dissolution-related events.
In the same year, the Church of the Lightbearers collaborated with internal traitors to invade Mythag once again, triggering turmoil in the Black Pool, opening the Ultimate Gate, and drawing the attention of the Supreme Will.
As Kadath was on the verge of being devoured by dissolution, @3 absorbed the Authority of the Three Aeons, confronting the Gaze of the Supreme Will within the Gate.
In the end, the Supreme Will fell back into slumber, and Kadath was saved.
@3 sacrificed {Male=his,Female=her} life.
Since all records related to {Male=him,Female=her} will be forever lost to Dissolution, Mythag decided to make an exception and seal the Silver Key {Male=he,Female=she} used during life, storing it in the campus history museum to commemorate {Male=his,Female=her} achievements.
No one knows {Male=his,Female=her} name, but the number K-0617 will endure through the ages.]]
  },
