  CollectionHall_90415_Title = {
    Text = "Beyond the Skies: Part I"
  },
  CollectionHall_90416_Desc = {
    Text = "One of a series of experiments cultivated by the Church of the Lightbearers, who luckily survived being discarded into the waste heap due to being born as twins.\nRaised alongside his younger brother Pollux as Divus from childhood, he underwent strict discipline and was constantly indoctrinated with the theology of the Lightbearer. The only exposure to the outside world was a beautifully crafted, heavy manuscript offered by a believer.\nAs a youth, after his brother underwent a cruel transformation ritual by the Church, the two decided to escape together in search of freedom, but were quickly recaptured.\nHe was submerged in the Dissolution pool known as the \"Pool of Sin,\" where the Sin-Effacement Rite was used to heal his wounds, enduring prolonged torment.\nUltimately, he was forgotten by everyone except Juliette—including Pollux—and his relationship with his brother grew strained.\nSince then, he has remained in dormancy, outwardly feigning obedience to the Church while never abandoning his obsession to escape with his brother again, patiently awaiting another chance to regain freedom."
  },
  CollectionHall_90416_LockTip = {
    Text = "Awaken \"Castor\""
  },
  CollectionHall_90416_Title = {Text = "Castor"},
  CollectionHall_94552_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Event: \"The Great Conquering: Divine Predation\""
  },
  CollectionHall_94552_Title = {
    Text = "The Great Conquering: Divine Predation"
  },
  CollectionHall_94553_Desc = {
    Text = "Pollux was one of the artificial twin test subjects created by the Church of the Lightbearers for a divine incarnation ritual. Just as they were deemed failures and about to be ruthlessly disposed of, Pollux was miraculously born, splitting from his brother's very flesh and blood.\nThis fierce, desperate attachment to life was not a blessing. It merely changed their destiny from a short-lived tragedy to a far more protracted one.\nPerhaps due to the mystery of their twin nature, his skin tone and personality were the complete opposite of his brother's. As the more lively and clever twin, he constantly engaged in mischievous behaviors that defied their strict indoctrination, much like a naughty boy in a normal family—that is, until he was selected to be a vessel for the divine and subjected to regular, painful, and bloody \"Divine Transformation\" rituals.\nUnable to endure the agonizing and hopeless fate, he pleaded and schemed with his brother. Over several years, they used a secret code to plan their escape and finally broke through numerous obstacles.\nHowever, their freedom was short-lived. They were soon captured by the Church's pursuers. Juliette ordered that his wings of freedom be clipped, and he was subjected to extreme brainwashing. This ultimately made him completely forget his brother and instead enjoy the feeling of being a revered figure, a Divus.\nAfter his second escape, Pollux recovered his memories due to his brother's death and the effects of the incarnation ritual. His \"Sacred Heart\" was ignited by hatred and rage, and he set his life on a new course: confronting and destroying the Church of the Lightbearers."
  },
  CollectionHall_94553_LockTip = {
    Text = "Clear Dreamscape \"Beyond the Horizon: II\""
  },
  CollectionHall_94553_Title = {Text = "Pollux"},
  CollectionHall_95436_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Up, up the bird struggled, wings beating against the cruel weight of the world, each desperate thrust carrying him further into the storm's embrace. 
Yet he did not know an invisible thread had always been tied to his foot. Even in flight, he was but a pitiful kite.
And now, the string was tightening.]]
  },
