  CollectionHall_98636_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The desecrators unleashe a cataclysmic wave, but the solitary king meets the roaring tide alone.
His hair flutters in the wind, his bones and blood his solemn proclamation. With a contemptuous smile, he offers himself to death and the moon.
The sea freezes in that instant, an inverted glacier suspended beneath the full moon. Everything falls silent, and peace returns to his kingdom.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98636_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Hard Astral Reign 3-10"
  },
  CollectionHall_98636_Title = {
    Text = "Full Moon Sacrifice"
  },
  CollectionHall_98637_Desc = {
    Text = "To cook the deceased is a solemn art.\nWith dining knife and spatula, he inquires about unfinished last words; with water and fire, he fulfills final wishes.\nEvery memory—awkward, painful, bitter—will transform into a brilliant and fragrant dish, for people to taste and cherish."
  },
  CollectionHall_98637_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Astral Reign 3-11"
  },
  CollectionHall_98637_Title = {
    Text = "Lord of Necrovia"
  },
  CollectionHall_98638_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The infant screams, demands, rages.
It is the center of the universe. It is the statute of all becomings.
All within Its sight must serve, obey, or be consumed.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98638_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Hard Stage 6-10"
  },
  CollectionHall_98638_Title = {
    Text = "Birth of a God"
  },
  CollectionHall_98639_Desc = {
    Text = [[
When he collects each death, he doesn't swing his scythe heartlessly.
His hands were once warm, his heart gentle and full of compassion.
When he drinks in the sorrow of a soul, he weeps with it.
When he weighs deep-seated hatred, he delivers judgment in its stead.
He made a solemn vow in the name of the Lord of Necrovia: all who profane death will vanish into the icy, dense mist.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98639_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Astral Reign 3-11"
  },
  CollectionHall_98639_Title = {
    Text = "Pietatis Mortis"
  },
  CollectionHall_98640_Desc = {
    Text = "The sweet taste of flesh, the texture of tearing tendons—these are his most familiar and unforgettable memories.\nHe has long understood that the City of Necrovia endures because of its dead's sacrifice, not its living's power.\nAnother splash of crimson goes down his throat. He closes his eyes, carefully savoring each unique fragrance, imprinting the taste of every soul into his memory. In this way, his loved ones and his people achieve eternal life within his body.\nThey are promised to be together, forever."
  },
  CollectionHall_98640_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Hard Astral Reign 3-10"
  },
  CollectionHall_98640_Title = {
    Text = "Bloodied Promise"
  },
  CollectionHall_98641_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The Sacrificial Knife glimmers, hungry, under the moon.
She presses it to her own throat, not in surrender, but to prove her free will with the only way she knows.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98641_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Stage 6-15"
  },
  CollectionHall_98641_Title = {
    Text = "Cold Moonlight"
  },
  CollectionHall_98642_Desc = {
    Text = [[
He had taught his people to fight, to kill, to survive. But he never taught them to run. Not from greater numbers. Not from death itself.
So he would not run.
Let them try to take his head!
He knew: Power devours those who chase it. And he had long since made his peace with that.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98642_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Psyche Deepdive: \"The Fall of A Giant\""
  },
  CollectionHall_98642_Title = {
    Text = "I Fear No Grave"
  },
  CollectionHall_98643_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Crunch, crunch.
The newborn god grins, hungrily savoring Its believers' devotion, along with the believers themselves.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98643_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Stage 6-15"
  },
  CollectionHall_98643_Title = {
    Text = "First Feeding"
  },
  CollectionHall_98644_Desc = {
    Text = [[
His own people turned on him, a fallen warlord cast into exile. But the mightiest ruler in Philistine history, a giant of unbreakable will, answered them with slaughter.
Amid endless screams, his blade drank deep, carving his battle creed into broken corpses: tyrannical, ruthless, savage, brutal.
Mercy had no place here.
They were merely the necessary stepping stones on his path back to power.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98644_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Psyche Deepdive: \"The Fall of A Giant\""
  },
  CollectionHall_98644_Title = {
    Text = "Necessary Carnage"
  },
  CollectionHall_98645_Desc = {
    Text = [[
When Elton turns his back and leaves, for a moment, he is that boy again, staring at the horizon where sky meets the vast blue sea, a world big enough for every dream to come true.
But now he knows the shape of dreams fulfilled. Now he carries a map back to that land of white birds.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98645_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Hard Stage 6-10"
  },
  CollectionHall_98645_Title = {Text = "Homeland"},
  CollectionHall_98646_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The time has come, the silver moon hangs high.
Quickly, let your cold toes rise and dance; tonight we celebrate this banquet.
She has reached the end of her journey, and we offer her a funeral with our stomachs.
A bite for you, a bite for me; from now on, she lives forever in our memories.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98646_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Astral Reign 3-11"
  },
  CollectionHall_98646_Title = {
    Text = "Requiem's Rhythm"
  },
  CollectionHall_98647_Desc = {
    Text = [[
If miracles had a shape, they would be the curve of her fingers clasped in prayer.
If the divine ever wore a face, it would be hers: serene as a still lake to drown in.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98647_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Stage 6-15"
  },
  CollectionHall_98647_Title = {
    Text = "Blessed Maiden"
  },
  CollectionHall_98648_Desc = {
    Text = "\"Celebrate, my friend♪\nThe bones beneath the moon hum a rotting tune♪\nA beloved lies still on the silver plate♪\nAll guests have arrived♪Sing! Dance! Now we consecrate!♪\nNever mourn the corpses♪Never pray for the dead♪\nHer memories in my hands♪her tears in my teeth♪\nLet us swallow her soul, her flesh so sweet ♪\nIn our deathly banquet, where loved ones meet♪\""
  },
  CollectionHall_98648_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Astral Reign 3-11"
  },
  CollectionHall_98648_Title = {
    Text = "Song of the Ghouls"
  },
  CollectionHall_98649_Desc = {
    Text = "They feared his strength. Worshipped it.\nThey hated his cruelty. Cursed his name.\nAnd when he fell, they crowned him failure, Just another exile to be erased from history.\nBut the clamor of cowards means nothing. The giant's gaze lingers only on power.\nNow, exiled to a wasteland of forgotten tides, he gambles his last breath—not for vengeance, not for glory, but for the one thing worth bleeding for: dominion absolute."
  },
  CollectionHall_98649_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Psyche Deepdive: \"The Fall of A Giant\""
  },
  CollectionHall_98649_Title = {
    Text = "The Reckoning"
  },
  CollectionHall_98650_Desc = {
    Text = "He remembers her.\nThe child he cradled in the storm, the one he gave to the Abyss—along with his conscience—in exchange for his dream of a homeland where white birds soar.\nNow the dream is real.\nNow the debt comes due."
  },
  CollectionHall_98650_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Stage 6-15"
  },
  CollectionHall_98650_Title = {Text = "Due Debt"},
  CollectionHall_98651_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Separation and death are this world's inescapable realities.
Though you've escaped countless sacrifices to walk an uncertain path, a faint sorrow lingers in your heart. But, having witnessed a people who live among their dead, and their king who weaves death into a gentle, everlasting embrace, you no longer fear the unknown.
A purple forget-me-not, a farewell gift from Doresain, drifts onto your shoulder.
You know now that no matter what, your journey home will not be a lonely one.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98651_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Hard Astral Reign 3-10"
  },
  CollectionHall_98651_Title = {
    Text = "Forget-Me-Not from Him"
  },
  CollectionHall_98652_Desc = {
    Text = "\"As your friend, your king, and the master of this eternal resting place, I implore you—awake! Return to the homeland you cherish! Banish these trespassers who disturb the peace of our kin, forever!\""
  },
  CollectionHall_98652_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Astral Reign 3-11"
  },
  CollectionHall_98652_Title = {
    Text = "Wrath of the Spirits"
  },
  CollectionHall_98653_Desc = {
    Text = "She and It could not coexist. With a dagger, she drove her no into their twin hearts, an answer etched in blood."
  },
  CollectionHall_98653_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Stage 6-15"
  },
  CollectionHall_98653_Title = {
    Text = "Day of Divine Parturition"
  },
  CollectionHall_98654_Desc = {
    Text = [[
You never imagined your conversation with the ghoul king would begin with a dance.
A forceful advance, a lingering probe, offense and defense, confrontation and yielding... You engaged in a secret duel within the swirls of your garments.
The transaction ended elegantly with the final bow. His long lavender-colored hair fell softly, and you saw a gleeful smile sparkling in his misty eyes.
Wait, were you just played?]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98654_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Astral Reign 3-11"
  },
  CollectionHall_98654_Title = {
    Text = "Tango de Salon"
  },
  CollectionHall_98655_Desc = {
    Text = "The most horrifying and profane feast you've ever witnessed was, for them, the most tender of reunions."
  },
  CollectionHall_98655_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Astral Reign 3-11"
  },
  CollectionHall_98655_Title = {
    Text = "Sanctuary of Final Repose"
  },
  CollectionHall_98656_Desc = {
    Text = "The stars do not care. They keep their indifferent orbits, while the lives below crumble to dust, rise, and crumble again."
  },
  CollectionHall_98656_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Stage 6-15"
  },
  CollectionHall_98656_Title = {
    Text = "Twisted Stars"
  },
  CollectionHall_98657_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Others heard the deadly witch's whisper and fell to their knees. They begged. They worshipped.
Not him. Never.
He saw that power and hungered for it. Not as a supplicant, but as a conqueror. He would take it, no matter the cost.
And when he did, he would rise again... Until his name thundered across every land the Philistines had ever claimed.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_98657_LockTip = {
    Text = "Complete Psyche Deepdive: \"The Fall of A Giant\" (Hard)"
  },
  CollectionHall_98657_Title = {
    Text = "The Titan's Ambition"
  },
  CollectionHall_99651_Desc = {
    Text = "<Bold:Silver Cod 24>\nEvery time I pass that fish and chips restaurant, I can't help but want to scream.\nWhy is it always the silver cod that suffers? We're not even real cod!\nIs it our fault that our flesh is firm and delicious?\n\n<Bold:Cat 24>\nSlurp slurp... meow, meow (indeed, indeed)!\n\n<Bold:Silver Cod 24>\nIn the Leonian Kingdom, a silver cod dies every minute to become a human meal.\nYes, as we speak, 10 silver cod have already perished.\nTen in total! Father above, do you hear their cries?\n\n<Bold:Cat 24>\nUh... meow? Meow meow, meow meow (where is it)?\n\n<Bold:Silver Cod 24>\nIt's just a metaphor, silly. You may be a bit dim, but you have a heart of gold, overcoming the base instincts and shortsightedness of a cat.\nListen, I have a plan. I need your help to make it happen...\n\n—Excerpt from \"Explosion at Big John's Fish and Chips: Case Summary Testimony B-03.\" Due to overcrowding at Bethlehem Mental Hospital, the suspect was rejected and held in Londinium Tower for 23 days before being released."
  },
  CollectionHall_99651_Title = {
    Text = "Silver Cod's Determination"
  },
  CollectionHall_99653_Desc = {
    Text = "To await \"that moment,\" the girl slept at the bottom of the glacier.\n\nThe deep ice of Elworth froze her body, but it failed to seal away her consciousness.\n\nThat wisp of consciousness belonged to a child—and a mother.\n\nWithin the dark womb of His daughter, the god dreamed an endless dream.\n\nOver those twenty-five years, did she ever think, yearn, or hope for anything?\n\nNo one can answer these questions now.\n\nAs for the girl herself... will she open her heart to those around her?\n\nOnly time and the future will tell."
  },
  CollectionHall_99653_Title = {
    Text = "Slumber Beneath the Glacier"
  },
  CollectionHall_99654_Desc = {
    Text = "Only the quietly dying are worth savoring. The living struggle, and struggle makes the taste bitter.\nWhen the platter arrives, the heart at its center is still faintly warm, its surface rising slightly as if mid-beat. Two eyes gaze up from the side, their pupils boiled docile—milky white, preserving a final instant of shock.\nHe lifts the knife, then pauses.\nThe soul inside still screams. A poet's heart, steeped in sickness and relief, yet tangled with one last regret. He sets the blade down. Folds his hands. Listens.\nTo truly honor this dish, he must wait.\nWait for the obsession in the meat to unravel. Wait for the poet's last memories to soften into aroma—ink and herbs, a lover's trembling breath, the shyness of dawn.\nHe inhales deeply. The air hums with stories.\nUnder the whispering tree, he sits, patient as a grave. The fruit will fall when it is ripe."
  },
  CollectionHall_99654_Title = {
    Text = "Macabre Delicacies"
  },
  CollectionHall_99655_Desc = {
    Text = [[
A bouquet that has withered and dried from being left for too long.

It will never see its master return.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_99655_Title = {
    Text = "Unsent Flowers"
  },
  CollectionHall_99656_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Since their birth, the twins have not been allowed to freely fly with their wings.
The second pair of arms growing on their backs resembles two ceremonial vessels displaying the majesty of the Son, always mandated to maintain a certain posture.
In childhood, Pollux was the most protective of those wings among the two, daily grooming and applying essential oils to keep those feathers shining like satin.
He always took advantage of brief moments of solitude to secretly flap those newly flourishing wings, wobbling off the ground in Castor's astonishment, reaching out to touch the embellished dome above.
Compared to how Pollux could make his wings dance in various agile poses, Castor often felt that his wings were as clumsy as two wooden planks.
During their secret time after going to bed each day, Castor quietly watched Pollux leap and spin in the dark, imitating flight within the small confines.
"My brother's wings are so beautiful, but as for me, I might never learn to fly," Castor thought.
So it was on the night of their escape that Castor first felt the coolness and ease of the evening breeze lifting his wings.
The more skilled Pollux tightly held onto his clumsily flying brother, laughing joyously in the sky, drawing arcs of dive and spin like a real bird of the sky.
Castor turned his head to see the moonlight gilding Pollux' long and powerful wings, reflecting a dazzling bluish-green halo among the feathers.
"That must be the most beautiful thing in the world; no matter what happens, I will protect Pollux and safeguard those wings."
Soon, the harsh wilderness life left Pollux's wings injured by beasts.
Castor, heartbroken, picked up the fallen feathers of Pollux and tucked them into his bosom, silently vowing that such a thing would not happen again.
But what he did not know was that this solitary feather would later become his most treasured possession, the last relic he would hold onto about those wings.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_99656_Title = {
    Text = "Lone Feather"
  },
  CollectionHall_99657_Desc = {
    Text = "Toot—Toot—\nAs the sound of the horn echoed, the cruise ship safely docked under the guidance of Corposant.\nPassengers laughed as they descended the gangway, tipping their hats to thank her, while sailors rushed over to express their praise.\n\"Well done, Corposant. If it weren't for your early warning, we would have been swallowed by the storm.\"\n\"Yeah, thanks to your correct guidance, we didn't get lost in the sea!\"\nThe sailors laughed, patted her shoulder, and gave her a thumbs-up.\nIn fact, Corposant could never adapt to such close social interactions; her rigid and rational mind had no thoughts beyond \"work\" and \"duty.\"\nSo, she could only attribute this to a part of \"work\" and \"duty.\"\n\"I was just doing my job. As a helmsman, my duty is to guide you safely home.\"\nA polite but dull response, yet the sailors who knew her well laughed heartily, bidding her farewell, singing sea shanties, and leaving the harbor with arms over each other.\n\"The Nautilus can finally set sail. Depart, Nautilus.\"\nThe singing gradually faded away, while Corposant remained on the shore, preparing for the future voyage.\nThe sea is unpredictable, no helmsman can guarantee victory every time; she cannot either. But she is willing to spend countless hours to increase even the slightest odds of success.\nChecking, patrolling, learning, verifying, it seems that \"work\" is the only thing left in her life.\nYet she is willing because all of this is for that moment, the successful helmsmanship, leading everyone home safely."
  },
  CollectionHall_99657_Title = {
    Text = "Navigator at Sea"
  },
  CollectionHall_99658_Desc = {
    Text = [[
In the endless abyss, the Azure Throne stands sentinel,
The sky hangs low, the stars tremble, and all creation is silent.

Ancient and mysterious entities have been utterly annihilated,
Yet across generations, mortals chant their hymns in dreams.
The abyssal waters and secrets long sealed in dust,
Your whispers surge like a tide, drowning the ravines of the soul.

In that boundless dreamscape, the Prophet and the Madman walk together,
In pursuit of the intangible spirit, fear and reverence intertwined.
The path entangled with dark algae, like a destiny being spun,
Gradually drawing the hearts of the lost toward that Azure Throne.
Ah, the universe's absurdity and its truth,
Where dream and reality intersect, an eternal brilliance flickers.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_99658_Title = {
    Text = "Blue Stone Throne"
  },
  CollectionHall_99660_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Everyone wants to defy fate but fears it.
The brave roar for battle, the cowardly whisper in submission, yet only he uncovered the secret to overcoming fate.
He constantly invites fate to gamble, urging it to deal another round.
He never feared fate, believing he would never lose.
He never questioned what was at stake, wagering everything, even his life.
With a roulette gun, he intimidated countless opponents and became Londinium's infamous gambling madman.
How lonely it is without a worthy opponent.
Until he met that man.
He defeated countless mortals and finally took a seat at fate's table.
He quickly lost everything, then regained it all with interest.
Upon being reborn as a beast, he found the gun that had fired its last bullet.
He reloaded it, pulled the trigger on himself once more.
In silence, he grinned.
He hadn't lost yet, believing that one day he would win in the end.
Even if it meant betting everything.]]
  },
  CollectionHall_99660_Title = {
    Text = "Fate Roulette"
  },
  CollectionHall_99663_Desc = {
    Text = "The mysterious lady approached her after the funeral.\n\n\"Poor child,\" she said, \"you shouldn't have had to go through this.\"\n\n\"Don't you know? After he caused Millie's death, Thompson went after him.\n\nThat scum Edward should have died last year, but someone saved him.\"\n\n\"Why? Oh, how should I know? Maybe they're two of a kind, or maybe... the 'saint' himself didn't realize his own sin.\nWhat was his line again? Ah yes, forgiveness. Forgiveness for sinners, for the crimes they commit.\"\n\n\"He believes everyone deserves a second chance. What do you think?\nShould we give Edward another chance, after he took Millie, your sister, and your mother?\"\n\n\"Exactly. People like him never change. So, you know what to do, right?\"\n\nShe was right. Such people never change.\nTo end these people, to end this evil, this tragedy, the only way is...\n\nTo expose their desires, lay bare their ugliness, let them tear each other apart, purge them completely—\nand welcome a land without sin."
  },
  CollectionHall_99663_Title = {
    Text = "Man in the Mirror"
  },
  CollectionHall_99666_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Vast flocks of sheep wander over vast grasslands.
There are many, many sheep in this world, and sheep are born to be led by a shepherd.
She has always been the prophet of this world, holding the staff of Knowledge.
She has always been a good shepherd, determined to lead the flock on the right path.
She disciplines the lambs with that staff, drives away the wolves with that staff.
She raises the shepherd's staff high, for she can always foresee the road ahead.
Once she led the flock to abundant water, to fresh pasture.
Now she sees the truth of the world, so she leads the flock into the ultimate embrace.
This way; don't look back.
She smiles, waving her staff of wisdom.
So the sheep cannot see the cliff ahead.
One by one.
The sheep fall, the shepherd sings.
Follow the selfless shepherd, for she has shown you the truest path.
Do not fear, even though you walk through the valley of the shadow of death, her staff is still with you.
