  CollectionHall_99671_Desc = {
    Text = "The reborn Clementine is like a naive larva, traveling through the human world, wandering in the prosperous world that does not belong to her race, feeling perplexed and confused.\nUntil that enlightening voice rings out—\n\"Excuse me, are you Doctor Charlotte? I came to seek psychological counseling from Doctor Charlotte...\"\nClementine finally comes to her senses. She doesn't care who Charlotte is; she is simply curious about the new term that the visitor spoke: \"psychological counseling\".\nBut she is a mature hunter and will never reveal her ignorance, so she smiled, as if she were Charlotte, the savior spoken of by the visitor.\nTears, torment, helplessness, no need to provoke; the visitor has already squeezed out the pain from the depths of her soul.\nBefore leaving, the visitor looked at Clementine with a relaxed expression and sighed, \"Thank you for being willing to listen. I feel so much better.\"\nThen came the sound of the door closing, along with Clementine's laughter, as she tasted the sweetness for the first time.\nThis laughter started softly, like that of a larva's buzzing, and then grew louder, as if it was the screech of an adult insect.\nAnd in this laughter, the insectoid named Clementine swiftly matured.\nEverything that followed fell into place. She became a psychologist, carrying a smile and a pendulum, diving deep into each patient's heart.\nShe continues to walk through the world of humans, still not belonging to this prosperous world, but no longer confused and perplexed.\nFor the entire human world is her hypnotic hunting ground."
